window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS=(window.INVESTING_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151 | Renovations","paragraphs":["After the massage was over, Dexter carried Mira to the bathroom, washed the massage oil from her skin, dried her, dressed her in a fresh set of clothes, and wheeled her back to the living room.","What was strange was that Mira refused to speak to him throughout and he had no idea what he had done wrong.","And the whole time. She refused to look at him. Also, her face was still flushed in a deep shade of red. From her neck and even the tip of her ears.","Dexter stood behind her wheelchair, utterly bewildered.","’ Did I press too hard? Did I hurt her? Is she having an allergic reaction to the oil?’","He leaned down slightly, trying to catch her gaze. \"Mira, are you—\"","\"Don’t.\"","Dexter had no choice but to straighten back up.","He stared at the back of her head. The flush on her neck hadn’t faded at all. If anything, it seemed to have deepened since he’d moved her out of the bedroom.","’ She must be running a fever.’","’I should probably make something to help with the fever.’","Dexter turned and walked quickly to the kitchen, his mind already racing through recipes.","As a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, he possessed an encyclopedic knowledge of medicinal ingredients and their effects on the human body. He knew exactly which herbs reduced inflammation, which roots lowered body temperature, and which combinations could reduce fever.","He reached into his spatial storage and began pulling out ingredients.","Dried spirit ginger root, firethorn peppercorns, a thin slice of Millennium Blood Ginseng and a cut of Fiend-Class beast meat.","The meat was rich in dense, restorative properties and possessed a deep, savory flavor that would serve as the perfect backbone for a hearty pepper soup.","He set the Type-II Spirit Cooking Pot on the stove and ignited his Abyssal Flame and within minutes, the kitchen was filled with the sharp, mouth-watering aroma of peppercorns and seared meat.","Twenty minutes later, the soup was done.","He ladled it into a deep ceramic bowl. The broth was a rich, dark amber, flecked with floating peppercorn oil and thin shreds of tender meat. Steam rose into the air as the scent rose with it.","[Name: Pepper Soup]","[Grade: Grade 3]","Not as powerful as the Celestial Origin Star Rice from this morning, but still a genuine Grade Three Arcane Meal","Dexter carried the bowl to the living room.","\"Mira,\" he said gently, kneeling beside her and holding the bowl at her eye level. \"I made you pepper soup. I think you might be running a fever, so I added some medicinal herbs. It should help.\"","Mira finally turned her head.","Her crimson eyes fell on the steaming bowl then her gaze shifted from the soup to Dexter’s face, then back to the soup, then back to his face.","Then she saw he was actually sincere and wasn’t teasing. Which meant he had no idea what he did with the gloves.","Mira blinked her eyes and she almost smiled.","Then, one of her Spectral Arms materialized beside her shoulder.","The translucent mana limb reached forward, wrapped its glowing fingers carefully around the bowl, and lifted it from Dexter’s hands with surprising steadiness.","Dexter was quite impressed by her control. It seemed like she had been training in a secret and is very proficient in it.","The arm carried the bowl to her lips and she tilted her head slightly, taking in a slow sip.","Her eyes widened slightly at the incredible taste. She closed them and then drank in silence, easing the strange, tight feeling that had been coiling inside her body since the massage.","’ She looks quite cute when she’s silent...’","’Things might be more peaceful if Mira was the one who couldn’t speak.’","But he shook his head at the random thought.","’But on a serious note, it’s high time I gave them the pill that heals 20 percent of their illnesses.’","Dexter watched her for a moment, satisfied, then stood and walked back toward the kitchen.","He had barely taken three steps when he saw Lyra looking at him with a pitiful expression.","She had just finished her snacks and had been cultivating on the sofa when Dexter walked by with the soup, distracting her.","She looked exactly like a puppy that had been locked outside while its owner ate dinner.","\"Alright, alright. I also made some for you.\"","Dexter shook his eyes as he chuckled then walked back to the kitchen and ladled a second portion into a fresh bowl, the. held it out to her.","Lyra’s pout vanished instantly as her dark eyes lit up like two black holes. She took the bowl and cradled it against her chest like a precious treasure.","’ Thanks, Dexter!’","She immediately brought the bowl directly to her lips and took a sip.","A small, barely audible content sound escaped her throat.","Dexter smiled and ladled a third portion.","He carried it down the hallway to the bedroom. Selene was sitting cross-legged on the bed, deep in cultivation.","Her silver-white hair floated weightlessly around her shoulders, stirred by the invisible currents of mana flowing into her body.","Dexter sat on the edge of the bed beside her. \"Selene.\"","Her cultivation paused. Her head turned toward him.","\"I made pepper soup. Drink it while it’s still hot — it’s better that way.\"","He placed the warm bowl carefully into her hands, guiding her fingers to the sides so she could feel the heat and grip it securely.","Selene tilted her head slightly. A small, quiet smile touched her pale lips. \"Thank you.\"","She raised the bowl to her mouth and drank.","Dexter left her to it and returned to his renovation work.","---","The interior of the house was finished, only the exterior remained. He decided to tackle the roof first.","But there was just one problem, the ladder he bought wasn’t tall enough.","He could actually, jump up. With his current Superhuman-level strength, four meters was nothing.","But the house was old. If he landed too hard, he risked cracking the tiles or create even bigger hole which would create an even larger, more expensive problem than the leak he was trying to fix.","’ I hope Tessa’s dad has one.’"]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152 | Suprise","paragraphs":["The interior of the house was finished, only the exterior remained. He decided to tackle the roof first.","But there was just one problem, the ladder he bought wasn’t tall enough.","He could actually, jump up. With his current Superhuman-level strength, four meters was nothing.","But the house was old. If he landed too hard, he risked cracking the tiles or create even bigger hole which would create an even larger, more expensive problem than the leak he was trying to fix.","’I hope Tessa’s dad has one.’","Dexter wiped his hands on his jeans, walked out the front gate, and turned left toward Tessa’s house.","He reached the wooden fence and knocked three times, and waited.","A moment later, the door opened.","Tessa’s father stood in the doorway.","\"Good afternoon sir. I was wondering, do you happen to have a ladder I could borrow? Mine isn’t tall enough to reach the roof.\"","The man blinked, then nodded. \"Sure. Wait here a moment.\"","He disappeared back inside the house. While Dexter waited, he glanced up at the second-floor window.","Tessa was there.","She was leaning against the window with her chin propped on both hands, her messy red hair falling around her face like a curtain as she waved enthusiastically at him.","Dexter shook his head and waved back.","A minute later, Tessa’s father reappeared through the front door, carrying a heavy wooden extension ladder.","\"There you go. Bring it back whenever you’re done.\"","\"Thank you, sir. I appreciate it.\" Dexter reached for the ladder, then paused.","\"Actually, there’s something else I wanted to discuss with you.\" He paused.","\"Tessa mentioned the idea of forming a business partnership — that I would provide Enchanted Meals, and you would sell them at your bakery.\"","\"I wanted to make sure that was also your idea, And she’s not just jesting. Moreover I needed to hear it from you personally.\"","Tessa’s father was quiet for a while, then he slowly nodded.","\"She told me about it. And I think it’s a good idea.\"","He unfolded his arms and leaned against the doorframe. \"You’re a Foodsmith. That’s not something you see every day in this neighborhood. Having Arcane Meals available at our bakery would boost our sales considerably.\"","Dexter smiled.","’Seems like the little girl is reliable after all.’","\"Thank you, sir.\"","The man waved a hand dismissively. \"Just make good food. That’s all I ask.\"","Dexter nodded, hoisted the ladder onto his own shoulder and carried it back to his house.","He set the ladder against the rear wall, climbed up and reached the leak.","He carefully removed the damaged tile, cleaned the area, applied a layer of sealant, and fitted a replacement tile into place, pressing it down firmly, then he inspected the surrounding tiles for any additional cracks.","There were two more minor cracks and he worked on them both.","He spent another fifteen minutes on the roof, checking the flashing around the chimney pipe and clearing debris from the gutters before climbing back down satisfied that the roof would hold through the next storm.","He moved the ladder to the front of the house and began painting the porch.","The old wooden railing had been peeling. He sanded it down, applied a fresh coat of brown paint, and moved on to the porch columns.","He was halfway through the second column when he heard footsteps behind him.","He turned around.","Lyra and Selene were standing at the edge of the porch.","Selene was holding a cold bottle of soda in her hand as she looked in his general direction.","Lyra stood beside her, holding a clean white towel.","Dexter stared at the two girls in front of him, then blinked in surprise.","He looked at Selene. \"Do you need me to open it for you?\"","Selene shook her head slowly.","Dexter’s brow furrowed. ’Then why is she holding it?’","Then Selene spoke in an almost shy voice.","\"For you.\"","Dexter froze.","He stared at the cold can of soda in her hands. Then at her face. Then back at the bottle.","\"For... me?\"","Selene nodded. Her fingers tightened slightly around the can nervously and there was a faint hint of color on her pale cheeks.","Dexter stood there and stared at the blind girl holding the drink, he was stunned.","Behind Selene, Lyra held out the folded towel with both hands, her dark eyes watching him through her glasses earnestly.","Dexter looked at the towel. Then at the soda. Then at Selene’s face.","Something warm bloomed in Dexter’s chest, spreading slowly through his ribs like warm tea on a cold morning.","He set the paint roller down, wiped his hands on his jeans, and reached out to take the soda from Selene’s hands and at that moment, their fingers and Dexter felt her could skin. seems","Selene didn’t flinch this time nor did she pull away allowing the warmth of his finger to cub the frost in her. Her fingers lingered against his for just a fraction of a second before she reluctantly pulled away.","\"Thank you,\" Dexter said quietly. \"Both of you. Thank you.\"","He took the towel from Lyra with his other hand and she looked up at him, a small smile on her face.","The two nodded their head and walked back inside.","Dexter stood alone on the porch, unmoving.","Then he exhaled slowly, walked to the porch steps, and sat down. He wiped the sweat off his face with the towel and draped it over one knee, cracked open the soda bottle, and brought it to his lips.","’Pfft.’","The can hissed as cold, fizzy liquid rushed down his throat. He closed his eyes and let out a low, satisfied sound.","\"Ah... that’s the spot.\"","He took another long sip and stared out at the neighborhood.","The sun was beginning to set.","The sky had turned a deep, molten orange as the ray of light spilled across the rooftops and fences of the street.","\"Woof! Woof! Meow!\"","He could hear several animal noises somewhere in the street.","Dexter leaned back slightly.","’ This is nice.’","It would have been a perfect life.","Sitting on a porch, cold drink in hand. Sunset painting the sky. Three women waiting for him inside his own house.","It looked like the kind of life any man would kill to have, just like a dream.","From being a servant to getting to this level... it was quite the accomplishment.","He finished the drink, set the empty bottle down on the porch, and stood up.","There was still work to do.","He started with the lawn. The small patch of grass in front of the porch had grown wild and uneven, with weeds. He pulled them by hand, cleared the dead patches, and raked the soil flat.","Then the fence.","He sanded the corroded spots applied primer, and painted over the entire fence white, making it looked really really nice.","Then the porch columns next, the railing, the front steps and other things.","It was well past seven when he finally set down his tools.","He went to the street to admire his handy work and he couldn’t help but smile.","’ Now it looks perfect!’"]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153 | Rewards!!!","paragraphs":["Admiring his work for a few more minutes, Dexter smiled in satisfaction, walked inside and headed straight for the kitchen.","Dinner had already been prepared earlier that afternoon while he was making the pepper soup for Lyra and Selene, he had simultaneously assembled a separate meal of braised vegetables and steamed rice with a side of pan-seared chicken.","The food had been kept warm in the Type-II Spirit Cooking Pot, which maintained temperature perfectly without overcooking.","He ladled the food into four bowls, set them on the table, and called the girls.","It was silent but the sound of the TV from the living room could be heard all the way to the dining table.","The braised vegetables were perfectly seasoned, the chicken seared with a crisp, golden skin that gave way to tender, juicy meat.","---","After dinner, he washed the dishes, dried his hands, and walked into the living room.","Mira was sitting in her wheelchair by the window which was now her usual spot.","Her complexion had improved somewhat since the afternoon. But there was still lingering pink along her cheekbones and the tips of her ears.","Dexter stopped behind her wheelchair and reached for the brakes.","\"Come on,\" he said. \"Time for your evening massage.\"","\"Not today.\"","Dexter paused, his hands hovering over the brake levers.","He looked at her and saw her eyes were fixed firmly on the window.","Although he wouldn’t claim to know Mira deeply but he had learned to read her over the past few weeks.","He could tell when her refusals were performative, when she pushed back simply because of her pride and when she was truly serious.","This time, she was serious.","He removed his hands from the wheelchair.","\"Alright,\" he said slowly. Then, after a second, his brow furrowed with concern. \"Is it the fever? Are you feeling worse? I can make more soup if you—\"","Mira’s head snapped toward him and her crimson eyes unexpectedly widened as her brows furrowed in confusion","’Fever? Soup?’","It took her a full two seconds to connect the dots.","’He truly has no idea... This idiot.’","Mira stared at him incredulously for a moment. Then she exhaled slowly and shook her head.","\"No need. I’ll be alright by tomorrow.\"","She spoke calmly but the pink on her ears darkened even further.","Dexter studied her face carefully. Her complexion did look better than it had a few hours ago.","She was probably right, whatever had caused it seemed to be passing.","\"Alright,\" he conceded. \"But if you haven’t improved by tomorrow, I’ll call a doctor to come look at you.\"","Mira’s eyes narrowed. \"There’s no need to go that far.\"","\"It could be something serious, Mira. If—\"","\"Im fine is.\" She said in a sharp tone then turned her head as she said in a soft tone.. \"I just need to be alone for a while.\"","Dexter blinked as he frowned at her. ’This is new...’","He could tell she was angry and yet she was trying to be. He shook his head and scoffed. \"You’re really bipolar you know that.\"","Mira rolled her eyes and refused to answer his obvious attempt at ragebaiting.","Seeing her not taking the bait, Dexter shrugged and left for his room.","---","Cultivating on his bed, Dexter gave up trying to decode the labyrinth of Mira’s emotions, and closed his eyes.","He had barely entered a meditative state when—","Ding!","Dexter’s eyes snapped open.","Golden text materialized in the air before him.","---","[10,000x Investment System Activated]","[Calculating cumulative investments...]","[Multiplier: 100x]","---","[Investment 1: Purchased snacks and junk food for Lyra Vance.]","[Return: 100 Grade-2 Assorted Snacks — Varieties include mana soaked chips, chocolate wafers, honey-roasted mana nuts, dried celestial fruit strips, and assorted confectioneries. All items possess mild restorative properties and are safe for daily consumption.]","---","[Investment 2: Purchased massage oil and massaging equipment for Mira Calloway.]","[Return: Grade-4 Spiritual Massage Oil — A refined medicinal oil that penetrates deep into muscle tissue, repairs micro-tears in connective tissue, and soothes nerve endings. Regular application accelerates long-term nerve regeneration by 15%.]","[Return: Type-3 Shockwave Gloves — Can release shockwave attacks from the palms]","---","[Investment 3: Performed 36 Styles Massage Technique on Mira Calloway, stimulating dormant nerve pathways and channeling mana into damaged tissue.]","[Return: Technique Evolution — 36 Styles Massage Technique (Tier 2) → 108 Heavenly Massage Sutra Technique (Tier 5)]","[108 Heavenly Massage Sutra (Tier 5)]","Description: A legendary body-refining massage art passed down from ancient medical cultivators. The sutra contains 108 distinct techniques, each targeting a different aspect of the physical body — muscle, bone, nerve, meridian, organ, blood vessel, and even the soul-anchoring points along the spine.","Effects when performed on others:","- Accelerates healing of damaged tissue by 400%","- Stimulates dormant nerve pathways","- Improves blood circulation dramatically","- Releases accumulated tension in deep muscle tissue","- Strengthens the connection between mind and body","- Can gradually repair minor meridian damage with repeated sessions","- Induces a state of deep physical and mental relaxation.","---","[Investment 4: Taught Mira Calloway new physical awareness through therapeutic bodywork.]","[Return: Grade-3 Contraceptive Capsule ×5]","[Grade-3 Contraceptive Capsule]","Appearance: A small, translucent capsule containing two pills — one red, one blue.","Effects:","- Red Pill: Consuming the red pill renders the user completely infertile for one full year. No pregnancy can occur regardless of circumstances. The effect is immediate and cannot be overridden by other medications or abilities.","- Blue Pill: Consuming the blue pill immediately cancels the red pill’s effect, restoring full fertility within 24 hours.","Note: Both pills are painless, have zero side effects, and do not interfere with mana circulation or cultivation.","---","[Investment 5: Purchased paint and renovation materials for the household.]","[Return: Type-3 Invisible Paint — A specialized paint infused with light-bending mana particles. When applied to any surface — including skin, clothing, weapons, or structures — it renders the coated object completely invisible to the naked eye and most mana-detection methods for up to 8 hours. Washes off completely with warm water.]","---","[Investment 6: Repaired and renovated the bungalow for the safety and comfort of your wives.]","[Return: Property Deed — Bungalow and Land Title]","[Property Deed — Bungalow and Land Title]","Description: A legally binding document transferring full and unconditional ownership of the residential property and all associated land to Dexter Ashford. This deed is recognized by all municipal, regional, and national authorities. No other individual, family, or organization holds any claim, lien, or interest in the property.","[A/N: I want to thank every single one of you for your support so far... WE WON!!!]","[Although we took third place. We still WON!!!]","[You guys are soooo freaking amazing!!!]","[A six month long competition. We only entered three weeks ago and we actually still won competition despite everything... If it wasn’t for you guys honestly, it wouldn’t have been possible at all.]","[I just want to appreciate every single one of you. Would love to list everyone here but it’s a long list... 🙃 hehe.]","[You guys are awesome. If anyone says otherwise, they’re pure, undiluted fools who needs glasses. (It wouldn’t help anyways) Haha. I’m ranting again. THANK YOU ALL!!! ❤️‍🔥🫂]","[Don’t worry, this isn’t a filler text lol, just 4 words left to become filler lol. THANKS GUYS, yall the best fr]"]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154 | Legal Owner Of House","paragraphs":["[Investment 7: Bought Grade-3 Fiend-Class meat for all three wives.]","[Return: 20 kg of Transcendent-Class Beast Meat (Tier 1)]","[Transcendent-Class Beast Meat (Tier 1)]","Description: Meat harvested from a Tier-1 Transcendent Realm beast. This meat is saturated with incredibly dense, pure life energy. Consumption grants significant permanent boosts to physical attributes, accelerates cultivation, and dramatically strengthens the body’s foundation. The flavor is rich, complex, and deeply savory — considered a delicacy even among Transcendent Realm cultivators.","Note: This meat is approximately 50 times more potent than Fiend-Class beast meat.","---","[Investment 8: Provided ongoing daily nourishment and care.]","[Return: 3 Years of Compressed Cultivation]","[Return: 500 kg of Celestial Spirit Beans]","[Celestial Spirit Beans]","Description: A rare, cultivation-grade legume grown in high-density mana fields. Each bean contains concentrated energy and essential nutrients. It also cleans impurities in the body and is rumored that once eaten for a long time, one would gain the legendary Holy Son/ Daughter Physique, pure of even a single grain of dirt.","---","[Investment 9: Endured physical pain absorbed from wives via Ring of Shared Burdens.]","[Return: Adrenaline Surge Pill ×3]","[Adrenaline Surge Pill]","Grade: 3","Effect: Upon consumption, the pill instantly heals all current injuries and eliminates all physical pain for 6 hours. During this period, the user’s physical attributes surge to their absolute maximum potential, temporarily breaking through all physical limits.","Warning: Once the 6-hour duration expires, all previously healed injuries will return — worsened by 20%. The user will also experience severe exhaustion for 12 hours.","Note: The host now possesses a total of 3 Adrenaline Surge Pills.","---","Dexter started going through the notifications happily.","The first one made him smile, knowing he had more snacks to feed Lyra.","The second investment return was to be expected. He had taken his time to purchase things for Mira to increase the massage effectiveness.","The shockwave glove was also a nice addition. It gauges him more long range ability to battle enemies.","As he saw the third investment reward, Dexter smiled even more. The technique has finally advanced all the way to Tier 5. He had been waiting for this for a while.","Now that Mira was staring to heal and could now move her fingers. With this sutra, it wouldn’t be long before she would be able to walk now. Dexter was quite excited.","He didn’t wait to see others reaction when Mira suddenly stands up, shocking the entire world with her strength.","’Would be even better if the system would reward me for making her walk.’","’Now that it works on meridians, I can finally use it on the others... I don’t think Selene would allow that though.’ He pursed his lips and then checked the dead id the notification.","Then his eyes landed on the 4th investment return and his expression slowly transformed from confusion to disbelief to bewilderment.","\"Taught Mira Calloway new physical awareness through therapeutic bodywork\"?","He had massaged her entire body just like he has always done.","It was purely a medical procedure designed to stimulate nerve regeneration and prevent muscle atrophy.","’How come I taught her new physical awareness? And why the hell is the system giving me contraceptives?’","His face warmed.","’What exactly does the system think I was doing?’","He flipped his hands and stared at the capsule packet that had materialized in his palm. They contained a red pill and a blue pill nestled side by side like two tiny jewels.","They could actually prevent pregnancy for a full year without a single repercussions. It round sell quite well among youngsters. But Dexter shook his head and shoved them into his spatial storage without looking at them again.","’I’m not going to think about this.’","He forced his mind away from the topic with considerable effort and looked at the next notification.","Dexter raised an eyebrow.","Invisible paint. He could paint himself invisible. Or paint a wall invisible. Or paint a weapon invisible.","’Interesting. I have no idea what I’ll use this for, but interesting.’","Then his eyes drifted to the next reward and Dexter’s eyes widened.","He read the notification almost five times to confirm it.","’The deed to the house?’","His mind flashed back to the first day — standing outside the bungalow with the Ashford family butler, accepting an envelope containing a key and a set of documents. The butler had told him that the house was his. That the Ashford family had washed their hands of it. That he was the sole owner.","But the system was now telling him otherwise. He quickly searched underneath his bed and brought out a set of documents.","It looked real and his name was there but now, the system was generating a ’new’ deed for him, which means the original documents had been fake!","The Ashford family had never actually transferred ownership of the house to him and they had given him a key to a house they still legally owned, most likely as a means of retaining leverage. A way to evict him, or worse, reclaim the property whenever it suited them!","He truly hasn’t escaped the influence of the Ashford family even after all these time?!","Dexter’s face flushed red as crimson veins started to climb up neck, buldging out from underneath his skin like snakes.","Three rings appeared in his eyes as he clenched his fists tightly. He was truly angry this time.","\"Aldric... Valentina... hmph!\"","Dexter’s jaw tightened.","’Of course they did. Of course they lied.’","The realization shouldn’t have surprised him. The Ashford family had lied about everything, his mother, his status, the marriage contract, the dungeon expedition that had crippled his wives. One more lie on top of the pile was entirely in character.","But now, thanks to the system, the house was genuinely his. Legally and permanently his with no hidden strings and leverage nor any hidden clauses.","’Let them try to take it back now.’","He folded the deed carefully and placed it into his spatial storage alongside the other rewards.","Dexter then focused on the other rewards and he blinked his eyes in disbelief."]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155 | Middle Of The Night & Selene","paragraphs":["’ Transcendent-Class meat...’","He had never even seen a Transcendent Realm beast, let alone held one’s meat in his hands. Transcendent Realm creatures were the kind of monsters that required multiple teams of Ultra-Rank heroes to bring down.","Not to mention that a single Tier-1 Transcendent beast could probably flatten this entire neighborhood if it wanted to.","And now he had twenty kilograms of its meat sitting in his spatial storage.","’ If I cook with this...’","His Great Grandmaster Foodsmith mind was already racing. A single cut of Transcendent-Class meat, properly prepared, could elevate a meal to Grade Five or higher. The girls’ cultivation bases would skyrocket. Their damaged bodies would receive an unprecedented surge of restorative energy.","Dexter’s mouth watered and his eyes lit up. He couldn’t wait to cook with the meat quickly but then, he forced himself to calm down.","He would save this for the right moment. Cooking with Transcendent-Class meat required careful preparation and the right combination of supporting ingredients to create a very high grade meal. It might even have the chance to enter the 6 tier!","Then his eyes at the three years of cultivation and the Celestial Spirit beans. He was particularly pleased cites about the beans. And as for the three years cultivation, he was already used to getting such things so it was alredy normal to him.","’I hope I get more of the Celestial Beans.’","With it, the impurities in his body would be cleansed and while he knew nothing about the Holy Child Physique, it sounded powerful and attractive.","As for the Adrenaline Surge pill, he didn’t want to think about it.","\"System. Apply the three years of compressed cultivation.\"","The effect was immediate.","A tidal wave of mana erupted from deep within his inner universe as it flooded into the massive Helix shape DNA.","His cultivation began to climb as he broke through all the way to the 9th level of the Superhuman realm.","\"Boom!\"","Dexter’s body shook as his muscles tightened and his bones crackled. His blood raced through his veins like liquid fire, carrying mana to every part of his body. The air mattress beneath him crinkled and deformed from the sheer pressure radiating from his skin.","9th Stage Superhuman Realm!","Just three more stages and he would stand at the absolute peak of the Superhuman Realm. Then breakthrough to the Ultra Realm, the realm of the powerful.","Where one can truly call themselves a powerhouse.","Dexter opened his eyes and three colored lights flickered in his pupils before fading to natural black as he let loose a soft smile.","However, Dexter didn’t pause to celebrate, he closed his eyes again and continued cultivating.","He cultivated through the night and only turned to sleep when it was 2.am.","He had been renovating the entire house throughout the day so he was quite tired and he slept quite quickly, just as quickly as his mom left.","---","An hour passed, maybe twi.","Then—","\"Creak.\"","The whisper of his bedroom door opening sounded through the room.","Although he was asleep, his enhanced hearing picked it up!","His consciousness snapped back to full alertness and he was about to move.","’ Who—’","Then the cold hit him like a ghost creeping around his room.","The temperature in the room dropped by several degrees in a split second. Dexter immediately recognized who it was.","There was only one person in this house who carried that kind of cold.","’ Selene? Is she having another episode?’","He internally shook his head. ’I’d just given her the serum. Even if It doesn’t hold a full week, it should be enough for three days right?’","Although he was thinking this, he didn’t move and wanted to see what she wanted.","\"Tap.\" \"Tap.\" \"Tap.\"","Hesitant footsteps sounded on the wooden floor as it got closer slowly as though trying their best not to make noise.","The footsteps moved from the door to the center of the room, then stopped as silence descended.","Selene was standing somewhere near the foot of his bed. Dexter could feel her presence through the cold mana emanating from her and her intoxicating smell just like when the first rain drop of water hit dry desert.","He could hear her breathing slowly.","20 seconds passed, then 30 seconds, as she remained there without moving.","Selene didn’t move and simply stood there, at the foot of his bed, in the dark.","It was then he came to a conclusion... ’ She’s cold.’","Of course she was cold. The chronic illness that infected her body generated an endless supply of freezing energy that her body couldn’t regulate. During the day, the warmth of the sun and the activity of movement helped distract from it. But at night, the cold became unbearable.","Even if Dexter had taken away the pain, the discomfort was still there.","And Dexter’s body radiated heat. And not just ordinary human heat but heat derived from one of the nine heavenly flames.","She had come to his room exactly for the heat, but she couldn’t bring herself to do it.","\"Tap.\"","She moved another step closer as her hand, stretched out toward him. Close enough that Dexter could feel the chill of her fingertips hovering just inches above his shoulder.","Then she pulled back.","A quiet, frustrated exhale escaped her lips, then—","\"Tap!\" \"Tap!\" \"Tap!\"","The footsteps retracted as it reached the door.","Dexter wanted to stand up and call her back but he stopped himself. What would he say? ’Stay? Let’s sleep together while I share my flame heat with you.’","\"Click.\"","The door closed softly and silence returned as Selene returned to her room.","Dexter eyes snapped open as he sat upright slowly.","He stared at his closed bedroom door for a long time.","’ It seemed she really wanted to stay.’","1","She had reached out to touch him. And then she had stopped herself.","’Why?’","Three weeks ago, she had flinched at the slightest brush of his fingers as though his hands were made of acid.","The fact that she now ’wanted’ to be near him and that she actively sought his warmth, was already a monumental shift in her behavior. But wanting something and allowing yourself to have it were two very different things.","She was caught between her body’s desperate need for warmth and her mind’s stubborn refusal to be vulnerable.","’ It seems we need to talk.’"]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156 | Strange Lady...","paragraphs":["Morning came quietly.","Dexter woke around 5:00 AM, as he always did.","The sky outside was still dark and the neighborhood was also silent with occasional sounds of dogs barking.","He showered, dressed in a clean grey wig-beater and a dark joggers, then began his morning routine.","Breakfast was simple today — Celestial Spirit Bean porridge with honey, soft scrambled eggs, and warm Star-Shaped Leaf tea.","He kept the portions moderate. The girls’ bodies were still processing yesterday’s concentrated wave of nourishment, and overloading them again so soon would be counterproductive.","He woke the girls one by one.","Lyra first with a typed message on his phone, [Wake up. Breakfast is ready.] held in front of her face until her eyes opened. She nodded, stretched, and shuffled to the bathroom.","Selene was alredy awake but she didn’t look at him directly. However, she didn’t avoid him either.","After making breakfast, he pushed her wheelchair to the bathroom, helped her through her morning routine.","\"Unclasping a bra with two fingers. You’re quite the expert now aren’t you.\"","Mira smiled wickedly as she watched him take care of her.","Dexter responded half-heartedly.","\"Yeah. My fingers are quite magical, aren’t they?\"","Mira was stunned at Dexter’s quick retort which made her remember about yesterday’s incident.","\"You—\"","\"You what? Didn’t you start it?\"","Dexter chuckled as he wagged his fingers in front of her face and laughed as Mira glared at him with a Mixture of anger and embarrassment.","Without waiting for her to speak anymore, he took care of her. He also noticed the flush from yesterday had faded entirely but it came back when he made fun of her.","...","Breakfast was eaten in silence. The Celestial Spirit Bean porridge was well-received and even Mira finished her entire bowl without complaint, though she would rather die than admit she enjoyed it.","After breakfast, Dexter left the girls to their own devices and stepped outside to the front porch.","The street was quiet, most residents already gone to work or school.","Dexter knelt on the porch with a bag of seeds and several empty clay pots. He filled each pot with dark, rich soil from the backyard, patted it flat, and carefully pressed small holes into the earth with his thumb. Into each hole, he dropped a single seeds and soon his hands were soon caked with soil.","Also, his grey wife beater were also a stained with dirt. He didn’t mind though and he found it deeply satisfying planting seeds.","\"Vrooom!\"","He was halfway through the fifth pot when a car pulled up to the curb.","Dexter glanced up briefly.","It was a luxury BMW.","The engine purred loudly like a beast.","Dexter’s eyes lingered on it for a moment, then he returned to his planting.","’ Must be visiting one of the neighbors. Probably Grandma Lucy’s relatives.’","’ Though why they’d park in front of my house instead of hers is beyond me.’","He shrugged mentally and went back to pressing seeds into soil.","Thirty seconds passed.","Then—","\"Knock. Knock.\"","Dexter frowned and he looked up, staring at the gate for a moment, then brushed his palms against his joggers and stood up.","He walked to the gate, unlatched the lock, and pulled it open.","A woman stood on the other side.","The woman standing on the other side of the gate had orange hair that caught the morning sunlight and threw it back in warm, reddish-gold threads.","It fell past her shoulders in carefully styled waves, it was obvious she had spent hours achieving the appearance of effortless beauty.","A pair of red-framed sunglasses on her face, partially covering her orange eyes.","She was dressed in a tailored cream blouse, high-waisted charcoal trousers, and pointed heels with a leather handbag on her shoulder, and thin gold earrings glinted beneath her hair.","Everything about her screamed money, wealth and taste.","\"Can I help you?\"","The woman’s amber gaze traveled from his face down to his chest, then to his dirty hands, then back up to his face.","Her lips thinned un disdain as ash spoke arrogantly.","\"Who are you?\"","Dexter’s eyes blinked, slightly stunned.","\"You came to my house and you’re asking me who I am?\"","\"Wrong address, lady.\"","He immediately pulled the gate shut, then turn back to continue his work.","He hadn’t taken two steps before—","\"Knock. Knock.\"","Dexter stopped. Closed his eyes. Counted to three. Then turned around, walked back, and pulled the gate open again.","\"What do you want?\"","The woman’s expression hardened and her amber eyes flashing with irritation and arrogance.","\"You dare slam the door against my face?\"","She glared at Dexter but inhaled deeply and calmed down and said sharply. \"I’m sure I have the right address. No. 18, Willow Creek Lane, Fenmore street. \"","\"Yes, this is the house,\" Dexter interrupted flatly.","\"Then this is the right address. I’m looking for my sister.\" The woman’s chin lifted as she looked down on Dexter indifferently.","\"I assume you’re the gardener?\"","Dexter’s expression didnr change but his eyes sharpened.","Gardener.","He looked at the woman again. Then he noticed the hair again, it wasn’t crimson but it was familiar and also, the facial structure was similar too. The same proud, deliberate way of holding her head.","’ Sister .’","This woman was looking for Mira. Which meant she was a Calloway.","But Dexter didn’t say any of that.","\"I’m no gardener,\" he said, his voice flat and stripped of warmth. \"State your business here.\"","The woman frowned. Her lips parted as if to deliver another sharp retort — then stopped as her amber eyes narrowed, studying his face.","Then her eyes flashed.","A slow, knowing smirk curled across her lips.","\"You’re not the gardener, which means you’re Dexter,\" she said. \"The bastard son of the Ashford family.\"","She said it as though she was sating singling filthy.","\"The ’conniving’ bastard son of the Ashford family,\" she mocked as her face hardened.","Instantly, her aura exploded.","\"Weng!\"","As though a mountain had landed on him, awall of compressed, dense and heavy pressure slammed into Dexter.","The pressure radiated outward from her body in visible waves, distorting the air around her and the grass on the side of the walkway flattened as though pressed by an invisible hand.","Ultra Realm!"]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157 | It’s Just The Wind...","paragraphs":["Ultra Realm.","The lady’s amber eyes locked onto Dexter with a sneer.","She expected to see fear on his face, waiting for his knees to buckle and for him to crash into the ground underneath the weight of her aura.","But...","Dexter stood perfectly still as though a slightly powerful wind just by passed him, ruffling his hair and fluttering his dirty wife-beater but, that was all.","His expression was totally flat and unimpressed. He was even slightly annoyed.","The lady’s expression changed slightly as her smirk faltered for a split second.","’Wasn’t this guy said to be useless? How was he able to overcome realm suppression?’","Dexter frowned and said flatly, his patience wearing thin.","\"If you’re done with the theatrics, you can come in. I assume you want to see your sister.\"","The woman stared at Dexter with a slight frown but she ultimately nodded her head as her subsided.m back inside of her.","\"Yes. I’m looking for my sister, Mira. I assume she’s here.\"","Dexter pursed his lips. \"Alright. Come in.\"","He stepped aside.","The woman removed her red sunglasses, and tucked them into her handbag.","As she stepped through the gate and into the front yard, her nose wrinkled in irritation as she walked the ground as though it would stain her expensive heel.","Her eyes swept the yard with pure disgust.","Even though it had all been fully renovated, she still behaved as though she was stepping in a crack house.","Dexter rolled his eyes.","He had spent almost two days transforming this property into something clean and presentable. The fence was freshly painted, the lawn was trimmed and the porch was spotless.","Even the walls were clean and whole. It looked really neat.","But this lady behaved as though it was beneath her.","’ Dramatic for nothing.’","He led her up the porch steps and to the front door. He pulled it open, turned to face her, gave her fake smile.","\"Come in.\"","Under normal circumstances, Dexter would have been genuinely welcoming. Discovering that a guest was his sister-in-law and Mira’s own blood. He would hosted her better.","But he didn’t for two reasons.","The first was her behavior.","And the second, was Mira.","If this woman was truly close to Mira, she would have been there three weeks ago, a the marriage and stand beside Mira on that evening.","Bur she wasn’t. And it wasn’t as though she couldn’t have known. The marriage had been public. The Ashford family’s humiliation of their bastard son had been all over the news.","Even the monster outbreak made news. Not to mention the assassination attempt on the highway.","If this woman had cared, she would have come days ago or even weeks ago.","Instead, she was showing up now.","Which meant one of two things. Either something had changed that had suddenly made Mira worth visiting, or this visit had nothing to do with sisterly affection at all.","’Mira isn’t going to be happy to see her.’","The lady was about to step inside when Dexter spoke in a sharp tone.","\"Take off your shoes.\"","The woman froze mid-step and her eyes widened as she turned to stare at him in disbelief.","\"What?\"","Dexter indifferently repeated himself.","\"You either take off your shoes and come in, or you keep them on and stay outside. Your choice.\"","The woman’s jaw tightened and he eyes seem to erupt in flames as she glared at Dexter as though she wanted to burn him right there.","Dexter blinked hind eye and continued to stare at her with a flat gaze.","He had been on the receiving end of Mira’s glares every single day, this woman’s glare was barely anything.","The two of them stood there on the porch, glaring at each other.","Eventually, the woman exhaled sharply.","\"Fine.\"","She reached down, unbuckled her heels and placed them neatly to the side of the door.","Dexter nodded. \"Good, you can now come in.\"","The woman walked into the house barefoot, and it looked like she was walking through hell.","Dexter chuckled internally. ’ That’s what you get.’","Of course he did it intentionally after all, he also wears his boots around the house.","The lady’s gaze swept through the place and her her lips curled in disdain.","While the house looked a bit small, it was clean and every square inch of it had been repaired, painted, and polished by his own hands.","If she couldn’t see that, it was her problem, not his.","The woman’s eyes continued their survey as it moved from the kitchen all the way to the living room then she froze as her gaze landed on a specific spot in the living room.","The space directly in front of the large window. And in that place was Mira","She sat in her wheelchair with her eyes closed and her hands in her laps.","To a stranger, she looked like she was resting but the lady in the doorway narrowed her gaze.","Anna was actually being absorbed by Mira.","The Star Nodes of the Grand Cosmos Scripture were passive. Even when Mira wasn’t actively cultivating, they still drew mana like a gravitational pull.","\"Mira,\" she breathed.","Mira heard it and the mana flow ceased as though it was an illusion.","Mira opened her eyes and turned her head to the direction.","Crimson eyes instantly collided with amber ember eyes as the two sisters stared at each other across small living room.","Mira’s expression was flat as she gazed at her sister while her sister’s brows were furrowed.","’I must have been imagining it.’","She had actually sensed mana flowing toward her sister whose meridians had been shattered beyond repair three years ago and had become a cripple physically and internally.","’ It’s probably just the wind.’","That was because the alternative was impossible.","Healing shattered meridians wasn’t a matter of medicine or rest or time. It required a sustained, astronomical investment of heavenly treasures like Grade 6 or higher pills, rare herbs and even transcendent healers.","The kind of resources that would drain even the wealthiest families in Stargate City.","She eas there when her family elders calculated the exact cost of restoring Mira’s meridians and it resulted in them losing 60 to 70 percent of their asset.","The Calloway family which was ranked fifth most influential family in Stargate City would have been reduced to commoners within a year.","And in a city like Stargate City, a wealthy family without wealth would be wiped out in days as old grudges would be settled.","All to heal just a single person."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158 | The Nine Families","paragraphs":["Therefore, even if the Calloway family sacrificed everything and successfully rebuilt Mira’s meridian, there was no guarantee she would walk again.","Of course the Calloway family refused.","From a purely strategic standpoint, sacrificing an entire family’s future for one member was a losing proposition. The Calloway family had other prodigies they could use the resources they had to nurture.","So they had let her remain until they had found another use for her.","Marriage.","Stargate City was governed by nine influential families. Nine pillars of wealth, power, and. strength.","At the top was the unquestioned, unrivaled, unapproachable Ashford family. The apex.","Their wealth was so vast that the second and third family combined wasn’t even half their net worth. Their political connections extended into every level of government, military, and commerce.","The name Ashford was a brand. They were so dominant that, over the decades, anyone in the city who happened to share the surname \"Ashford\" through coincidence had changed their name. Whether voluntary or involuntarily, it was unknown.","Below the Ashford family was the Sterling family They controlled the city’s monster corpses. In any other city, they would have been the premier family. In Stargate City, they were second.","The third family was the Montclair dynasty, from old money and old blood.","Their influence was from generational political power. They possess members seated on nearly every major civic committee, regulatory board, and judicial panel in the city. Their wealth was comparable to the Sterlings, though slightly less, and their strength was supplemented by an extensive network of alliances with smaller families and guilds.","The fourth family was the Hawthorne family.","The fifth family, was the Calloway family. They had produced more B-Rank and A-Rank heroes per generation than any family outside the top three. Their daughters, in particular, were known for exceptional mana affinities and rare talents. Mira had been their crown jewel with an S-Rank affinity with an A-Rank Crimson Flame-Heart talent, the youngest B-Rank hero in the city’s history. Her potential had been limitless until the dungeon.","The sixth family was the Frost family.","The seventh family was the Vance family.","The eighth and ninth families were the Carver and Delacroix families respectively","The competition between families are wild and the hierarchy was rigid. Moving up even a single position required decades of sustained effort, strategic marriages, and careful accumulation of wealth and military power.","Or, the easiest way, through marriage alliance with a massively wealthy and influential family. The three families room this shortcut.","Each had negotiated independently ans each had been promised the same prize: marriage of their daughter to the firstborn son and heir of the Ashford family.","The contract had been ironclad as per the insistence of the three lesser families to prevent the Ashfords from wriggling out of the arrangement and making it so that dissolution was nearly impossible.","They had thought they were being clever and had cornered the Ashfords, but knowing that the Ashfords had been smarter.","The firstborn was Dexter.","By the time the three families discovered the truth, the contract was already signed and they couldn’t back out.","The Ashford family had scammed all three families in one stroke. They had rid themselves of their embarrassing bastard son, fulfilled the marriage contract to the letter, and — most brilliantly — avoided giving the three lesser families access to the real Ashford heir and the genuine political leverage that would have come with him.","But the three families had still benefited from the arrangement. A marriage tie to the Ashford name, even through a bastard, was still a marriage tie. The Calloway family had risen from 5th to 4th. The Frost family from 6th to 5th. The Vance family from 7th to 6th. Each had climbed a single rank.","Had they married the true heir the political and social capital would have been enormously greater. It would have been a two-rank jump instead of one, along with access to Ashford resources, Ashford support, and Ashford political backing.","Instead, they got Dexter, a bastard who couldn’t even cultivate.","At least — that was what they had believed.","---","Although it took time to explain, roughly three seconds had passed.","Rosalind’s fake smile widened as she approached Mira’s wheelchair.","\"Sister.\"","She said in an almost sweet tone.","Mira’s crimson eyes glanced indifferently at her elder sister as she spoke in a cold tone.","\"Rosalind. What are you doing here?\"","’Rosalind... sounds villainous.’","Dexter hadn’t bothered to ask when she arrived at his gate, nor that he cared to anyways.","Rosalind face made a mock frown, prey pretending to be hurt.","\"Mira, I’m your elder sister. Of course I have to check on your wellbeing. You’ve been married for almost a month now. I was worried andneeded to see how your husband is treating you.\"","She turned toward Dexter as her eyes swept over his dirty wife beater.","Her smirk deepened.","\"So this is your husband,\" she said, addressing Mira but speaking loud enough for Dexter to hear every syllable. \"I thought they said he was useless.\"","She paused as she sensed his energy wave but there was nothing.","\"He really is as useless as they said.\" she sneered and said in a loud tone.","She turned back to Mira.","\"During the assassination attempt, I’m pretty sure he was busy hiding in a corner while the real hero did the work.\" She let out a soft, musical laugh. \"Thankfully, you’re alright. That’s what matters.\"","Mira rolled her eyes.","She glanced at Dexter and a faint trace of amusement could be seen in her eyes but she turned back to Rosalind.","\"What do you want?\"","Rosalind’s fake pout faltered for a fraction of a second before she recomposed herself.","\"I came here for you,\" she said, her voice stiffening. \"And you’re not being very appreciative. I traveled all this way to check on my own sister, and this is the reception I receive?\" She placed a hand on her hip. \"But I won’t take it to heart. I know you’ve been through a lot.\""]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159 | Get Out!","paragraphs":["Rosalind fake pouted in a false hurt tone.","\"I came here for you, and you’re not being very appreciative. It kind of hurts but I won’t take it to mind. I know you’ve been through a lot.\"","She then moved toward the sofa. As she turned to sit, her nose wrinkled. She looked at the cushion which dexter had cleaned and vacuumed clean, recently vacuumed as though she was about to sit in a public toilet as she gently sat at the edge of the sofa.","It was as though the sofa might contaminate her if she allowed herself to fully relax against it.","Dexter’s eye twitched.","’She’s beginning to get in my nerves.’","Dexter’s patience was wearing thin but he chose to wait and continued watching.","Rosalind crossed one leg over the other as she started speaking.","\"Alright,\" she said, her tone shifting from performative sisterly concern to business. \"I won’t argue with you anymore, Mira. I came here for a reason.\"","She paused, letting the silence build.","\"We found the Phoenix Flare Flower.\"","The name landed in the room like a thunderclap.","Mira’s eyes widened slightly as she stared hard at her sister.","Seeing this reaction, Rosalind smiled smugly and continued, clearly savoring the moment.","\"Crowell lead a dungeon raid a few days ago to an S-Rank dungeon, I was also part of the team. \" she said. \"We cleared the dungeon and killed the Phoenix. One of the rewards was actually a Phoenix Flare Flower.\"","’Crowell.’","Crowell Montclair. Of the Montclair family. The third most influential family in Stargate City.","Mira’s former fiancé.","The man she had been engaged to before her meridians were shattered, and before she became a cripple and packaged off to marry a bastard she had never met.","Rosalind’s smile widened.","\"As you know, the Phoenix Flare Flower is a Tier-5 Heavenly Treasure,\" she continued, her voice taking on the smooth, persuasive cadence of a saleswoman delivering her pitch. \"As I’m sure you know, it possesses a restorative ability called Phoenix Rebirth.\"","She uncrossed and re-crossed her legs as her confidence grew even stronger.","\"Phoenix Rebirth is known for one thing, creating a secondary meridian and repairing damaged ones, granting one the legendary Phoenix meridians which is wider, stronger, and more efficient than the others.\"","\"If you use it, you will gain another set of meridians and repair your former damaged ones. And once your meridians are restored...there might be a chance you could walk again.\"","Rosalind smiled, crossed her arms and waited for Mira to react.","She wanted the proud, broken sister little sister of hers to be excited, beg, ask about Crowell, plead with her to arrange a meeting. To promise anything in exchange for the flower that could make her use mana again.","And even insult and forsake her useless husband.","Rosalind had rehearsed this moment and she couldn’t help but smile with expectant gaze.","What she got instead was —","Mira’s utter indifference!","Mira’s eyes had widened slightly because she had suppressed a yawn then they narrowed and went completely, indifferent.","\"No need.\"","The two words from Mira’s lips felt like jolt in Rosalind’s brain.","Rosalind blinked.","\"I’m sorry?\"","\"I said I don’t need it,\" Mira repeated, her voice unchanged. \"Now, if that’s all you came here for—\"","She turned her head away from Rosalind.","\"Get out.\"","Dexter slapped his mouth to suppress his laughter. So it wasn’t just him Mira was annoying to.","Rosalind stared with a stunned look on her face as though she was dreaming. She frowned uncrossed her legs as she opened her mouth.","\"I don’t think you heard me right. Crowell MontClaire , your real fiancé entered an S-rank dungeon for you and found a Phoenix Flare Flower capable of restoring shattered meridians.\"","She spoke slowly, enunciating each word as though Mira had lost the ability to comprehend language along with her ability to walk.","\"If you use it, your shattered meridians will heal, completely. Do you understand what I’m saying, Mira? You would be able to cultivate again.\"","Mira turned her head back toward Rosalind impatience.","\"And I don’t think ’you’ are hearing me right,\" she said, her voice was so flat at that moment. \"I said I do not need it.\"","She held Rosalind’s gaze for one cold, unblinking second.","\"Now, if that is all you came here for, get out.\"","Rosalind’s mouth opened and closed like a fish gasping for water as the narrative in her head collapsed.","The sister she had come to rescue was refusing to be rescued and was even looking at her with the same contempt she always had for her.","Rosalind stood up from the sofa. Her hands were clenched at her sides, her knuckles white.","\"I don’t think you understand what you’re refusing,\" she said, in a sharp tone. \"Father wants you to speak with Crowell. He wants you to ask Crowell to provide the Phoenix Flare Flower to you.\"","’There it is.’","Mira’s lips curved upwards in a cold smile.","\"So Crowell hasn’t actually given the flower yet. And you want me to meet a condition in exchange for a Tier-5 treasure.\"","She tilted her head, her crimson eyes sharp as she glanced at her sister. She wanted to say something more but she eventually shook her head.","\"Forget it. Just leave.\"","Rosalind’s face flushed with anger and embarrassment.","\"You dare defy father? Father will not hear of this!\" she snapped as she spoke in a cold tone. \"Father has ’ordered’ you to—\"","A figure stepped between the two sisters.","Dexter.","He positioned himself directly between Rosalind and Mira’s wheelchair in a relaxed and casual posture but his eyes were cold.","He looked directly at Rosalind, and when he spoke, his voice was anything but gentle.","\"Whether it’s your father, or your entire Calloway family...\"","He paused.","\"...that has nothing to do with this house.\"","Rosalind stared at him, her amber eyes wide with a mixture of shock and outrage.","Dexter held her gaze without blinking.","\"You’ve said what you came to say.\"","He raised his right hand and pointed toward the front door.","\"So now, please leave.\"","[A/N: Dedicated To Reader Crow_Constellation]","[A/N: I definitely haven’t forgotten you all. My next Chapters will be dedicated to you guys! Thank you for the new month gift and thanks reading]","[Oh... I still haven’t forgotten I owe you guys Mass release Chapters for the gifts...they will be released in 2 to 3 days. Love y’all!]"]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160 | Impossible!","paragraphs":["Rosalind’s amber eyes flashed with cold fury. She looked at Dexter, from his foot all the way to his head and her lip curled with undisguised contempt.","\"When did a bastard servant earn the right to speak to me like that?\"","\"Know your place.\"","She stepped forward and her Ultra-Rank aura exploded.","\"Now... Fuck. Off.\"","Dexter blinked in surprise at this girl’s audacity, telling him to fuck off in his own house.","’Bitch, you asked for it.’","His eyes glowed violet and crimson as killing intent flashed in his gaze.","He raised his finger, reaching for the connection he shared with the Protection Talisman.","The talisman repelled all everyone and anything below the Transcendent Realm.","Rosalind who had just entered Ultra-Rank would be sent flying like an ant in a hurricane.","He was a split second from activating the talisman when—","\"WHOOOOOM!!\"","A roaring wall of flame exploded from behind him.","Dexter’s eyes went wide as a massive roaring heat hit him he took a step back, turning around and was stunned by what he saw.","Mira was actually on fire!","The woman sitting in the wheelchair moments ago was now enveloped in magnificent crimson flames.","Her blood-red hair floated in the air as though dancing with the fire itself and her crimson eyes burned like twin suns.","The blazing flames wrapped around her slender body like an hurricane and she was in the eye of it. She dint look like a goddess of flames, but a goddess of death and slaughter!","Dexter stared blankly.","This...","This was the first time he had ever seen Mira use her talent and it was breathtakingly beautiful and absolutely terrifying. It’s no wonder she was called the Crimson Valkyrie!","Then the flames surged as gathered behind Mira’s wheelchair as they twisted and solidified.","A two meters tall phantom image of a Crimson Valkyrie immediately materialized behind her.","She stood tall and proud, with a flaming sword in her hand.","Dexter stared in slight surprise.","He had read about the Crimson Valkyrie’s signature technique called the Crimson Flame Demoness technique.","It was said that in her prime, Crimson Valkyrie uses this to attack multiple enemies at the same time.","And at her peaks, she could merge with the Crimson Flame Demoness, raising her strength by almost 200%.","With this technique, she had killed above her level and cleared multiple S-rank dungeons.","It was probably what had saved her during the SSS-rank dungeon before she managed to escape.","Mira’s blazing crimson eyes instantly locked onto her sister as he voice lacked any warmth at all.","\"When...\"","\"...did it become your turn to speak to my husband like that?\"","Her right wrist actually moved at that moment as she suddenly flicked her index finger.","\"BOOM!!\"","The Flame Goddess moved.","The enormous sword descended in a vertical arc as it moved so fast the air shrieked!","Rosalind’s face changed as the color drained from her cheeks.","\"Impossible!\"","Her Ultra-Rank aura exploded outward as a scarlet barrier materialized before her.","\"BANG!!\"","Shockwave exploded as the flaming sword slammed into the barrier.","The scarlet barrier blazed brightly for half a second.","Then—","\"Crack!\"","The barrier shattered as the flaming sword slammed directly into Rosalind’s arms which she quickly crossed before her.","\"BOOM!!!\"","She was blasted backward like a cannonball as her body smashed through the living-room window.","\"Crash!\"","Glass exploded everywhere as her entire body flew completely out of the house before crashing onto the street outside.","Dexter cheered internally and couldn’t help but grin.","’Home run!’","Dexter’s smile suddenly stiffened and his eyelid twitched.","’Wait. I just renovated this house and now there’s a hole in my living room.’","Dexter glanced at Mira, then at the hole, then back at Mira and he smiled bitterly.","\"You should have let me chase her out myself.\"","Mira blinked and the blazing fire in her eyes flickered as the Flame Goddess dissolved along with the crimson flames.","She looked down with a slightly embarrassed and apologetic expression like a kid who had done something wrong.","Mira remained silent.","Several seconds later, she quietly mumbled, \"...I didn’t like the way she spoke to you.\"","Dexter froze and for a brief moment, his heart skipped a beat. He was actually speechless at that moment.","Pride and warmth bloomed in his chest, making him smile. But it froze at Mira’s next words.","\"Only I get to bully you, no one else.\"","Dexter clicked his tongue and rolled his eyes.","\"...Alright, but next time, let me handle it first.\"","Mira gave a small nod and turned away.","Dexter fake glared at her then leapt out of the house through the broken window.","He landed lightly on the front porch and walked toward the gate.","Outside...","Rosalind slowly climbed to her feet in the middle of the street. She was barefooted as her heels was still on Dexter’s front porch.","Her pretty clothes were covered in dust and burn holes. Her hair had become disheveled and blood at the corner of her lips as she panted.","Her chest was in pain but it wasn’t as painful as the humiliation in her chest.","Various expression flashed across her face.","Shock, confusion, disbelief, anger and also fear!","\"Impossible...\"","She mumbled over and over and over again as though she couldn’t believe what had happened just now.","Because, Mira should not have been able to do that!","Mira’s meridians were shattered, her mana dissipated and not only that, she was paralyzed from the neck down and in every way a, cripple.","And yet she had just launched an Ultra-Rank hero backward with a single strike from the technique she was famous for!","’How’s that possible? What changed?’","Something that Rosalind didn’t understand.","At that moment, Dexter jumped through the window and started walking calmly towards her.","’Right, the bastard husband will know what happened.’","Suddenly, a terrifying Ultra-Rank aura erupted from her body.","\"BOOM!\"","The pressure swept across the entire neighborhood.","Dogs that had been barking suddenly tucked their tails between their legs, birds scattered into the sky and even the insects fell silent as the peaceful street became deathly quiet."]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161 | You’re Truly Beautiful When You Smile","paragraphs":["Rosalind’s eyes locked onto Dexter with blinding, murderous rage.","\"You...\"","She wasn’t able to finish the word.","A hand landed on her shoulder.","Instantly, the entire aura erupting out of her body dissipated like smoke, collapsing back into her body as though it had never existed.","The heavy pressure that had been pressing down on the entire neighborhood evaporated rapidly.","One second, an Ultra-Rank hero was radiating enough killing intent to silence the entire street, the next, she felt like an ordinary woman standing in the road in her bare feet.","Rosalind’s eyes went wide in confusion and shock as she turned around.","There, she saw an old woman standing behind her.","The old woman was short, slightly hunched, with her white hair pulled back in a bun, with deep wrinkles framing a pair of bright, mischievous eyes.","She wore a faded gardening apron over a simple cotton dress, and her hands were still dirty from working in her flowerbeds.","The old lady was smiling warmly as she held softly held Rosalind shoulder like a neighbor who had just stopped to chat with a fellow neighbor about the weather.","\"Hey kid,\" the old woman said in a warm tone. \"Who are you looking for?\"","Rosalind stared at the lady and her mind went blank. That single tap on her shoulder had retracted her entire aura against her own will!","’ What the hell is this woman?’","Although this was her first thought, she didn’t dare to voice it out!","For someone to be able to casually withdraw an Ultra-Rank hero’s aura with a single touch meant only one thing.","This old woman was stronger than her.","Far, far stronger.","Her mouth opened and closed twice before she managed to produce sound.","\"I... my... I came here to visit my sister.\"","She stuttered like a little girl caught doing ai something bad.","At that moment, Dexter just reached the gate.","He stopped and took in the scene.","There, he saw Grandma Lucy’s holding Rosalind’s shoulder and she seem to be cooperating?","Grandma Lucy ignored Rosalind completely and turned toward Dexter with a warm smile.","\"Little chef. I heard some commotion from your place. Is this girl bothering you?\"","Dexter blinked.","He looked at Rosalind and he saw her face was pale and her eyes wide with terror.","Dexter raised an eyebrow and looked at Grandma Lucy. And his eyes narrowed slightly.","He had specifically came outside to vent and teach Rosalind a lesson about speaking with respect but it seems he was late.","Dexter let out a small smile and shook his head.","\"Sorry for the disturbance, Grandma Lucy. It was just a slight argument between sisters, nothing serious. Moreover, this young lady was just leaving.\"","Rosalind shot Dexter a venomous glare but she didn’t dare say otherwise. So she forced a smile and managed to speak.","\"Y-yes,\" she stuttered, nodding rapidly. \"Yes, yes. I was just leaving.\"","\"Alright kid. Take care of yourself then.\" Grandma Lucy smiled and patted Rosalind’s shoulder three times and then retracted her hand.","Each tap made Rosalind face pale even further as her body rumbled. Blood spilled from the corner of her lips.","Rosalind didn’t dare say anything but gritted her teeth and stared at Dexter with deep hatred.","But whatever words she wanted to deliver died on her lips under Grandma Lucy’s cheerful gaze.","She turned and walked toward her BMW with unsteady legs.","She didn’t have her handbag nor her shoes. She was walking barefoot on the street, stepping on the same dirt, and germs that she had been so careful to avoid inside his house.","Now she was stepping on all of it with full confidence because she had no choice.","And that made her even angrier.","She shot Dexter one final, ugly glare over her shoulder before yanking open the car door, sliding into the driver’s seat, and slamming it shut.","\"Vroooom!\"","The engine roared to life as the BMW pulled away from the curb, accelerating down the street, and disappeared around the corner.","Dexter watched her go then he turned to Grandma Lucy and rubbed the back of his neck.","\"Sorry for the disturbance, Grandma Lucy.\"","Grandma Lucy smiled and nodded. \"It’s alright, little chef. These things happen when you have family.\" She paused, her bright eyes twinkling. \"Just remember your promise about giving me a taste of your cooking.\"","Dexter smiled warmly. \"Don’t worry, Grandma Lucy. When I start cooking, you’ll be the first to taste the food. I promise.\"","\"Good kid,\" she smiled and turned back to her course.","Dexter watched her go with narrowed eyes.","’ She’s definitely not simple.’","He shook his head, and walked back inside through the front door.","---","The living room was a mess.","Glass shards covered the floor, dust coated every surface ans curtain hung by a single hook, swaying in the breeze that blew through the enormous hole where the window used to be.","Dexter looked at the destruction and pursed his lips.","’ That’s going to cost money to fix.’","He sighed and began carefully picking up the larger pieces of broken glass, setting them aside in a pile. He would need to purchase new glass, new framing, new plaster, and possibly new insulation depending on how deep the structural damage went.","He was halfway through sweeping the smaller fragments into a dustpan when Mira spoke.","\"Is she gone?\"","Dexter nodded. \"Yes. She left.\"","Mira’s brow furrowed. \"She left just like that?\"","Dexter shrugged. \"Yeah. She left just like that.\"","\"Rosalind now knows I can use mana.\"","Dexter stopped sweeping.","He turned back toward her. \"Yeah.\"","Mira’s crimson eyes were fixed on her own hands. She suddenly spoke softly.","\"Things might become very difficult for you over the next few weeks,\" she said.","Dexter’s brow furrowed as he thought about it.","Rosalind had seen Mira use mana which meant she thinks she had fully recovered her meridians, not knowing it was the Grand CosmosTechnique.","And Rosalind would definitely not keep that information to herself.","She would tell the Calloway family. Immediately and once the Calloway family learned that their broken, discarded daughter could cultivate again, they would want her back. Afterall, Mira was an S-Rank mana affinity holder with an A-Rank Crimson Flame-Heart talent. She was also supposed to be the future family head before disaster struck and now that she was half healed, therefore, they’re definitely not let her rot with a bastard husband.","But Dexter had read the marriage contract. Multiple times after realizing he had been scammed.","He had been looking for a loophole but he realized the contract was ironclad.","Moreover, it wasn’t a normal contract but a Death God Contract.","The three families had insisted on it. They had been so determined to prevent the Ashford family from finding a loophole that they had invoked the most binding form of magical contract in existence. A Death God Contract didn’t just bind the parties legally. It bound their souls.","If any party broke the terms of the contract, their body would remain intact. Their body would continue to exist. But their soul would be ripped from their flesh.","The contract itself enforced the penalty, and no power in the world could override it.","The Calloway family, the Vance family, the Frost family, and the Ashford family had all signed it. All four families were bound by it. And none of them, no matter how powerful, no matter how wealthy, no matter how desperate, would dare break it.","Breaking the contract was the same as seeking death.","So no. The Calloway family could not take Mira back. The same ironclad contract they had designed to trap the Ashford family was now the very thing preventing them from reclaiming what they had discarded.","Dexter turned to Mira and shook his head.","\"Don’t worry about it,\" he said, his voice calm and steady. \"Everything will be fine.\"","Mira glanced at him. Her crimson eyes searched his face for a long moment, looking for doubt, but she saw he was completely confident.","Suddenly, something warm bloomed in her chest as it spread slowly, filling her heart. Her gaze turned gentle and she suddenly smiled without knowing.","Dexter stared, completely dumbfounded. Mira was an extremely beautiful lady and now that she was smiling so warmly, her beauty multiplied by 1000 fold!","She was, in that single moment, breathtakingly beautiful.","The words left his mouth before his brain could stop them.","\"You’re truly beautiful when you smile.\"","Mira froze, her eyes widened as the smile vanished.","Her face suddenly flushed red as she quickly whipped her head away.","\"Pervert,\" she muttered.","He blinked.","\"What did I do this time?\"","Mira refused to answer.","But as she turned her face further toward the wall, hiding her expression behind the curtain of her hair, the corners of her lips curled upward once more.","[Mira Calloway Affection: ...]"]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162 | Whenever You Wish","paragraphs":["Dexter chuckled and turned around into to see Lyra and Selene standing in the hallway. It seemed they had witnessed everything.","Lyra eyes lit up in curiosity as her dark eyes moved between Dexter and Mira with barely concealed interest.","But Selene was another story, she seemed to be glaring at him even though she couldn’t see!","Dexter was confused at first but then it took 2 seconds for him to figure out why.","’ They heard me call Mira beautiful.’","Dexter cleared his throat and smiled awkwardly.","\"Uhm, you two are also very, very pretty.\"","Selene said nothing. She simply turned around and quietly walked back toward the backyard.","Lyra, however, lingered. She looked at Dexter with an expectant gaze.","Dexter scratched the back of his head.","’I really need to be more careful about what I say out loud.’","He flipped his hand. Three bags of chips materialized in his palm.","They were Grade-2 Sminley Chips. He had no idea why the system had chosen that particular name, but the packaging looked nice enough and the chips themselves were infused with mild restorative properties.","\"I assume you want this?\" Dexter said with a soft smile.","Lyra’s face lit up like a lantern.","She took the bags from his hand with both hands, cradling them against her chest like small treasures. Then she looked up at him, and a small smile touched her lips.","’ Thank you, Dexter. You don’t look half-bad yourself.’","Dexter blinked and laughed.","Lyra’s smile widened by a fraction before she turned and hurried back to their room, already tearing open the first bag.","’ One down, one to go.’","Dexter walked through the hallway toward the backyard.","---","Selene was sitting on the swinging chair at the backyard.","Her eyes were closed with her hands rested on her knees, palms upward as she cultivated.","Dexter stopped in front of her.","\"We need to talk.\"","Selene didn’t respond, her face remained perfectly still, her cultivation unbroken.","Dexter pursed his lips and decided to get straight to the point. \"I know you came to my room last night and I also know why.\"","A faint trace of embarrassment flickered across Selene’s pale face but it disappeared quickly.","\"I don’t know what you’re talking about,\" she said quietly.","Dexter smiled helplessly. \"You don’t have to pretend. I understand.\"","Selene opened her eyes. Her white gaze was aimed roughly in his direction but she said nothing.","\"I’ve absorbed your pain,\" Dexter continued, keeping his voice gentle. \"Because of that, I experienced the Eternal Winter Ice inside your body.\"","He paused.","\"I know it isn’t exactly pain but more like an endless, freezing prickling discomfort.\"","Selene’s eyes trembled slightly.","\"You know?\" she whispered.","Dexter nodded. \"I do.\"","He slowly raised his right hand.","With a soft whoosh, the abyssal emperor flame quietly appeared above his palm, spreading heat that radiated warmth in every direction.","The surrounding temperature rose immediately and the air around them grew several degrees warmer. The chill that clung to Selene’s skin began to recede,","Selene stared at the flame. Her pale lips parted slightly.","\"An heavenly flame,\" she murmured. \"So you really possess it.\"","Dexter closed his hand. The flame vanished.","Selene lowered her eyes but she still remained silent.","Dexter smiled gently.","\"Sharing a bed would probably make both of us uncomfortable,\" he said. \"So how about this instead?\"","Selene looked up.","\"Whenever the chill becomes unbearable, you can simply cultivate in my room. The Heavenly Flame naturally radiates warmth from my body, even when I’m sleeping. It should help suppress the Eternal Winter Ice without requiring any direct contact.\"","He paused.","\"When you feel better, you can return to your own room, anytime you wish.\"","Silence filled the backyard.","The breeze stirred Selene’s silver hair. A bird chirped once from the neighbor’s tree, then fell silent.","Several long seconds passed.","\"Thank you.\"","She mumbled quietly.","Dexter smiled. \"It’s alright.\"","Then he looked at her for a moment and added, \"I meant what I said, by the way.\"","Selene tilted her head. \"About what?\"","He held her gaze steadily. \"The three of you are uniquely beautiful in your own way. And that is the truth.\"","A small smile graced Selene’s lips.","She didn’t turn away, letting Dexter bask in her beauty as she closed her eyes and continued her cultivation.","---","Dexter went back inside and headed for the storage room.","Among the renovation materials he had purchased, there were several planks of untreated pine. He selected three that were large enough to cover the hole in the living room wall, carried them to the living room, and began measuring them against the damaged section.","Mira watched him work from her wheelchair. She had moved slightly away from the window but remained in her usual spot near the wall.","Dexter cut the planks to size with a hand saw, fitted them into the gap, and nailed them securely into place.","It doesn’t look nice but it would keep the wind and the rain out until he could purchase proper materials.","He hammered the last nail into place and stepped back.","The living room was now noticeably darker.","The afternoon sunlight that had been streaming through the window was gone, replaced by the dim, flat light of the overhead lamp.","Mira’s favorite spot by the window was now just a spot by a wooden board.","---","The rest of the day went by smoothly.","Dexter cooked a light dinner. The girls ate.","Mira finished her entire bowl without complaint. Lyra ate three portions. Selene ate slowly but steadily.","After dinner, Dexter cleaned the kitchen, washed the dishes, and then turned to Mira.","\"Time for your massage.\"","He expected another flat refusal, another sharp ’no’.","Instead, Mira simply replied, \"Fine.\"","Dexter blinked.","’ Fine? Just fine? No argument? No insult? No death glare?’","He shrugged and wheeled her to the bedroom, helped her onto the bed, and began the familiar routine.","Shirt off. Skirt off. Sports bra and cotton briefs remaining. Face down on the mattress.","He pulled on the special Glove, applied the massage oil to his hands, and then began."]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163 | Damn Vixen","paragraphs":["Shirt off. Skirt off. Sports bra and cotton briefs remaining. Face down on the mattress.","He pulled on the Massage Glove, applied the upgraded Massage Oil to his hands, and began. He started with her shoulders, using the same technique as shown in the 108 Body Massage Sutra.","He set the glove to its lowest vibration and worked the muscles along her spine, channeling mana through his fingertips into the damaged nerve pathways.","Everything was fine.","Feeling a tough muscle in her spine, he increased the vibration as he hands slowly massaged her back, moving lower against her smooth shiny skin.","Eventually, he reached her and massaged her back dimples.","The glove hummed as it he imbued his mana deep into her muscle tissue, stimulating and rejuvenating it, pressing and rolling at the same time.","Suddenly, Dexter felt Mira’s body tremble. He frowned slightly.","’ Was I hallucinating?’","Mira was fully paralyzed, there was no way her body shook. He noticed the slight redness of her ears blinked his eyes and proceed to ignore it.","He moved to down her legs, her toes, then moved upwards her thighs as the glove continued its steady, deep vibration against her skin.","Mira’s face, which was turned to one side against the pillow, moved slightly as her breathing started ri change.","Noticing this, Dexter frowned slightly. ’ Is she in pain?’","But he shook his head, the pain was serenely transferred to him so she isn’t supposed to feel pain.","He moved to her upper thighs. The glove hummed against the thick muscle tissue there, vibrating deep into the connective fibers below as he moved upwards, reaching the peak of her thighs, close to the small gap between her thighs.","At that moment, Mira’s muscles involuntarily spasmed lightly against his skin as Mira’s ears went from red to crimson.","Dexter’s eyes widened slightly as realization crashed into his mind like an explosion.","’ Vibrations, girls... I’m a fool.’","When it came to girls, vibration only meant one different things but against a specific part of their bodies, it meant another thing.","’ And I’ve been doing it for the past two days!’","Dexter almost slapped himself. Ehich groen man wouldn’t have understood? And yet it flew over his head like his dad did when choosing a son.","Throughout his time dealing with Mira, he had always cleared his mind by meditating because no man in their right mind wouldn’t be aroused thinking of touching such a beauty everyday not to mention the fact that Dexter takes care of her everyday.","The technique has worked perfectly well until now. Seeing Mira’s muscles involuntarily tremble and her ears flushed red, he couldn’t help but swallow hard as his thoughts ran rapid and wild.","’ Chaos in order, order in chaos. The primordial universe was birthed by...’","He immediately inhaled deeply and started to recite the mantra of Limitless Grand Cosmos Scripture because right now, his thoughts were beginning to have multiple scenes with various occupations involved.","’This is going to be hard.’","After several seconds, Dexter managed to tame his mind. He clenched his jaws and exhaled. Then after calming down considerably, he continued the massage but his movements had became noticeably stiffer.","Mira had noticed Dexter’s rigid movements. She suddenly shifted her neck to left side, facing Dexter.","Seeing his flushed face, she smirked, realizing he was finally putting two and two together. In an innocent and perfectly misleading tone, she asked, \"Dexter, is something wrong?\"","Dexter blinked and cleared his throat. \"Nothing. Nothing is wrong. Stop speaking, let me focus on the massage.\"","Mira’s smirk widened. \"Are you sure nothing is wrong? Your face is awfully red.\"","Dexter remained silent as he tried focusing on his massage.","Mira’s smile grew wider.","\"If you’re sick, I can ask Lyra or Selene to buy medicine for you.\"","She paused dramatically before adding.","\"Or if it’s a fever, I can perhaps make you some medicinal pepper soup. It might calm your internal organs and make you less hot.\"","She said it in a mocking tone, and Dexter’s gaze immediately flew towards her face and he saw a faint smirk at the corner of her lips and finally realized it.","She was teasing him.","He looked down at her, stunned.","\"...You’re enjoying this, aren’t you?\"","Mira blinked innocently.","\"I have no idea what you’re talking about.\"","Dexter’s face flushed even more as he glared down at Mira, who was lying on the bed. \"You are quite evil, you know that?\"","Mira chuckled. \"I simply caring about your well-being. How’s that being evil? I must admit, seeing you embarrassed is a novelty.\"","Dexter forced his face to be expressionless as he feigned indifference.","\"Please... I was only feeling a little embarrassed.\"","Mira chuckled softly. \"Took you this long to notice.\"","Dexter almost face palmed himself before he stopped halfway. The glove was covered in massage oil.","Mira’s brows rose as she glanced at Dexter’s gloved hands near his face. \"So, touching me isn’t enough?\"","Dexter rolled his eyes. \"Behave, otherwise I will leave without completing the massage?\"","\"Tch! No one likes a ’quick’ tempered husband.\"","Mira’s snorted jokingly, placing emphasis on ’quick’ as she turned her face to the other side.","However, her shoulders trembled ever so slightly as she laughed. Seeing her like that made Dexter shake his head helplessly.","’Damn vixen.’","He managed to keep his composure long enough to roughly finish the massage, hitting the required pressure points and meridian pathways as fast as the technique allowed without actually skipping anything important.","When the last stroke was done, he cleaned the oil off of Mira’s skin.","Usually he would have taken her to bath, but at this moment, it was basically a bad idea.","Afterwhich, he dropped her on the bed and then called Selene and Lyra to the room to go sleep while he rushed into his room.","---","On the bed, Mira looked up at the ceiling, smiling in satisfaction.","The great, calm, mysterious Dexter Ashford, she had finally made him flustered.","’ Finally, i was really worried he might not like women.’","She tilted her head back and blinked.","’ Or maybe I should really be worried now...’","She chuckled.","For three years, she had been trapped in this broken body, unable to feel much.","But the massage had changed that."]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164 | Cultivating With Selene","paragraphs":["Back in his bedroom, Dexter glanced at the ceiling and let out a sigh.","’ Vixen .’","’I truly thought she had fever yesterday.’","He chuckled bitterly as he thought about the previous day.","Then he glanced at the gloves on his palm.","’ Should I toss this away?’","It was quite a dilemma because with the glove, the effect of the massage technique increased a lot which speeds up Mira’s recovery.","But now that the glove Wa steering to have another effect, he wasn’t quite sure he should continue using it.","’ Ah, this is causing me to have a headache. Will think about it another time.’","He threw the glove into his storage ring and sighed as he sat on his bed to cultivate. It took almost 30 minutes for him to finally clear all distracting thoughts and focus on meditating.","---","The clock ticked as an hours passed as he cultivated, then another hour passed.","At this moment, Dexter suddenly opened his eyes, glanced at the time on his phone.","\"1:00 AM.\"","’ Selene isn’t here yet.’","He had been expecting Selene.","Ever since their conversation in the backyard that afternoon, he had been quietly certain that she would come as the arrangement was quite simple and straightforward.","But it was 1:00 AM, and Selene hadn’t come.","Dexter shook his head.","’She’s not comfortable with it yet.’","He wasn’t dejected but understood Selene’s concerns.","After-all, cultivating together in the same room was considered an intimate act, even if it wasn’t technically dual cultivation.","The mana that passed through one person’s body could mingle with the mana of another person in the same space. Their energy fields would overlap and if they were practicing the same cultivation technique, their breathing would synchronize as the shared mana would carry traces of each person’s unique cultivation signature.","For Selene, who absolutely loathes being touched and maintained strict personal boundaries, that kind of proximity was a significant step.","Dexter didn’t blame her. He simply resumed cultivating.","Roughly thirty minutes to an hour later—","\"Creak...\"","Dexter’s eyes opened slowly as his door slowly opened. There, a ghost-like beuty stood in the doorway.","The beauty’s head was bowed as her silver-white hair fell forward, covering her face.","At that moment, a chill speed through the air and fog seemed to float with her as she seemingly floated slowly towards him.","The ghost-like beauty was Selene.","Selene hesitantly walked into the room, but seeing Dexter warm smile, the hesitation faded slightly as she into the room.","Dexter stood up from the bed and gestured toward the mattress. \"Here. You can take the bed.\"","\"I will take air mattress.\"","Selene tilted her head, her hair tilting with her as she shook her head.","Dexter blinked. \"You don’t want the bed?\"","\"We can both cultivate on the bed,\" she said quietly.","Dexter raised an eyebrow, slightly surprised.","But he nodded and sat on the far edge of the bed, leaving as much space as possible between himself and where Selene would sit.","Selene walked to the opposite edge, then sat down slowly, raised her legs, crossed them beneath her, and settled into a meditation posture with her spine was perfectly straight, her palms on her thighs, facing upward and then, she closed her eyes.","There was a faint flush on her pale cheeks and the tips of her ears were slightly pink.","Dexter held back his smile, refusing to say anything. He simply closed his eyes and activated his Heavenly flame. The Abyssal Emperor Flame roared to life.","The temperature in the room shifted dramatically.","Selene’s body constantly radiated cold as the Eternal Winter Ice leaked from her skin in invisible waves, dropping the temperature by several degrees.","But with the activation of the Heavenly Flame, everything changed instantly!","The frigid temperatures instantly rose.","Heat poured from Dexter’s body like a roaring flame.","But Dexter didn’t actually erupt with flames. He simply activated the warmth or heat of the heavenly flames. It rolled outward from his skin and filled the room like sunlight through a window.","The two energies met, one cold and one extremely hot.","Dexter’s heat was overwhelmingly stronger, afterall, it was an heavenly flame.","It radiated intense heat that Selene’s suppressed Eternal Winter Ice couldn’t hope to match.","At that moment, Selene let out a soft, comfortable sigh as the prickling sensation on her skin reduced by a lot and her muscles relaxed.","Dexter noticed it through his Enhanced Hearing and watched her heartbeat slow down incredibly. Her breathing had also deepened and the tension in her muscles had eased.","’ Seems like it’s working.’","He nodded internally and then focused on his cultivation.","An hour passed.","Dexter occasionally opens his eyes every 30 minutes.","This time, he opened his eyes and noticed something.","Selene’s spine, which had been perfectly straight when she sat down, was beginning to lean slowly towards his direction.","From her breathing, she wasn’t sleeping but her body was tilting towards him unconsciously like a flower turning toward the sun.","Dexter wanted to increase the heat mire intensely, so she wouldn’t need to lean.","But if he did that, the temperature would cross the combustion threshold and everything, including the mattress, the sheets, the wooden bed frame would burst into flames.","But he also couldn’t tell her to come closer. She was already like a frightened rabbit.","So instead, he moved closer to her.","He shifted his position on the bed, sliding forward until his knees were almost touching hers.","Selene noticed.","Her eyes snapped open and widened as she felt the sudden surge of heat intensify.","The pricking sensation beneath her skin, the maddening itch of frozen nerve endings, seemed to melt as the deep ache in her bones faded.","It felt as though standing in front of a fireplace after a blizzard.","She looked up at him.","Dexter’s eyes were closed, absorbed in cultivation, he was pretending nothing had happened.","Selene stared at his peaceful expression for a long moment.","Then a small, quiet smile touched her lips.","She closed her eyes, straightened her back and continued cultivating."]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165 | It’s Not What You Think!","paragraphs":["Roughly another hour passed.","Selene’s body was leaning forward again.","Dexter opened his eyes and looked at her. At this moment, her eyes were closed and her expression was incredibly peaceful.","Without a word, he shifted his position again. He didn’t move directly in front of her this time but actually moved directly beside her.","At this position, their shoulders were touching with no space in the middle as the heat from Dexter body directly made contact with Selene’s body.","Then he closed his eyes and resumed cultivating as though he had simply changed positions for comfort and nothing more.","Selene’s eyes opened as the heat penetrated through her skin through physical contact.","At that moment, the heat was so intense Selene almost let out a comfortable moan.","The hear from the heavenly flame pierced through her body and the Eternal Ice Winter retreated like a cowardly wolf","She immediately wanted to recoil and leave but it had been a while she felt this better.","Selene stared at Dexter’s face through her Echolocation. She could see the blurry outline of his expression and could tell he was calm and unbothered.","He was still pretending nothing was happening.","Her thoughts ran wild. She wanted to leave, but at the same time, her body wanted to stay!","It was a conundrum...","She eventually gave up as her body won the battle.","She slipped into cultivation and the atmosphere remained peaceful and warm.","It was the most comfortable Selene had been in three years.","She didn’t even know when she fell asleep.","---","\"Ring! Ring! Ring!\"","Dexter’s phone alarm shattered the silence like a hammer through glass.","His eyes snapped open.","The room was dim as the morning light filtered through the dusty window. The clock on his phone read 5:00 AM.","Dexter blinked and yawned slightly.","\"Ugh.\"","He was aback by his morning breath.","His body was incredibly stiff. He had been sitting in the same cross-legged position for nearly four or three hours without moving.","He suddenly felt something in his shoulder. He looked to the left and saw Selene was asleep on his shoulder.","At some point during the night, her body had leaned towards him as her head layed on his shoulder with her silver-white hair spilling across his chest like moonlight on water.","As Dexter looked down at her, she looked very peaceful. More peaceful than he had ever seen her.","Dexter stared down at her for a long moment wondering how someone could be blessed with such beauty. It was as though she was molded and crafted specially by a creator.","He could see the hair on her eye was also silver in color and it looked really fascinating. If the creator used a day to craft others, they definitely used a Millennium to craft such beauty.","The dull pain snapped Dexter back to reality.","He had been sitting in this exact position for almost three hours, his legs were numb, his spine ached and his neck so stiff he could barely turn it.","But he hadn’t moved because she had been sleeping, and she looked comfortable, he didnt have the heart to disturb her.","It was at that moment Selene’s eyes opened and her brows furrowed for a moment before everything came to her and her eyes widened.","She felt the warmth beneath her cheek and felt rise and fall of his chest beneath her head.","Her Echolocation activated instantly, painting a picture of her surroundings and she realized she was holding Dexter’s left arm, while sleeping in his shoulder.","Her entire body stiffened instantly as she scrambled upright so fast she nearly flashed step!","\"I-I!\" she gasped. \"S-sorry! D-didn’t—\"","She shook her head as she backed off the bed, standing there for a split second, her face burning, her mouth opening and closing without producing any further words.","Then she turned and vanished ran out of the room.","\"Bang!\"","The door slammed shut behind her.","Dexter sat alone on the bed, staring at the closed door.","He let out a long, slow breath.","Then he smiled.","\"Cute.\"","He stretched his arms above his head. His spine popped and his neck cracked twice. His legs tingled with the return of circulation, pins and needles shooting through his calves and feet.","He stood up, stretched again, and opened his bedroom door.","He stepped into the hallway.","And nearly collided with Lyra.","She was standing in the middle of the corridor, with her arms full.","Her left arm was cradling the Primordial Beast Egg against her chest and her right arm was hugging an open bag of Sminley Chips.","Also, her mouth was full of chips with crumbs the front of her shirt and the top of her massive breasts.","She had been heading toward the living room when Dexter emerged from his room.","She stopped.","Dexter stopped.","They stared at each other.","Then Lyra’s gaze shifted to Selene who had just entered their room and then back to Dexter and then behind Dexter, to his open bedroom door, then to the rumpled bed inside.","Her dark eyes blinked behind her glasses as a something suddenly clicked in her mind.","Dexter’s room. Dexter’s bed. Early morning. Selene coming out of Dexter’s room moments ago.","Lyra’s ears instantly turned bright red!","The chip she had been chewing fell out of her open mouth and landed on the floor.","She immediately turned and bolted into the room, the egg and the chip bag clutched tightly against her chest as the door slammed shut behind her.","Dexter stood in the hallway, as he blinked his eyes in confusion at first, then everything came to him as his eyes widened.","\"Lyra, wait, that’s not what happened.\"","He wasn’t able to finish his words when the door clicked shut.","Dexter face palmed himself right there, his expression caught somewhere between exasperation and amusement.","Then he dropped his hand, rubbed his face, and sighed.","’I am never going to hear the end of this, am I?’"]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166 | You’re insufferable","paragraphs":["Defeat is not the worst of failures. Not to have tried is the true failure\" — George Edward Woodberry","’I’ll explain later.’","He shook his head and walked to the kitchen.","Today was an important day.","He had promised Tessa and her father that he would deliver twenty batches of Enchanted Meals to their bakery for sale.","But first, the girls came first.","He pulled out his ingredients and began planning the morning meal.","He had Diamond Rice, the Celestial Spirit Beans and had premium organic rice. He had the Transcendent-Class beast meat, and various Heavenly Treasures sitting in his spatial storage.","None of those would be used for the bakery orders. Those were exclusively for his wives.","The bakery meals would be made from ordinary ingredients.","For the girls’ breakfast, however, he had something special planned.","He reached into his spatial storage and pulled out a small, glowing pill.","The Phoenix Heart Elixir.","He still had three of them. These were Grade-4 Divine Medicines, capable of repairing damaged organs, restoring vitality, and greatly reducing permanent injuries.","The problem was delivery.","He couldn’t simply walk up to the girls and say, \"Here, take this medicine.\" Even though they were beginning to trust him, they weren’t at the level where he could hand them unidentified pills and expect them to swallow without question.","’Lyra would probably take it without asking.’","Dexter chuckled as he thought of the cute girl.","But for Mira and Selene, he needed a subtler approach.","As a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, he possessed the advanced ability to dissolve the concentrated medicinal properties of high-grade pills directly into an Arcane meal.","By doing this, the healing effect would be even increased than consuming the pill directly and all three girls would benefit simultaneously.","He dissolved one Phoenix Heart Elixir into a small vial of warm water, using his heavenly flame to break down the pill’s structure at the molecular level.","Then he began cooking.","He selected the Celestial Kirin Spirit Rice from his recipe collection.","Celestial Kirin Spirit Rice","Improves physical constitution. Removes cultivation impurities. Greatly enhances mana absorption. Increases breakthrough success rate.","He prepared the rice in the Type-II Spirit Cooking Pot, infusing it with carefully balanced herbs and a thin slice of Millennium Blood Ginseng. As the rice simmered, he drizzled the dissolved Phoenix Heart Elixir into the mixture, using his Great Grandmaster technique to weave the medicinal essence evenly throughout the grains.","[Ding! Congratulations! You have successfully created Celestial Kirin Spirit Rice (Grade 5)]","Effect: Permanently heals 25% of all internal injuries. Improves physical constitution. Removes cultivation impurities. Greatly enhances mana absorption. Increases breakthrough success rate.","Dexter nodded in satisfaction.","Twenty-five percent permanent healing was better than the pill alone. The food had amplified the medicine’s effectiveness from twenty percent to twenty-five.","He plated four bowls and carried them to the dining table.","Then he turned around, expecting to see Lyra hovering at the kitchen door, but she wasn’t there.","Dexter blinked and sighed.","’ She’s definitely hiding. She probably thinks Selene and I did something last night.’","He rubbed the bridge of his nose and chuckled quietly.","’I really should explain before her imagination runs even wilder.’","But that would have to wait. Right now, he needed to get everyone fed.","He walked to the bathroom. Lyra and Selene had already finished washing up.","He found Mira sitting in her wheelchair, eyes closed, cultivating. He wheeled her to the bathroom, helped her through her morning routine.","He pulled a clean blouse out and began dressing her. He slid the fabric over her arms, positioned it across her shoulders, and reached behind her back to clasp her bra.","His fingers found the clasp.","And then his eyes flashed.","The Talent Upgrade Cards.","He had received three of them from the system. Three cards capable of raising any talent below C-Rank directly to C-Rank without side effects.","He had been waiting for the perfect opportunity to use them on the girls. But the right moment never seemed to arrive.","But right now, Mira was unguarded and was relaxed, fresh from the bath.","’I should probably do it now.’","Dexter flipped his right hand and a golden card materialized between his fingers.","It was small, roughly the size of a playing card, with a \"C\" engraved on it.","He pressed it against the bare skin of Mira’s back.","Instantly, the card dissolved.","It merged into her skin like a drop of water absorbing into sand, vanishing completely in less than a second.","A faint golden ripple spread outward from the point of contact, racing across her skin before fading.","\"Hmm.\"","Mira groaned softly and her brows furrowed as she felt a slight prickle in her back.","\"Why did you pinch me?\" She tilted her head, glancing at Dexter with the corner of her eyes as she said in irritation.","Dexter finished clasping her bra and walked around to the front of her wheelchair and shrugged","\"I didn’t pinch you. It’s probably a mosquito bite.\"","Mira’s crimson eyes locked onto his face as she gazed intently at him.","\"Mosquito?\"","Dexter nodded innocently. \"Yeah. They are everywhere now. Even daring to feast on you. Tsk tsk tsk...\"","Mira glared at him and said dangerously. \"You’re becoming quite gutsy.\"","Dexter held up both hands in surrender. \"Mosquito. I swear.\"","\"There are no mosquitoes in this house.\"","Dexter blinked. \"They probably came in through the broken window.","Mira’s eyes narrowed further.","But before she could deliver whatever punishment she was planning, Dexter heard a sound.","[Ding!]","Golden text materialized in his vision.","---","Talent Upgrade Successful!","Target: Mira Calloway","Talent: Spectral Arms","Rank: D → C","Talent has evolved successfully.","---","Dexter’s lips curved upward ever so slightly.","’Success.’","With this upgrade, her proficiency should increase vastly and maybe she could create more arms.","’ Two left now.’","He would find the right moments for those too.","For now, he simply smiled at Mira, who was still glaring at him","\"Breakfast is ready,\" he said cheerfully, changing the subject. \"I made Celestial Kirin Spirit Rice. You will like it.\"","He grabbed the handles of her wheelchair and began pushing her toward the kitchen before she could reply.","\"You are insufferable,\" she muttered.","Dexter simply chuckled, then parked her at the dining table and walked to the hallway.","\"Lyra! Selene! Breakfast!\"","A pause.","The door cracked open and a single dark eye appeared in the gap, scanning the hallway cautiously.","\"Come eat,\" Dexter said keeping his inner voice and outer voice neutral and his expression innocent.","Lyra’s eyes narrowed.","Then the door opened fully as Lyra stepped out, holding the Primordial Beast Egg against her chest. Her face was carefully blank, but her ears were still pink.","She walked past Dexter without looking at him, to the dining table and sat down, staring at her bowl of Celestial Kirin Spirit Rice intently."]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167 | When Good Becomes Bad","paragraphs":["Selene also stepped out. Her silver-white hair was neatly brushed and fell over her shoulders in a smooth cascade. Her pale skin was clean and fresh. Her white eyes were aimed at the floor.","She did not look at Dexter.","Not once.","Her ears, however, were a shade of pink that closely matched Lyra’s.","She walked past him quietly, pretending very hard that the last twelve hours had not happened.","Dexter watched her go.","’Well. This is going to be a fun breakfast.’","He walked to the dining table and sat down.","Four people. Four bowls of glowing, golden rice. Three women who were all, for various reasons, refusing to make eye contact with anyone else at the table.","The silence was thick enough to cut with a knife.","Dexter picked up his spoon.","\"Eat up,\" he said. \"It’s good.\"","No one responded.","At that moment, Mira’s seemed to have noticed something as the three of them sat down.","She looked up at Selene and then her gaze shifted to Lyra.","Lyra’s ears were red and she was actively trying g nit to look up.","Then Mira looked at Dexter.","Dexter was calmly and his expression was neutral.","Mira’s crimson eyes narrowed.","\"What happened between the three of you?\" Mira suddenly asked projecting the question to her surface thought.","The question landed on the table like a brick.","Lyra was startled and she immediately dove into her food like it was the most important thing in the world.","Selene didn’t say anything either. She glanced briefly at Mira, and Dexter could have sworn he saw the faintest trace of a smirk on Selene’s lips before it vanished.","But Mira had seen it too.","Mira’s brows furrowed even more as her crimson gaze sharpened, zeroing in on Selene. She had caught that smirk. She knew what it meant. Selene knew something she didn’t, and she was quietly amused about it.","’Did something really happen?’","Mira was beginning to feel slightly annoyed without knowing why as Selene’s behavior irritated her.","She turned her sharp gaze on Dexter.","\"What happened?\"","Dexter shrugged. \"It was just a misunderstanding. That’s all.\"","Mira stared at him, waiting for elaboration but Dexter gave non and simply resumed eating.","Mira’s eye twitched.","She held her glare for a full five seconds, but Dexter didn’t crack.","Mira snorted.","\"Hmph. Fine. Keep your secrets to yourself.\"","She conjured her Spectral Arms. The translucent orange limbs materialized behind her shoulders, reached for her spoon, and resumed feeding herself.","The rest of the meal passed and it was incredibly awkward.","They finished eating.","Dexter collected the bowls and carried them to the sink.","---","\"Knock. Knock.\"","A sharp double-knock echoed from the front gate.","Dexter’s Enhanced Hearing activated automatically and he filtered the surrounding sounds and listened for a heart beat and he immediately knew who it was.","He dried his hands, walked to the front door, and opened the gate.","Tessa stood on the other side.","She was smiling softly like a kid who had just been given a lollipop.","She wore a simple blue dress with a white apron, and she was holding a large transparent bag filled with empty thermo food containers.","\"Good morning!\" she said brightly, her green eyes sparkling. Then she grinned very mischievously.","As she tilted her head letting her hair bounce to the side.","\"Hope I didn’t disturb anything.\" Her voice was innocent but it was obvious she was thinking of another thing.","Dexter looked at the mischievous sparkle in her eyes before lightly flicking her forehead.","\"Quit it, brat.\"","\"Ow!\"","She rubbed her forehead while pouting but her grin returned instantly.","Dexter gestured at the bag of containers. \"I assume these are what you wanted me to use.\"","Tessa nodded rapidly, her curly hair bouncing with each movement. \"Yep! Hen- Dad said to bring them over so you can fill them up. He’s already cleared a shelf in the display case for your meals.\"","Dexter took the bag from her. The containers were clean, sturdy, and came with temperature scaling effect.","\"Alright,\" he said, glancing back at the house. \"I should be done before nine or ten.\"","Tessa blinked. \"That fast?\"","\"It’s just a Grade One meal. Won’t take long.\"","Tessa’s nodded.","\"Alright,\" she said, rocking on her heels. \"I’ll be looking forward to it.\"","But she didn’t leave.","Dexter waited. She continued standing there, her green eyes fixed on him.","He raised an eyebrow. \"Do you need something else?\"","Tessa clasped her hands behind her back and rocked forward onto her toes. \"Can I watch you cook?\"","Dexter was slightly taken aback by the request. Then he smiled, reached out, and gently pushed her forehead with his palm, tilting her back a step.","\"No.\"","He closed the gate.","Tessa stood on the other side, pouting through the iron bars with the wounded expression of a puppy that had been denied a treat.","\"Wicked.\"","Dexter waved a hand over his shoulder without turning around and walked back inside.","---","He found Mira in the living room.","She had wheeled herself to the window with her Spectral Arms.","Even though the window was now boarded up,she still sat there.","But she wasn’t cultivating.","She was staring at him as he came in.","Her expression was indifferent but sharp.","\"I assume that was Tessa,\" she said.","Dexter paused. \"Yeah. How did you know?\"","Mira’s lips curled into a cold sneer. She didn’t answer.","He decided not to press the issue.","\"Right,\" he said, walking past her toward the kitchen. \"I’ll be busy cooking, so let me know if you need anything.\"","Mira said nothing. She simply turned her head back toward the window and closed her eyes.","As Dexter left, Mira opened her eyes as she muttered.","’Interesting.’","---","Dexter placed the containers on the kitchen counter and stood there for a moment, thinking.","The challenge ahead of him was not cooking. Cooking was easy, the challenge was the opposite of cooking.","He had to make his food worse.","As a Great Grandmaster Foodsmith, his natural cooking ability produced Grade Two meals at minimum, even when using ordinary ingredients. The mana infusion happened automatically. His techniques were so refined, that every dish he touched inevitably absorbed and channeled mana beyond the Grade One threshold.","To produce a Grade One meal, he would have to intentionally suppress his skill.","It was, in a strange way, harder than cooking at full power."]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168 | The Food Business","paragraphs":["Dexter had no choice.","This neighborhood was nice but it people here weren’t that rich.","A Grade Two Enchanted Meal would sell for 12,000 to 50,000 dollars per portion. That was a month wages for many families here.","But a Grade One Enchanted Meal? could sell for 3,000 to 10,000 dollars. It was still expensive but some could decide to spend on an arcane meal for its effects.","Dexter rolled up his sleeves, tied his apron, and began pulling ingredients.","Ordinary rice, fresh vegetables, eggs, and the grade 1 arcane meat, soy sauce, ginger, garlic, sesame oil, nothing that would push the meal above Grade One.","He took a deep breath and began cooking but it was hard.","He had to suppress his Heavenly Gastronomy body, stop himself from using heavenly flame and even not even infusing mana into the meal.","He had to suppress all of it.","He cooked with basic techniques instead of using his various Foodsmith techniques.","The containers Tessa had provided were mass-produced thermal boxes. Just well-made disposable containers with basic insulation that could keep food fresh for one to two days.","By 8:54 AM, he was done.","Twenty containers of Grade One Enchanted Meals, neatly packed. Each portion contained a generous serving of vegetable fried rice with seared Berserk Beef, seasoned with ginger and garlic, garnished with green onions.","The aroma was rich and savory but not overwhelming.","Dexter inspected the first container and checked the system notification that appeared.","[Grade One Enchanted Meal — Comfort Chicken Rice]","[Effect: Mana Regeneration c 300%, Strength x 200%, Slight stamina boost. Improved digestion.","[Duration: 3 hours.]","’Perfect!’","He packed all twenty containers into his spatial storage. Then he paused, then ultimately decided to pack extra portions. Tessa had given him thirty containers in total, probably in case any containers turned out faulty.","Twenty for the bakery. Five for his plans.","He packed them separately and stored everything.","Then he turned around.","Two dark eyes stared at him from the kitchen doorway.","’Shit! You almost scared me!’","Lyra was standing there. Her AI glasses sat on her nose as the Primordial Beast Egg was cradled against her left hip.","She had been trying so hard to avoid Dexter all morning, but the aroma from the kitchen had been relentless.","Before she knew it, her feet had carried her to the kitchen without her permission.","She saw Dexter turn to met her and she immediately remembered the morning and her cheeks flushed crimson.","She wanted to leave but the smell was too good.","Dexter calmed his beating heart and smiled.","He pulled a container from his spatial storage and held it out to her.","\"Here. I made this for you.\"","Lyra blinked, looked at him suspiciously but then she slowly went forward and reached for the container.","Her fingers closed around it as she took it but Dexter didn’t let go.","Lyra looked up at him with fluahed checks.","’W–hat?’","Dexter gently stared at her.","\"Nothing happened between me and Selene.\"","Lyra’s eyes widened slightly.","\"I only used my Heavenly Flame to help suppress Selene’s Eternal Winter Ice,\" Dexter continued.","He paused.","\"Do you understand?\"","Lyra held his gaze for a long moment, then she nodded.","’I believe you.’","Her sweet voice rang out in his mind.","Dexter aighed in relief and released his grip on the container.","\"Good.\"","Lyra took it and immediately turned to leave the kitchen.","But before she crossed the door, she suddenly turned back.","\"Even if you were.\"","Her face went even redder.","’I wouldn’t mind.’","’She is also your wife anyway.’","Then Lyra turned and fled the kitchen like a startled rabbit as the door slammed shut a second later.","Dexter stood alone in the kitchen, staring at the empty doorway.","’Even if I was what?’","’Doing what?’","’So she only looks innocent, uhn?’","He shook his head, rubbed his face with both hands, and firmly refused to think about it.","---","He changed into clean clothes into a simple black t-shirt and dark jeans, then walked to the living room.","Mira was in her wheelchair by the boarded-up window. Lyra was at the bedroom and Selene was in the backyard, cultivating.","\"I’m heading out,\" Dexter announced loudly as it echoed through the entire house. \"I’m delivering the meals to Mr. Henry’s bakery today.\"","Mira opened one eye. \"Good luck.\"","Lyra’s voice echoed in his mind.","And he heard Selene muttered at the backyard.","\"Thanks,\" Dexter said as he opened the door and walked out of the house.","Then he turned back and poked his head inside and spoke to Mira.","\"Don’t open the door for anyone.\" he joked.","Mira’s crimson eyes snapped to him with the force of a laser beam.","\"Get, out.\" she hissed.","Dexter grinned, closed the door, and locked it behind him.","---","He stood on the porch for a moment, looking down the street.","Grandma Lucy’s gate was open and he could see her silver hair bobbing above her garden fence as she tended her morning flowers.","Dexter walked over and knocked on her gate three times. But the gate opened before his third knock.","Grandma Lucy stood on the other side, beaming. Her bright eyes crinkled at the corners.","\"Little chef! You’re here early!\"","Dexter smiled and produced a container from his spatial storage. He held it out to her with both hands.","\"Grandma Lucy. I promised you the first taste of my cooking. Here it is.\"","The old woman’s eyes went wide. She took the container with both hands, cradling it as though it were a newborn baby.","\"Oh, you actually remembered!\" She looked down at the container, then back up at Dexter. \"Thank you, Dexter. You’re a truly good kid.\"","Dexter scratched the back of his head. \"I try.\"","Grandma Lucy chuckled. \"Do you want to come inside for a cup of tea?\"","Dexter smiled politely. \"I would love to, but I need to get these meals to Mr. Henry’s bakery as soon as possible. Rain check?\"","\"Of course, of course.\" Grandma Lucy nodded. \"Next time then.\"","\"Next time,\" Dexter agreed.","He waved goodbye and headed down the street toward the bakery.","[A/N: Gimme golden tickets 😭]"]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169 | The Scheme!","paragraphs":["The walk took about five minutes.","When he arrived, he saw the shop was busy this morning.","Several customers stood in line at the counter. Some were regulars picking up their morning order. Others were browsing the pastry selection. A mother with two children was trying to decide between croissants and muffins while the children tugged at her sleeves and pointed at everything.","Behind the counter, Tessa was in her element.","She wore a clean white apron over her blue dress, her curly red hair tied back with a ribbon as she packed pastries into paper bags, making change, calling out order numbers, and chatting with customers all at the same time.","The moment Tessa saw Dexter walk through the door, her face lit up.","She turned to the older man beside her. \"Take over the register for a second.\"","Then she ducked under the counter and hurried over to Dexter, her curly hair bouncing.","\"Hey, Dexter!\" She grinned. \"You’re here earlier than I expected.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Yeah. Cooking didn’t take as long as I thought.\"","He raised both hands. In each hand, he held a large bag containing ten sealed containers.","\"I came to deliver the items,\" he said, glancing around the busy shop. \"Though I have to be honest. I’m worried.\"","Tessa raised an eyebrow. \"Worried about what?\"","Dexter lowered his voice slightly. \"No one in their right mind is going to spend 5,000 Dollars on a meal made by a stranger without a reputation. \"","Tessa shook her head slowly.","\"You truly do underestimate the people in this neighborhood.\"","She crossed her arms and leaned against one foot as she smirked.","\"Some people here are not as simple as you think, Dexter. You’re always indoors. Apart from me and Grandma Lucy, you don’t know anyone. You should get to know them.\" She tilted her head, a small smile playing on her lips. \"I think they’d like you.\"","Dexter raised an eye brow but shrugged.","\"Maybe I should.\"","Tessa’s smile widened.","\"Come on,\" she said, taking one of the bags from his hand. \"Let’s get these in the display case. Hen- Dad cleared a shelf specifically for your meals.\"","She led him behind the counter, past the ovens, to a large glass display case near the front window.","A small handwritten sign sat on the empty shelf.","\"Arcane Meals— Fresh Daily — Made by A Master Foodsmith.\"","\"6000 dollars per Portion.\"","\"6000?\" he asked. \"I was thinking 5000 first to gauge the reactions of customers.\"","Tessa shrugged. \"Henry and I discussed it. If we stuck to 5000 which is the lowest, people won’t want to purchase something so low. But 6,000 will make them curious. And once word spreads about the effects and taste...\" She grinned. \"We’ll sell out by noon.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow. \"That confident?\"","Tessa placed the first container on the shelf with a click.","\"Let me put it this way,\" she said. \"There’s a retired hero two streets over who can’t cultivate anymore because of a broken sternum. There’s a woman on Steering Street whose son has a competition in a week. And also a construction worker who comes home exhausted and barely have time to cultivate.\"","She placed the second container beside the first.","\"None of them can afford Nexus cores, but a Grade One Enchanted Meal that costs 6000 dollars that increases their cultivation speed is within their means.","Dexter was surprised by Tessa’s intelligence and nodded his head.","Dexter rolled his eyes.","\"You’re pretty smart for one so young.\" he said as he turned around to leave.","Tessa’s lips curled upward. \"Oh, I’m young, am I? I look really young, don’t I?\"","Dexter glanced at her from the corner of his eye. \"Obviously.\"","Then he stopped and raised an eyebrow rose.","\"Why aren’t you in school today?\"","He paused for a beat then chuckled.","\"Forget it. I know you’ll give another excuse again.\"","Tessa’s innocent smile widened until her dimples showed. \"I actually have a really good excuse this time. Don’t you want to hear it?\"","Dexter held up a hand. \"Save it. I’m good.\"","Tessa chuckled behind him as he pushed open the bakery door and stepped out onto the sidewalk.","He waved once without turning around. \"Bye, Tessa. Thanks.\"","\"Bye, Dexter! Good luck!\"","---","Dexter had intended to greet Mr. Henry before leaving, but the man hadn’t been in the shop. Only Tessa and a couple of part-time helpers were behind the counter. He figured Mr. Henry must have stepped out for something and decided not to linger.","But as it turned out, he didn’t have to wait long.","He was halfway when he saw a familiar broad-shouldered figure walking toward the bakery from the opposite direction. Mr. Henry was carrying holding a large bag in his grip.","The man’s face was expressionless as always.","Dexter stopped and waited.","When Mr. Henry’s eyes landed on him, recognition flickered in his eyes and he spoke.","\"I assume you came to drop off the Arcane Meals.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Yes, twenty portions. Tessa’s already got them in the display case.\"","Mr. Henry studied him for a moment then smiled.","\"Alright. Let’s see how today goes.\"","Dexter smiled and produced a single container from his spatial storage. He held it out to Mr. Henry with both hands.","\"This is for you.\"","Mr. Henry blinked as he looked at the container, then at Dexter.","\"For me?\"","Dexter nodded. \"Yeah. This is my way of showing appreciation for letting me sell the food at your place.\"","Mr. Henry stared at him for a long moment. Then a low chuckle rumbled from his chest.","\"You’re quite the schemer, aren’t you?\"","Dexter smiled innocently. \"I have no idea what you’re talking about.\"","Mr. Henry shook his head, still chuckling as he took the container with his free hand.","\"Forget it.\"","\"Thank you, sir,\" Dexter replied, stepping aside to let the man pass.","Mr. Henry walked past him and pushed open the bakery door. Before it closed behind him, Dexter caught one last glimpse of the man shaking his head with a quiet grin.","He understood exactly why Mr. Henry had called him a schemer. And the man wasn’t wrong.","The truth was that they had never discussed profit sharing. When Tessa had proposed the arrangement, she had talked about selling his meals in the bakery. She hadn’t mentioned a commission.","And in the absence of an explicit agreement, the default assumption in any business relationship was that the seller took a cut. Ten percent, twenty percent, thirty percent of whatever the market bore.","If the meals sold well, Mr. Henry would naturally expect a portion of the profits for providing the storefront, the customer base, and the display space. And he would have been entirely justified in asking for it.","But by giving Mr. Henry a free meal, thanking him for letting him sell his stuffs in his bakery for free, Dexter had created an unspoken agreement and accepting a gift created obligation. By accepting the container, Mr. Henry had implicitly accepted the terms that Dexter had set without ever stating them aloud.","No commission or profit sharing.","The bakery would sell his food for free. Dexter would keep every credit.","Dexter had spent 19 years in the Ashford estate. He had been cheated, shortchanged, manipulated, and exploited by servants, strangers and mostly relatives and had learnt a thing or two."]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170 | Shadow Sylve Syndicate","paragraphs":["The hardware store was a fifteen-minute drive from the bakery.","Dexter parked the SUV in the small lot beside the building and walked inside. The store was a large, warehouse-style space with high ceilings, concrete floors, and rows of shelving stocked with everything from lumber to plumbing supplies.","He found the window section after a few minutes of searching.","The damage Rosalind had caused was significant. The entire window frame had been blown out along with a portion of the surrounding wall. He needed a new frame, new glass panels, insulation, exterior trim, drywall for the interior wall repair, and the appropriate fasteners and sealant.","He did the math as he walked through the aisles, loading items onto a flat cart.","New window frame, standard size.","Double-paned tempered glass panel, interior drywall sheet, insulation roll, exterior trim and caulking.","Fasteners, sealant, and miscellaneous hardware.","Total was approximately 2200 dollars.","He loaded everything onto the cart, paid at the register, and transferred the entire load into his spatial storage.","Dexter had just climbed back into the SUV and started the engine when his phone suddenly rang out.","He pulled the phone from his pocket and glanced at the screen.","[Unknown number]","’Is it Rachel?’","He frowned slightly.","He had saved Rachel’s number after her text so it definitely wasn’t her. Also, he hadn’t given his contact information to anyone else. Not even Tessa or Mr. Henry.","He stared at the ringing phone for a few seconds then shrugged and answered it.","\"Hello?\"","A somehow familiar voice came through the speaker.","\"Hello. Is this Mr. Dexter?\"","...","Deep West of Stargate City, existed a forest that most citizens knew only by name.","The Green Rim Forest. One of the many dangerous forests in all of Stargate city","From above, if one were to look over with a bird eye view, one would see an unbroken expanse of green.","Endless canopies of ancient trees that is dense and tall that their branches wove together, blocking all sunlight from reaching the forest ground.","But inside the forest was dangerous and dark.","The official explanation, maintained by the Hero Association, was that the Green Rim Forest was not fully explored and populated by monsters of various ranks, with rumors of Transcendent-tier beasts lurking in its deepest reaches.","Adventurers who ventured inside rarely returned.","The Hero Association had long since classified the forest as a Restricted Zone and thepublic accepted this without question.","After all, who would want to venture into a forest full of monsters?","Deep within the forest, in the expanse of green, if you looked with the eyes of a Legendary Hero, would actually see that at the center of the forest was actually a formation.","The moment one pierced through the illusion, there was a mini modern city, nestled in the heart of the forest and there were people in dark purple cloak walking about the street.","And at the center of this mini city was a massive skyscraper. It was impossibly tall, its peak vanishing into the low-hanging clouds.","This was the central stronghold of the Shadow Sylve Syndicate.","The most feared criminal organization in Stargate City. A collective of villains, assassins, information brokers, who operated outside of the law.","They did not seek power, or crave territory or political influence. They dealt in something far more valuable.","Death and money.","Money in exchange for the death of an individual, no matter who the person was.","The Hero Association had attempted to infiltrate Shadow Sylve seventeen times over the past decade.","None of the operatives sent in had ever returned.","---","At the very top of the skyscraper, on the highest floor, a man stood alone.","The office was sparse, with a single desk at the edge and a chair was pushed behind it.","The stood at the open balcony and there was no glass separating him from the outside world as the cold wind poured freely into the place.","His black coat fluttered behind him with his hands folded behind his back.","The man was middle-aged that looked between 45 to 50. He had dark hair and a single eye. A scar ran across his left eye.","\"Tsss!\"","A door behind him slid open and two shadowy figure dressed in dark violet cloak walked in","The hoods were drawn up, casting their faces in shadow. Only their jaws were visible as they stopped twenty meters behind the scarred man.","They immediately bowed their heads and remained still as silence filled the office.","The scarred man’s coat fluttered and the two cloaked figures stood motionless, heads bowed, waiting.","Ten minutes passed when the scarred man finally spoke.","\"Did you get in contact with the leader?\"","The two cloaked figures exchanged a glance beneath their hoods and the one on the left, slightly taller than the other, straightened and answered.","\"No. We were unable to get in contact with the leader.\"","He immediately continued.","\"We came across unexpected trouble.\"","The scarred man’s head tilted slightly.","\"Unexpected trouble,\" he repeated.","\"The entire house seemed to be protected by a high-level formation,\" the cloaked figure continued. \"We attempted to approach from multiple angles. But every vector was blocked. The formation activated the moment we crossed the perimeter and repelled us before we could reach the structure. Breaking it also seemed impossible.\"","The scarred man was quiet for a moment.","\"Oh?\" The man said in a slightly surprised tone.","\"A high-level formation. In a neighborhood like that?\"","He turned his head slightly more. His single dark eye shifted toward the two cloaked figures, though his body remained facing the balcony.","\"So you were unable to pierce through the formation?\"","The second cloaked figure spoke. His voice was rougher than the first. Lower.","\"The formation’s threshold appeared to be Transcendent Level. Anyone below that realm was automatically repelled. We tested it three times from different positions. Same result each time.\" He paused. \"Unless you or one of the elders personally makes a move, we are unable to break through that formation.\"","The scarred man remains silent as his eye remained fixed on the two figures behind him.","Then he asked a different question.","\"Were you able to see her?\""]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171 | Calloway Residence","paragraphs":["The first cloaked figure nodded.","\"Yes. But only a glimpse. She was inside the house, near a window. We observed her for approximately twelve seconds before she went out of view.\"","A pause.","\"She appears to still be ill. The amnesia is still present. Otherwise, that bastard fellow would have been long dead.\"","The scarred man’s expression didn’t change. But something shifted in the air around him as a pressure emanated from him.","The scarred man exhaled.","\"It’s already been long enough.\" He muttered to himself then, he moved his right hand from behind his back.","With a single, fluid motion, he flipped his palm upward. A translucent stone materialized above his hand. It was small, roughly the size of a marble, and perfectly spherical. Its surface was pale blue and faintly luminous, with thin veins of silver running through its interior like frozen lightning.","A Soul Stone.","A rare and extraordinarily expensive treasure designed to increase one’s soul strength.","The scarred man held the stone between his fingers then, without turning around, he flicked it backward.","The stone shot through the air through the air.","The first cloaked figure caught it without hesitation.","\"It is not convenient for me to go there personally right now,\" the scarred man said. \"The situation is delicate. Too many eyes and too many parties involved. If I make a move, it will be noticed. So you will do this instead.\"","He turned fully now, for the first time since the two figures had entered.","\"Take the Soul Stone, watch the house and wait for an opportunity.\"","\"She will not be holed up in that house forever. She will come out eventually. When she does, and when she is alone, you approach.\"","The two cloaked figures listened attentively.","\"Place the Soul Stone on her forehead. It should be able to help her recover some of her memories. Once her memories begin to return, she will understand who she is and what needs to be done next.\"","He looked directly at the taller of the two figures.","\"If she doesn’t remember and refuses...\"","He said nothing more.","They nodded their heads in understanding.","...","The Calloway family residence was an empire unto itself.","The Calloway Estate occupied a massive tract of prime real estate in the eastern quarter of Stargate City, surrounded by walls of reinforced white stone that stretched nearly a kilometer in each direction. The perimeter was patrolled by hired heroes in Calloway livery.","Anti-intrusion formations were layered into the walls themselves, invisible to the naked eye but deadly to anyone foolish enough to test them.","Inside the walls, the estate was a self-contained world. Manicured gardens, training grounds, barracks for the family’s private military force and various other buildings.","And at the center of it all, rising above everything else like a crown, sat the Calloway Mansion.","The mansion was enormous. Three stories, with sweeping balconies, tall arched windows, and a grand entrance framed by pillars carved with the Calloway family crest.","This was the seat of the fifth most influential family in Stargate City.","And it was here, in the private study on the second floor, that the current head of the Calloway family sat at his desk and signed documents.","---","The study was large but understated. Dark wood shelves lined three walls, filled with leather-bound ledgers, cultivation manuals, and historical texts. A single window behind the desk offered a view of the central garden, where ancient maple trees cast long shadows across lawn.","The man behind the desk was handsome, sharp features, strong jaw and high cheekbones.","His hair was a deep, burnished red, darker than Rosalind’s copper-orange but lighter than Mira’s blood-crimson, tied back neatly in a low tail that hung past his collar.","A pair of thin gold-framed reading glasses sat on the bridge of his nose.","He looked to be in his mid-forties but he was, in fact, fifty-three.","The pen never paused as he signed various documents, his eyes scanned each page in the few seconds it took to sign, absorbing the contents with speed.","Suddenly, the door to the study opened but Victor Calloway didn’t look up and simply continued signing.","He signed three more documents, then he set his pen down, removed his glasses, and looked up.","There, Rosalind stood in front of his desk.","She stood with her hands folded before her but her eyes were blazing with fury so intense it seemed to heat the air between them. And at the corner of her mouth, was a trace of blood.","She hadn’t wiped it off and had left it there deliberately, so he would see it.","Victor looked at the blood.","Then at her eyes.","\"What happened?\"","Rosalind’s jaw clenched and she took a breath through her nose as she spoke like a brat reporting to their parent.","\"Mira happened.\"","Victor’s brow furrowed.","\"Explain.\"","Rosalind explained.","She told him everything. The visit to the bungalow. The bastard husband who had disrespected her at the gate. The sheer audacity of a man with no name, no status, and no power ordering her around as though she were a servant.","She told him about Mira’s refusal. The Phoenix Flare Flower offer. And Mira’s flat rejection of everything.","\"She refused to beg,\" Rosalind said, her voice tight with disbelief. \"She refused to even consider it. She said she didn’t need it. She told me to get out.\"","Victor’s expression didn’t change.","Rosalind continued.","\"And then she attacked me.\"","The room went very still.","Victor’s pen, which he had been idling rolling between his fingers, stopped.","\"She what?\"","\"She attacked me,\" Rosalind repeated. \"Actually using Crimson Demoness techniques against her own sister. She’s grown even more disrespectful after living a while with that batard! Hmph!\"","She touched the corner of her mouth where the blood had dried.","Silence.","Victor stared at his daughter with a blank expression on his gaze.","\"Has she repaired her meridians?\" he asked quietly.","Rosalind nodded. \"Yes. Definitely. She was mid-session when I arrived. I caught her meditating, pulling mana into her body before she stopped.\"","Silence.","Then—","Victor Calloway threw his head back and laughed.","\"Hahahaha!\""]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172 | Strange Family Tradition","paragraphs":["\"Hahahaha!\"","Rosalind stared at her father in shock as his laughte rumbled through the entire study.","\"This is excellent,\" Victor stood up as a hearty laughter bubbled in his chest.\"This is great news.\"","He walked out from behind the desk happily with his hands clasped behind his back.","\"I knew she wouldn’t disappoint me,\" he said with pride.","He stopped at the window and looked out at the garden.","\"To think she restored her meridians without relying on our family.\" He turned back to Rosalind, his eyes bright. \"This is even better than I expected.\"","Rosalind’s face changed.","Her father had doted on her after Mira’s accident and she had received her fathers unconditional support for the past three years so she had expected her father to be furious that Mira had attacked his eldest daughter.","Instead, he was celebrating.","Her eyes flashed coldly as she immediately spoke.","\"Father,\" she said carefully, \"I asked her to come with me, told her about the Phoenix Flare Flower and the arrangement with Crowley.\"","\"She said over her dead body.\"","Victor’s expression shifted slightly.","\"She doesn’t want anything to do with the Calloway family. She said since she’s married to the Ashford, she is no longer a Calloway and belongs to someone else.\"","The words landed in the study like stones dropped into still water.","Victor’s face instantly ardened.","The pride faded and smile in his face faded as his face filed cold.","He remembered the contract.","The Death God Contract.","The ironclad, soul-binding agreement that the Calloway, Vance, Frost, and Ashford families had all signed. The contract that had been designed to trap the Ashfords but...","Recollecting this bad memory, Victor’s fist clenched as he slammed it against the deck!","\"BANG!\"","The desk cracked as spiderweb of fractures spread outward from the point of impact, splitting the polished wood surface.","Victor’s hair literally ignited into actual flames. Thin tongues of fire licked along the strands. The temperature in the room spiked. The edges of the nearest documents began to curl and brown.","His eyes blazed with the same fire, the Calloway family’s signature Crimson Flame talent, activating involuntarily under the pressure of his fury.","\"Those Ashford snakes,\" he growled through clenched teeth.","\"Actually managing to deceive us. Twice.\"","His burning gaze fixed on the far wall as though he could see through it, through the city, all the way to the Ashford family estate on the other side of Stargate City.","\"First, crippling the most talented person our family has produced in a thousand years. And we let them convince us it was an accident.\"","\"And then, deceiving us into marrying our daughters to a bastard, a damned nobody. Keeping it secret until the contract was signed and sealed with a Death God oath. Bullying all three of us just because they are stronger and possess more resources.\"","He slammed his fist on the desk again. The cracks widened as the desk groaned.","\"This will not stand.\"","He took a step forward as his hair blazed brighter.","\"There will come a day when we all come together and...\"","He stopped as his eyes flicked to Rosalind. He has almsot let out their plan in front of his daughter.","Victor inhaled deeply and exhaled. The flames in his hair dimmed and then died.","He straightened his posture. Adjusted his cuffs. Picked up his fallen glasses and placed them back on his nose, ignoring the crack that now ran across one lens.","\"The contract will still stand,\" he said flatly. \"There is no way we can possibly break it. Not without triggering the Death God penalty. Even my death won’t break it. The curse would simply transfer to the next Calloway family head. And I will not condemn my successor to that fate.\"","He walked back to the desk, looked down at the cracked surface and smoothed a wrinkled document with his palm.","\"But we cannot personally bring Mira to come back. The contract forbids it. Any direct action by the family to reclaim Mira would constitute a breach.\"","He paused as his eyes narrowed.","\"However, there is no rule that says she can’t come in her own or a third party cannot coerce her.\"","He looked up at Rosalind.","\"Set a meeting with Crowley Montclair.\"","Rosalind blinked. \"Crowley?\"","Victor’s lips curved into a thin, cold smile. \"It’s high time we met and strategized.\"","He leaned against the edge of his cracked desk, folding his arms.","\"Once the news of Mira’s recovery spreads, the Montclair family will be very interested. Crowley was engaged to her before the incident. The engagement was broken when she was crippled. But now that she’s healed...\"","He let the implication speak for itself.","\"Doesn’t he love Mira?\" Victor’s smile widened, but there was no warmth in it. \"Let’s see what he’s willing to do now that she has recovered.\"","He turned and looked out the window again. The garden was peaceful. The maple trees swayed gently in the afternoon breeze. Somewhere in the distance, a child was laughing.","\"Set the meeting, Rosalind.\"","Rosalind bowed her head.","\"Yes, Father.\"","She tuned and left the study as the door closed behind her.","Victor Calloway stood alone in his cracked study, and smiled.","’Mira, you think you can escape us by hiding behind a bastard and a broken contract.’","’You are wrong.’","’You will come home, one way or the other and perform the family tradition.’","A faint sinister smile spread across his face making one think about the trauma Mira had faced in the hands of her father.","...","Dexter picked up the phone.","\"Who is this?\"","A faintly familiar came through the phone.","\"Is this Dexter Ashford?\"","Dexter frowned slightly. \"Who is this?\" he repeated.","The person on the other end cleared his throat.","\"This is Cole. Cole Stanley. You might know me as Plasmatic Man.\"","Dexter’s frown deepened for a moment. The name Cole Stanley meant nothing to him. But Plasmatic Man...","Then it clicked.","The monster outbreak. He had fought alongside several of them in the chaos.","\"Plasmatic Man,\" Dexter said. \"I remember now. You’re the one who killed most of the monsters.\""]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173 | A Call & Thoughts Of Buying A House","paragraphs":["Cole laughed quickly on the other end. \"No, no, no, without your help, it would have been impossible for any of us to even get into position. If you hadn’t been there, I and the other heroes would have been dead. I wanted to call personally and say thank you.\"","Dexter smiled. \"It’s no big deal. You’re a hero, I’m a hero, saving each other and protecting civilians is larr of the job.\"","Cole chuckled. \"You’re quite modest. But whether it’s our duty or not, I still have to say thank you, sincerely.\"","\"You’re welcome,\" Dexter said.","Cole paused for a bit and then spoke again.","\"I’m sorry if this question is too personal but do you happen to have a Hunter party squad?\"","Dexter blinked.","He didn’t have a squad yet and hadn’t asked the Hero Association to assemble one for him as he was too busy with his wives, his system and his cultivation.","He had no idea whether it would become stable enough to support him in the long term.","And while the bakery partnership with Tessa and Mr. Henry would provide one source of income, relying on a single revenue stream was risky. Especially when that revenue stream depended on his time, his energy, and his ability to cook meals that people wanted to buy.","Dungeon raiding was the other obvious option. Nexus cores, monster materials, rare drops. A single successful mid-rank dungeon run could yield more money than a week of food sales.","Combining the two together was the goal. Bakery sales for steady, reliable cash. Dungeon raiding for larger, periodic windfalls and cultivation resources.","With both, he could properly provide for his wives.","Maybe, eventually, enough to buy a piece of land somewhere far from the city. Far from the Ashfords, the Calloways, the Vances, the Frosts, thw Montclairs and everyone else who wanted to use his family as a pawn in their games.","A quiet place and safe place. Where he could properly take care of his wives.","\"No,\" Dexter said. \"I don’t have a squad yet.\"","He could almost hear Cole smiling through the phone.","\"Perfect.\"","Dexter raised an eyebrow at the enthusiasm.","\"How about a get-together tomorrow?\" Cole said. \"Me, you, and a few of the other heroes who fought alongside us that day. Just a chance to get to know each other. Figure out what we’re each good at and what we’re terrible at.\"","He paused.","\"Then maybe, if everyone clicks, we head over to the Titan Training Center, run some tactical drills. Test our teamwork in a controlled environment. See if we’re compatible as a squad before we commit to anything serious.\"","Dexter pondered the offer.","Tomorrow.","He didn’t have a clear picture of his schedule for the next day. The bakery sales would need monitoring. The girls needed care and also, the window needed repairing.","Selene’s nighttime cultivation arrangement was still new.","And there was always the possibility that another unannounced visitor would show up at his gate.","But those were all variables he could manage. A few hours away from the house wasn’t unreasonable, especially with the Type-5 House Protection Talisman active and the girls’ cultivation progressing steadily.","\"What time?\" he asked.","\"Any time your schedule is free,\" Cole said. \"We know you’re married, and we know married life comes with its own set of responsibilities. Most of us aren’t married, so we don’t have the same constraints. But you do. So it’s entirely up to you. We’ll work around your availability.\"","Dexter was quiet for a moment.","\"I’m not sure about my schedule tomorrow,\" he said. \"Let me get back to you. I’ll text you with the details once I’ve sorted things out.\"","Cole chuckled. \"That’s the best case scenario, actually. Take your time. We’ll be ready whenever you are.\"","\"Thanks for reaching out,\" Dexter said.","\"No, thank you,\" Cole replied. \"For saving us. And for picking up the phone.\"","The call ended.","Dexter lowered the phone and stood there for a moment, deep in thought.","A squad.","It wasn’t something he had actively considered before. The idea of joining a team, of trusting other people with his safety in a dungeon environment, hadn’t crossed his mind.","But Cole was right. If he wanted to enter a dungeon in the future, he needed a squad for it.","And it would be best if it was people he knew, rather than been randomly assigned a squad by the Hero Association.","He pocketed his phone, walked around the corner of the building into a narrow alley where no one was watching, and flipped his hand.","The SUV materialized in front of him with a soft thump. He opened the door, climbed in, and started the engine.","---","The drive into the city took twenty minutes.","He found a hardware supply warehouse in the mid-district that carried everything he needed.","A new window frame.","Double-paned tempered glass panel, Interior drywall sheet, Insulation roll, exterior trim, caulking, and weatherproofing sealant.","Fasteners, brackets, and miscellaneous hardware. Everything totaled at about 2000 dollars.","He paid at the counter, loaded everything into his spatial storage in the parking lot, and climbed back into the SUV.","---","The drive home took him through the commercial district, past the towering glass buildings and large billboards that lined the main highway.","He wasn’t paying much attention to the large advertisements by the aid when the road.","However, one particular billboard caught his eye.","It had the image of a smiling hero in casual clothes who stood in front of a modern two-story house with a small garden and a white picket fence.","Beneath the image was a large stylized text","\"HARVEST HOMES — A Comfortable House for You and Your Family\"","\"Because Heroes Deserve a Place to Come Home To\"","Below that, in smaller print: \"Flexible Payment Plans Available for Licensed Heroes. Visit any Harvest Homes branch for details.\"","Dexter only glanced at it. His eyes lingered for perhaps two seconds before returning to the road.","But as he read the texts, an idea started forming in his head.","Buying a house. A real house with four rooms and in a nice neighborhood too.","The idea began to grow, feeding on the accumulated stress and worry of the past three weeks.","Two monster outbreaks had occurred within walking distance of his bungalow. The first had been in his own neighborhood and the second had been at the market district, less than five minutes away.","Two outbreaks in a month. In the same general area was enough for anyone to flee immediately.","Either way, staying in that neighborhood was a risk.","A risk he didn’t need to take since he had a bit of money right now.","While he was already getting used to the neighborhood and he liked Tessa, Mr. Henry and Grandma Lucy, liking a neighborhood and being safe in a neighborhood were two very different things.","And to him, the safety of his wives came first.","’Surely, one million dollars should be enough to purchase a house right?...’"]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174 | Strange Diary...","paragraphs":["\"Ding!\"","Dexter’s phone rang and he caught a glimpse of the message.","It was credit apart and from the hero association.","[Bank Account: $1,200,556]","Dexter immediately smiled. \"Perfect.\"","The payment for his official promotion and licensing had finally arrived.","\"1.2 million should be enough to purchase a house, right?\" he muttered, glancing at the billboard photo on his phone.","The idea continued to grow.","By the time he pulled up in front of his bungalow, it had evolved from a vague notion into a genuine plan and a goal he could look forward too.","’And maybe while I’m at it, I should also change my surname.’","Dexter arrived at the front of his bungalow. He parked the car and climbed out.","There were a few people walking around the neighborhood.","Dexter smiled and nodded at a few and they actually smiled and waved back at him which took him by surprise.","’When did they suddenly become nice?’","He shook his head and opened the gate, retrieving the construction materials from his spatial storage and stacking the window frame, glass panel, drywall, insulation, trim, and tool bag neatly against the exterior wall.","Then he walked to the front door, unlocked it, stepped inside, and closed it behind him.","\"I’m home,\" he called out.","Mira was in her wheelchair by the boarded-up window with her eyes were closed, cultivating.","Lyra was on the couch with her legs were crossed beneath her in a meditation posture.","The Primordial Beast Egg rested in her lap with the AI glasses on her face.","Her eyes were closed which meant she was cultivating as well, but the moment Dexter’s voice reached her AI glasses, it vibrated and Lyra opened her eyes.","She frowned confusion at first, then turned her head to the door.","A faint smile touched her lips and she raised one hand from the egg and waved.","’Welcome back.’","Her cute voice rang out in his mind. Dexter smiled. \"Thank you.\"","He looked at Mira but she hadn’t moved bro had she opened her eyes or acknowledged his existence in any way.","He smirked and considered saying something but he decided against it and walked to the front window and began removing the wooden planks he had nailed up the day before.","Sunlight poured through the empty window frame suddenly, slamming directly against Mira’s face, bathing her closed eyelids in warm, golden light.","Mira’s face scrunched up in a frown as she opened her eyes.","She squinted against the brightness, her crimson irises contracting to pinpoints.","Through the sun ray, she saw Dexter standing in front of the window with a pry bar in one hand and a wooden plank in the other.","He was looking down at her smiling.","’ Since you’re pretending not here, how about now?’","Mira glared at him.","But dexter simply smiled as he pulled the last plank free and set it aside.","Mira’s Spectral Arms appeared behind her as one of them reached for the wheel of her chair.","Then with astonishing proficiency, she wheeled herself backward, away from the window, and away from Dexter’s insufferable grin.","\"Hmph!\"","She snorted and moved her self to the far edge of the living room, turning her back to him.","Dexter chuckled.","’Finally got a reaction out of her.’","---","He spent the next hour repairing the window.","Removing the damaged frame, cleaned the opening, installed the new frame with fresh fasteners, fitted the tempered glass panel into place, and sealed the edges with weatherproof caulking.","He patched the interior wall with new drywall, taped and mudded the seams, and applied a quick coat of paint that matched the surrounding wall.","When he was done, the window looked even better than before.","He was cleaning up his tools when a thought struck him.","’The beds and the weapons.’","All three girls were out of the bedroom.","Mira was in the dining room, Lyra was on the couch and Selene was in the backyard.","Right now, their bedroom was empty.","Which meant he could finally change the beds.","He had been meaning to do this for days but one of them were always in the room or it slipped his mind but now, he could change them.","He walked to the bedroom and pushed the door open.","The room wasn’t very large but it was enough to fit the three beds.","This was one of the reasons he wanted to change their place.","The three girls can’t possible live in one room forever. They would need their own personal space to do their own thing.","Lyra’s weapon was on her bed.","Mira’s weapon was on the stand beside her bed and Selene’s weapon was on the dresser.","Dexter flipped his hand and Three Type-6 weapons materialized on the bed in front of him.","He immediately swapped them, replacing each Type-3 weapon with its upgraded Type-6 counterpart in the exact same position.","The Type-6 versions looked similar to their predecessors at a glance.","Same general shape, basic design but the mana density radiating from them was orders of magnitude higher.","If any of the girls picked up their weapon and channeled even a thread of mana into it, they would immediately feel the difference.","’That would be for later.’","Now the beds.","He pulled the first mattress off the frame and leaned it against the wall. He retrieved the new mattress from his spatial storage.","He positioned the first new mattress on the frame, fitted it with fresh sheets and a new pillow, and moved to the second bed and repeated the exact same thing.","Then he moved to the third bed.","It sas Lyra’s. The sheets were wrinkled and slightly greasy from the chips she ate while cultivating. He gathered the corners of the fitted sheet and pulled it free from the mattress.","\"Thump!\"","Something fell.","It dropped from inside the folded sheet.","\"Uhn?\"","Dexter set the sheet aside and looked down.","What was on the floor was a book. The book was much thicker than a normal book with leather cover and no printed words.","’A diary?’","As it fell, it had open to a page near the middle.","Dexter picked it up and his eyes landed on the first few lines. His brows instantly furrowed and his eyes widened slightly."]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175 | Strange Reaction...","paragraphs":["Dexter raised an eyebrow.","He didn’t know Lyra had a diary.","He looked at the open page and unconsciously read the first few lines.","\" My time is growing shorter and shorter. Can’t live as a cripple anymore, might as well let her in. It’s the same as death.\"","Dexter frowned.","The words were strange.","’ Letting her in?’","What did that mean?","His curiosity was stirred, reaching its peak and he wanted to read more but his conscience pressed back just as hard.","It was someone else’s diary which contained detailed private thoughts most likely containing types of snacks she loved.","But reading them without her permission wouldn’t be nice and was a complete disregard of privacy. He slaps wouldn’t want someone prying into his thoughts either.","So he sighed and immediately closed the diary.","He lifted the edge of the new mattress, intending to slide the diary back underneath where it had fallen, when a chilling voice rang out behind him.","’ What are you doing with my stuff?’","The voice was incredibly cold and icy. Dexter even felt his skin prickle with danger and his brows furrowed.","Dexter immediately turned around only to see Lyra standing in the doorway.","She was not wearing her AI glasses as her dark eyes locked onto Dexter like a predator looking at a prey.","Her expression was flat and indifferent, her eyes, cold and dearly.","Dexter’s was at first stunned by Lyra’s sudden change in behavior and he thought about various lies to tell.","But he ultimately decided to tell the truth.","\"I swapped your bed for a better one,\" he said, holding up the diary. \"I was changing the sheets and this fell out. I assume it’s yours.\"","Lyra’s face didn’t change.","Dexter frowned. Lyra at this moment looked extremely unfamiliar.","Lyra glanced at the diary in his hand, then at Dexter as she began walking slowly towards him.","\"Tap.\" \"Tap.\" \"Tap.\"","Her feet barely making any noise on the ground as she stopped three feet away from him and tilted her head slightly, studying his face like a cat studying a mouse.","’ Do you know the saying about the cat and curiosity? ’ she asked.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed, something was wrong.","The voice sounded like Lyra, but it was different.","Dexter didn’t respond immediately. He stared at Lyra, searching her face for something.","His frown deepened.","\"I assume this is your diary,\" he said carefully.","Lyra continued to look at his face.","’ Hm. You look quite different from the first time.’","Dexter blinked. \"What do you mean?\"","Lyra’s eyes suddenly widened slightly as something similar to confusion flickered across her face before it vanished.","The with speed that surprised even Dexter, she snatched the diary from his hand.","’ Don’t ever touch my stuff, ’ she said with a smile and in a soft voice but that voice was even sharper and deadlier than Mira’s angriest voice.","Dexter remained silent, still feeling strange about Lyra’s sudden behavior.","But then again, he reasoned, if someone had touched his diary without permission, he would have been angry too.","It was an honest mistake on his part, but it was still a violation of her privacy. Her reaction, while unusually intense, was not unreasonable.","He nodded. \"I won’t. I’m sorry. It was an honest mistake.\"","Lyra stared at him for a long, cold moment.","’ Get out. ’ she said.","Dexter’s frown deepened. The tone was harsher than anything Lyra had ever directed at him. Not even in the early days, when all three women had treated him with cold indifference, had Lyra used that tone.","He considered saying something but inhaled deeply and walked out of the room.","---","He stood in the hallway for a moment, processing what had just happened.","’ She was angry. That’s fine. People get angry when their privacy is violated. I would be too.’","But the voice and the words with the way she looked at him.","\"You look quite different from the first time.\"","What did that mean? Different from the first time how?","Dexter’s thoughts drifted to something the system had told him.","’ Shadow Corruption.’","The system had warned that Lyra’s talent was beginning to corrupt her physical cells. If the corruption reached 100%, her body would collapse and transform into a permanent portal to the Shadow Realm.","He immediately opened his system interface and navigated to Lyra’s status panel.","[Name: Lyra Vance]","[Shadow Corruption Level: 2%]","Dexter exhaled slowly.","’ So it’s not the corruption, the foodie Lyra is actually this scary when she’s angry.’","He shook his head and walked to the living room to continue repairing the window.","---","The rest of the morning passed in silence.","Dexter finished the window repair.","He massaged Mira while maintaining a mental focus so disciplined it would have impressed a monastery of celibate monks.","His face remained perfectly neutral throughout but Mira’s face and breathing did not which almost broke him.","At one point, Dexter even felt like the battle with the Four-Armed Goblins wasn’t even half as difficult as this.","After fleeing, he calmed himself down and made lunch which consisted of Celestial Spirit Bean porridge, seared vegetables and sliced Transcendent meat.","When he called out to them, Lyra actually came out last and when she ate, she only ate a single plate.","In the two weeks he had been cooking for these women, Lyra had never eaten less than two portions. Most days, she ate four. On particularly good days, she ate six.","And today, she ate one, leaving the remaining food on the table as she stood up, and walked back to the bedroom without a word.","Not just Dexter, Mira and Selene were both stunned to see Lyra leave without touching her food.","Mira glanced at Dexter and said expressionlessly. \"What did you to her now?\"","Dexter glared back at Mira. \"Why do you think I did anything?\"","Mira lips curled upwards. \"Men.\"","She immediately turned her wheelchair to the living room and left.","Dexter smirked. ’ Seems like she’s still mad about this morning.’","He ignored her and focused on Lyra.","If there was one thing in this world that could always cheer Lyra up, it was food.","The fact that she had turned her back on food meant she was not just annoyed, she was genuinely angry.","Dexter sat there, thinking for a long while.","He thought about going to her and apologizing again, since he would never intentionally violate her and the other girl’s trust.","But he thought even more about and maybe pushing her now, while she was in this state, would only make things worse.","’ Let her simmer down for today.’","1","He would talk to her tomorrow. She might have calmed down by then. ’ Moreover, I did nothing wrong either way.’","He collected the plates, washed the dishes, and spent the rest of the afternoon, practicing his punching and fighting techniques in the backyard.","[A/N: Valid crash out or nah? Or maybe something else is going on?]","[I promised Mass release since last week but one thing or the other kept popping up. I apologize for that. Just wanted to say that I haven’t forgotten and it will be possible this week at least.\""]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176 | Scheming Brat","paragraphs":["\"Knock!\" \"Knock!\" \"Knock!\"","Dexter heard a knock at the gate.","His Enhanced Hearing picked up the heartbeat before the knock even landed and he immediately knew who it was.","He sighed, cleaned up his hands from washing the plates and then walked out of the door, to the gate.","Tessa stood on the other side, grinning from ear to ear as her green eyes sparkled.","\"So?\" Dexter asked, leaning against the gate frame. \"How did the food business go?\"","Tessa’s grin widened as she batted her eyelashes, and placed both hands behind her back.","\"Guess.\"","Dexter rolled his eyes.","He was not in the mood for guessing games.","Lyra’s strange behavior was still gnawing at the back of his mind, spoiling imhjs mood slightly.","He rubbed the bridge of his nose.","\"Just tell me.\"","Tessa pouted at his bluntness. The pout lasted approximately two seconds before the grin broke through again.","\"We sold out,\" she said. \"All twenty portions. In under eight hours.\"","Dexter stared at her.","\"Eight hours?\"","\"Eight hours, every single container was gone. The shelf was empty by 3 to 4 in the afternoon.\"","Dexter was stunned.","Eight hours was not something he had expected. He had prepared for the possibility that the meals would take two or three days to sell and had braced himself for the likelihood that most people in this neighborhood would take one look at the price, hesitate, and walk away.","He had been wrong.","People in this neighborhood had been willing to spend money on a meal made by a stranger for 5000 dollars which was insane.","The heaviness that had settled over him since the incident with Lyra’s diary lifted as he felt a hint of satisfaction.","As a chef, as a Foodsmith, there was no greater validation.","\"I didn’t have your contact information,\" Tessa continued, rocking on her heels. \"Otherwise I would have called you. Definitely. We probably could have sold ten more portions if we’d had them.\"","\"A few people came in specifically asking if there was more. One man bought two portions. A woman from Elm Street bought one, and came back twenty minutes later asking if she could buy another. And then there was this one older guy.\"","She paused dramatically.","\"He wanted to personally know who made the food. I had to come up with some sort of excuse about the chef being a private person who didn’t want to be identified. It took some convincing to make him leave.\"","Dexter nodded slowly. The man had probably felt the effect of the Grade One meal.","\"Thank you, Tessa,\" Dexter said. \"Seriously. Thank you for handling everything.\"","\"You’re welcome, Boss Chef.\"","Dexter considered the numbers.","\"I should increase the batch size,\" he said. \"From twenty to thirty. Maybe even forty if I can manage the prep time.\"","Tessa nodded vigorously. \"I was going to say thirty minimum. Maybe even fifty if you have the time. Mr. Thompson, you know, the retired hero two streets over? He bought a portion and loved it and also, Mrs. Alvarez. They want to buy more, regularly.\"","She paused, her expression shifting to something slightly more earnest.","\"And some of them are quite curious about you.\"","Dexter shrugged. \"I’m quite busy. Maybe another time.\"","Tessa’s eyes lit up with a new idea.","\"There’s a festival this weekend,\" she said. \"Well, more of a picnic, really. The whole neighborhood participates. It happens at Roland Stone Garden, which is close by. You and your wives could come. Meet everyone. Get to know the people around here.\"","Dexter blinked as he thought about it but then, he shook his head.","\"I’ll probably be too busy to attend. But I’ll keep it in mind.\"","Tessa pouted again. This time the pout was genuine. \"It would be really good if you came, Dexter. The neighbors aren’t as bad as you think. They’re just... cautious. They don’t know you yet. Once they do...\"","She trailed off, leaving the implication hanging.","Then her expression shifted back to business.","\"Okay, give me your account information. Let me transfer the funds.\"","Dexter nodded and recited his account number. Tessa typed it into her phone, double-checked the digits, and hit send.","Dexter’s phone buzzed in his pocket. He pulled it out and opened the notification.","[Transfer received: 90,000 credits]","[From: Tessa Wren]","[Available balance: 1,590,000 credits]","Dexter stared at the number.","Ninety thousand credits. In a single day. From twenty portions of food that he had cooked in less than two hours using ordinary ingredients and deliberately suppressed techniques.","The warmth in his chest expanded.","But then his Foodsmith mind, ever analytical, kicked in. He ran the numbers. Twenty portions. The price on the sign had been set at six thousand credits per portion, which Tessa had apparently adjusted upward from the original five hundred when she saw the demand. Twenty portions at six thousand credits each was one hundred and twenty thousand.","Not ninety thousand.","There was a thirty thousand credit discrepancy.","Dexter looked up from his phone. He stared at Tessa with narrowed eyes.","\"Where is the rest of the money?\"","Tessa smiled. It was the smile of a woman who had been waiting for this exact question and had prepared her answer in advance.","\"That’s my commission.\"","Dexter’s eyes narrowed further. \"Your commission?\"","\"For selling the food. Twenty-five percent.\"","\"Twenty-five percent?\"","\"Yep.\"","Tessa crossed her arms and leaned against the gate post with her green eyes shinnng bright in amusement. She looked like a cat that had just stolen a fish and was daring the owner to say something about it.","\"I sold the food,\" she said, ticking off points on her fingers. \"I dealt with the customers. I handled the payments. I answered all their questions about the meals and what they did and how they worked. I protected your identity when people started asking who the chef was. And I personally dealt with four separate people who begged me for extra portions that didn’t exist.\"","She lowered her hand and pointed at herself proudly.","\"Don’t you think I’m worth twenty-five percent?\""]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177 | Forgive What?","paragraphs":["Dexter stared at her for several seconds.","The girl was at most 17 and had negotiated a twenty-five percent commission on his product with such confidence that she wasn’t even slightly apologetic about it.","He thought about Mr. Henry.","He had schemed against the father. The daughter had schemed right back.","\"You really are a little schemer,\" he said.","Tessa grinned in satisfaction.","\"Learned from the best.\"","Dexter’s mouth twitched. He wanted to be annoyed but he couldn’t bring himself to be.","Because she was right, she had done the work, handled the customers, managed the transactions and protected his privacy.","Twenty-five percent was bit much but also fair.","\"Get out,\" he said.","Tessa covered her mouth and let out a tickling giggle.","\"See you tomorrow, Boss Chef!\"","She turned and skipped down the sidewalk, her curly red hair bouncing with each step as she waved once over her shoulder without looking back.","Dexter shook his head and he looked down at his phone again.","His total balance was now 1,290,556 dollars.","He slipped the phone back into his pocket and walked inside.","...","Dinner time arrived.","Dexter stood at the kitchen, stirring the food as the aroma filled the entire house.","He was plating the food when he felt a presence behind him.","He turned around.","Lyra was there standing at the kitchen door.","She was staring at the with drolling mouth as her fingers twitched.","Dexter blinked as he glanced at her carefully. Her exprsssion wasn’t as cold as it was that afternoon.","And the stranger seemed to have disappeared bringing back the cute Lyra.","She seemed to have forgiven him. Or at least forgotten. Or at mthe she decided that whatever anger she had been carrying was less important than food.","Dexter wasn’t sure which. So he didn’t say anything and just smiled at her.","He served the stew into four bowls, arranged them on the small dining table, and stepped back.","\"Sit do—\"","Lyra was in her seat before he could even pull the chair out.","She sat down, picked up her spoon, and began eating without a word.","Dexter stared at her for a moment then he went to get Mira, wheeling her to the dining table while she cultivated in silence.","Then he went to the backyard for Selene.","She was on the swing with her eyes closed in cultivation.","\"Selene. Dinner.\"","She opened her eyes and gently stood up. Then she walked toward him without hesitation.","She paused as she passed him.","\"Smells good,\" she said quietly.","Dexter smiled. \"It’s the bean stew. You’d like it.\"","Selene smiled faintly as they both walked tk the dining room.","---","The four of them ate silently together at the small dining table. The silence wasn’t awkward and it seemed they were lost in their own world as they ate.","Well, except for Lyra who was devouring the food rapidly.","One bowl. Gone.","She looked at Dexter and her melodious voice rang in his head.","’M-more .’","Dexter blinked and then stood up as he refilled refilled her bowl.","Less than a minute, it was all gone.","She blinked her eyes pitifully at Dexter, making Dexter smile.","\"Alright.\"","This happened repeatedly until six bowls were all devoured!","Dexter’s eyebrows rose steadily with each refill.","Six full bowls of food was more than she had ever eaten in a single sitting. And she wasn’t slowing down. She was slowing up. Each bowl seemed to make her eat faster, as though she was trying to make up off the afternoon.","Finally, after the sixth bowl, she set her spoon down and leaned back in her chair.","\"Sigh.\"","Her hands moved to her stomach, pressing gently against her full belly as a satisfied exhale escaped her lips.","Then she looked at Dexter.","’ Thank you.’","Dexter’s brow furrowed slightly as she stood up and walked to the living room couch.","’ She was angry at me all day, ate only one portion at lunch and didn’t speak to me for hours. And now she’s acting like nothing happened.’","He checked her status through his system reflexively.","[Lyra Vance — Shadow Corruption Level: 2%]","Still two percent. Stable. No increase.","’ At least the corruption isn’t getting worse.’","He finished his own food, collected the dishes, and began washing them.","He turn turned back and could see Lyra on the couch. She had the Primordial Beast Egg cradled in her lap and her eyes were closed while her other rested on her belly, patting it gently as she cultivated.","Dexter shook his head with a quiet smile.","He finished the dishes, dried his hands, and walked to the living room.","Lyra was still on the couch.","Dexter looked at her and spoke as he also projected his surface thought loudly.","\"I assume you aren’t angry anymore,\" he said quietly.","Lyra’s eyes snapped open. She looked at him through her AI glasses, as her dark eyes blinking with what appeared to be genuine confusion.","’ Why would I be angry?’","Her telepathic voice was innocent and slightly baffled as she stared at Dexter in puzzlement.","Dexter stared at her.","\"This afternoon,\" he said. \"With the diary matter.\"","Lyra blinked and her brows furrowed cutely.","\"About this afternoon?\" she repeated, her voice carrying nothing but confusion.","Dexter’s frown deepened.","It doesn’t seem like she was pretending.","’ Did she genuinely forget?’","2","If Lyra didn’t want to remember, then it was better wasn’t it?","Moreover, he didn’t want her to be even more annoyed by bringing up the past.","\"Forget it,\" he said, shaking his head. \"It’s nothing.\"","Lyra stared at him for a moment longer. Then she shrugged, closed her eyes, and resumed cultivating.","After dinner, the girls drifted to their respective spaces.","Dexter went to his room and sat cross-legged on his bed, and exhaled slowly.","It had been a long day and a productive ine at that.","But even with all that, he still needed to cultivate and grow stronger so he could take care of himself and the girls.","But before he could begin, the system spoke.","[Ding!]"]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178 | Life Span Reward","paragraphs":["---","[10,000x Investment System Activated]","[Calculating daily investment returns...]","[Multiplier: 100x]","---","[Investment 1 — Protecting Mira]","[Action: Host shielded Mira Calloway from emotional and physical threat posed by hostile family visitor. Host absorbed Mira’s chronic pain via Ring of Shared Burdens and provided ongoing medical care through massage therapy and Grade-4 Enchanted Meals.]","[Return: Ultra Violet Protection Earring — Type 3Artifact]","A black stud earring that automatically protects the wearer against attacks from a Peak Ultra-Rank opponent. It can completely nullify three such attacks before its protective energy is exhausted.","...","[Investment 2 — Suppressing Selene’s Eternal Winter Ice]","[Action: Host activated Abyssal Flame to provide warmth for Selene Frost during shared cultivation session. Host endured three hours of immobile sitting to avoid disturbing Selene’s sleep. Host’s body heat suppressed the Internal Winter Ice throughout the night, allowing Selene her first pain-free rest in three years.]","[Return: Cold and Frost Resistance (Permanent) — 20%]","...","[Investment 3 — Caring for Mira]","[Action: Host performed 108 Body Massage Sutra on Mira Calloway using Shockwave Glove and Grade-4 Spiritual Massage Oil. Host channeled mana into damaged nerve pathways, stimulated dormant muscles, and provided sustained physical therapy over multiple sessions.]","[Return: Joy and Harmony Acupuncture Technique]","A peculiar acupuncture technique that stimulates specific acupoints throughout the body, triggering intense relaxation and pleasure. It has no healing effect and is purely designed to induce bodily comfort and pleasure.","...","[Investment 4 — Caring for His Wives]","[Action: Host provided sustained daily care for all three wives including cooking, cleaning, bathing assistance, medical treatment, emotional support, and household maintenance over an extended period without compensation or complaint.]","[Return: Lifespan Extension — One Additional Year]","...","[Investment 5 — Seeking a New Source of Income]","[Action: Host established business partnership with local bakery, prepared and sold 20 Grade-One Enchanted Meals to generate independent income for household support. Host deliberately suppressed own abilities to produce affordable meals suited to neighborhood economic conditions.]","[Return: Arcane Nutrition Insight — Passive Ability]","A passive knowledge ability that allows Dexter to identify the nutritional, restorative, and energy-boosting properties of any ingredient on sight. It also allows him to determine which ordinary, non-spiritual ingredients can be combined to create meals that provide minor but genuine benefits.","Effects include:","Improved stamina","Faster recovery from exhaustion","Better cultivation efficiency","Slightly improved concentration","Temporary resistance to fatigue","...","[Investment 6 — Repairing the Broken Window]","[Action: Host personally repaired damage to family home caused by hostile visitor. Host purchased materials, installed new window frame, fitted replacement glass, patched interior wall, and painted surrounding area to restore the living space for his wives.]","[Return: Type-3 Pure-Air Fragrance Artifact]","A small decorative artifact that releases a faint, pleasant fragrance throughout the house. It continuously filters dust and impurities from the air, removes unpleasant odors, reduces airborne pollutants, freshens the entire house, and maintains clean, breathable air for all occupants.","The artifact can operate continuously for one full year before needing to be replaced or recharged.","...","Reading the first notification, dexter flipped his hands and an simple black earring materialized in his palm.","Although it looked simple, it actually contained the power to nullify three full attacks of a Peak Ultra-Rank attack. That was the kind of defensive artifact that could save his life when placed in a desperate situation.","If he had this during the outbreak at the market district, he might have been more bold with his attacks.","The three girls already had their own defensive equipment. This one, he would keep for himself.","He immediately placed it in his ears. While he didn’t know how he looked, it should be quite alright right?","And maybe he would look even handsome. ’What would Mira, Lyra and Selene say?’","Before he knew it, his train of thought went to what his wives would think of it.","He laughed softly and shook his head to remove his thoughts from them. Then accepted his second reward.","20% permanent resistance to ice? It wasn’t necessary needed as he had a high ranking flames but if he came into contract with an ultra rank ice user, then maybe it would prove useful.","Since all attacks involving extreme cold, freezing temperatures, or ice-based energy will have their effectiveness reduced by twenty percent against him.","Dexter flexed his fingers but didn’t feel much of a change but he noticed even without his heavenly flame heating his blood, there wasn’t a shred of coldness in his body.","---","When it came to the Joy And Harmony Acupuncture Technique, Dexter ea stunned and read the notification twice.","’Pleasure.’","’Purely designed to induce bodily comfort and pleasure.’","’No healing effect.’","His face went through several expressions in rapid succession as he finally figured out what the system meant.","’First the contraceptive capsules. Now this.’","’What exactly does the system think I am doing with my wives?’","He pressed his palms against his face and groaned quietly into the darkness of his room.","’I am a Foodsmith. A husband who is trying his best to take care of three wives in peace. I am not running some kind of pleasure palace.’","He shoved the technique’s knowledge into the back of his mind.","---","Then his next return which was an additional year of lifespan.","Dexter lowered his hands from his face and blinked at the notification.","One year of life, just like that? He had thought he would receive a year of cultivation, not lifespan.","But every human being, no matter how powerful, was bound by the finite length of their life. One additional year meant one more year to live longer.","Although he didn’t think his lifespan was low but having additional life span wasn’t bad.","He accepted it without hesitation.","---","The next was the ability: Arcane Nutritional Insight.","Dexter’s eyes widened as the knowledge integrated into his mind. While he had a bit of this ability due to his high level foodsmith and his Heavenly Gastronomy Body, this ability would make him gain more insights into materials.","He could create an entire menu of affordable, beneficial meals tailored to different needs.","His mind was already racing through recipe combinations when the final notification appeared."]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179 | Joy And Harmony Acupuncture Technique","paragraphs":["The last reward was the Pure-Air Fragrance.","Dexter accepted the reward and watched as a small object materialized on his palm.","It was a delicate ceramic lotus flower, no larger than a teacup, painted in soft shades of white and pale blue.","The petals were slightly open, revealing a tiny crystal set into the center that glowed faintly.","The moment it touched his skin, he felt a gentle, almost imperceptible wave of clean, fresh air radiated outward from the lotus as it released a subtle, clean freshness that reminded him of mountain air after a spring rain.","’This is actually really nice.’","He walked out of his room, holding the lotus and placed it behind the curtain.","The effect was immediate and noticeable.","The air in the bungalow, which had been carrying the lingering smells of cooking oil, paint and plaster dust, began to clear but by bit, like opening a window in a stuffy room.","Dexter stood in the hallway and breathed in.","He thought about his wives that loved their spots. it should help with the circulation of their breathing.","Dexter smiled as he returned happily to his room.","On his bed, he surfed through the internet dir random stuffs, reading various articles, dungeon outbreaks and even invitations to join a squad to enter a Dimensional Gate together.","His thumb paused on the billboard photo he had taken earlier that afternoon.","Dexter stared at the number for a moment then held the number and clicked the press call option.","The line rang three times before someone picked up.","\"Harvest Homes, this is Jennifer speaking. How may I help you?\"","\"Good evening,\" Dexter said. \"I saw your billboard advertisement on the main highway. I’m interested in learning about your available properties.\"","\"Of course, sir. We have a wide range of options available. Residential homes, townhouses, estate properties, and undeveloped land parcels in various districts throughout Stargate City. I can email you our current catalog with pricing details and specifications, or...\"","She paused.","\"It would actually be preferable for you to visit our office in person. We can discuss your needs face to face, review floor plans, and I can walk you through the financing options available for others and also licensed heroes.\"","Dexter considered it as it would take him away from the girls.","But this was important and was about their future.","\"Can I come tomorrow morning?\" he asked. \"Around ten?\"","\"Ten o’clock works perfectly. May I have your name?\"","\"Dexter Ashford.\"","The line paused for a bit as a something clicked in Jennifer’s mind.","\"Thank you, Mr. Ashford. I’ll have everything prepared for your visit. Do you need directions?\"","\"I’ll find it.\"","\"Excellent. We’ll see you tomorrow at ten.\"","The call ended.","Dexter set the phone down and immediately thought of something else.","Plasmatic Man had called yesterday about meeting with a potential squad. Dexter had told him he would text back with his availability. He had forgotten about it until now.","He picked up the phone, saved Cole’s number, and typed a quick message.","[Available tomorrow at 12 PM. Let me know if that works for you.]","He didn’t wait for a response. He placed the phone face-down on the nightstand, closed his eyes, and began cultivating.","Tomorrow’s schedule was going to be busy.","He needed to make 50 portions of meals, also, ten o’clock at Harvest Homes, twelve o’clock with Cole and the others.","---","He had been cultivating for roughly an hour when he heard a familiar heartbeat.","His bedroom door opened slowly and the air in the room shifted as the temperature dropped by several degrees in seconds.","Dexter smiled.","’ She’s early.’","Last night, Selene had come to his room around late midnight, but tonight, it was barely 11 and she was here.","He had half expected her to come even later tonight, embarrassed by the fact that she had fallen asleep on his shoulder that morning.","Instead, she had come earlier.","’ She’s getting comfortable.’","Dexter kept his eyes closed and didn’t acknowledge her presence as he simply continued cultivating, giving her the space to settle in on her own terms.","Selene’s footsteps were soft as she walked to the bed but then, stopped.","Dexter opened his eye and smiled at her, gesturing with his arms pointing to the bed.","Then he closed his eye and erupted with his heavenly flames as he resumed cultivating.","Selene couldn’t see but with her talent, she ’saw’ his gesture and knew he trying his best not to make things uncomfortable.","She slowly sat down on the edge of the bed, raised her white, pale legs, crossed them beneath her, and settled into her meditation posture.","Themn she closed her eyes and then her cultivation began.","Mana flowed into the room from the surrounding air, drawn by the combined gravitational pull of their respective Star Nodes. The energy pooled around them like water filling a basin, warm and golden from Dexter’s side, cool and silver from Selene’s.","Thirty minutes passed.","Dexter suddenly opened his eyes and shifted his position.","He moved across the bed toward Selene as though he was simply adjusting his posture for comfort.","He only stopped when his knees were almost touching hers, their crossed legs forming a small diamond of space between them.","Selene didn’t need to open where eyes to see and her ears turned slightly pink as she felt the heat from his knees flowed directly to her lower body.","Dexter increased the heat radiating from his body, just enough so it won’t ignite the surrounding space.","They cultivated in silence.","Another thirty minutes passed and Dexter shifted again.","This time, he moved directly beside her.","Their shoulders touched and the sides of their knees pressed together.","With this position, the heat from his body flowed directly into hers through the points of contact.","Her shoulder, her arm and her knee. The warmth seeped through her thin sleeping clothes and into her skin, spreading through her damaged meridians and pushing back the Internal Winter Ice that lived beneath the surface.","Selene’s ears went from pink to red.","But she didn’t pull away.","Instead, she let out a slow, quiet breath. The kind of exhale that comes from a body finally letting go of tension it has been holding for so long that it forgot what relaxation felt like.","\"Thank you,\" she murmured.","The words were barely audible but Dexter heard it.","Dexter didn’t respond and simply continued cultivating as he warmed her body.","They cultivated through the night."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180 | You’re Insane...","paragraphs":["Sometime past midnight, Selene’s head drifted sideways and rested directly on Dexter’s shoulder. Her silver-white hair spilled across his arm as her breathing slowed.","A few minutes later, her hands actually found his as her fingers closed around his arm, snuggling and cuddling his arm like a koala and Dexter was awake through all of it.","And then, unbidden, unwanted, and thoroughly unhelpful, his mind drifted to a particular system reward he had received earlier that evening.","’Joy and Harmony Acupuncture Technique.’","’Purely designed to induce bodily comfort and pleasure.’","Heat started to rise within his body.","Not the Abyssal Flame kind of heat. Not the mana-circulation kind of heat. A different kind entirely. One that had nothing to do with cultivation and everything to do with the fact that a beautiful woman was pressed against his side, her fingers wrapped around his arm, her hair brushing against his neck.","Dexter inhaled sharply through his nose.","’Don’t. Do not. Do not even think about it.’","He activated his breathing technique, forcing his mana circulation into a slower, deeper pattern to calm his mind and it helped slightly. .","’Just calm down. You’ve seen OnlyHeroes, done somethings, so you should be resistant to this.’","But his body was not listening to his mind with the same fidelity it usually demonstrated. The warmth continued to build as something within him started to rise.","’Just the thought is getting a rise out of you.’","He almost slapped himself.","’If she kissed you, what would you do?’","He rapidly thought about something else. Mira’s sister.","It helped.","For about ten minutes.","Then Selene shifted in her sleep, her head sliding from his shoulder to his chest, her body curling slightly toward his warmth. Her grip on his arm tightened.","\"Sigh.\"","A quiet, content sound escaped her lips.","Dexter eyes trembled and he stared at the ceiling with the wide, unblinking eyes of a man enduring a trial of temptation.","He gritted his teeth as he glared at the air. It was this goddam system that placed useless thoughts in his mind.","First was the pill, then the glove and now the jog and harmony acupuncture technique.","’I am going to kill the system.’","He barely survived the night through stubbornness and willpower that rival’s that of John-wick.","---","\"Ring! Ring! Ring!\"","The alarm shattered the silence at 5:00 AM.","Dexter’s eyes snapped open.","Selene’s eyes snapped open.","For a brief, disorienting moment, neither of them moved.","Then Selene processed her situation.","Her head was on his chest, not on his shoulder but on his chest and her arm was wrapped around his waist as her body pressed against his side, curled into him like a vine clinging to a tree trunk.","Even her leg had somehow ended up draped across his knee.","She was, for all practical purposes, attached to him like a koala on a tree.","\"W-what...?\"","Selene’s face went from zero to crimson in half a second as she released him so fast it was as though his skin had been made of hot iron.","She scrambled backward on the bed, her hands slapping against the mattress, her silver hair flying in every direction. Her pale eyes were wide. Her lips were parted. Her entire face was the color of a ripe tomato.","She turned toward the door. Took two steps and then stopped.","Her hand gripped the door frame.","She stood there for a moment, her back to him, her shoulders tight, her ears burning.","\"Thank you and I’m really sorry i did that, Dexter. It won’t happen again.\" she stuttered but sounded solemn.","Dexter was stunned and before she could leave he immediately spoke up.","\"I don’t mind.\"","Selene who was planning to leave suddenly froze.","Dexter immediately relayed himself. \"I truly don’t mind. As long as it makes you comfortable? I’d do anything to help you.\"","As he spoke those words, Selene’s body trembled. And she froze for a while before she muttered.","\"Because it’s your responsibility, right?\"","Dexter immediately nodded his head. \"Yes.\"","Selene breathing paused and it seemed she didn’t receive the answer she wanted but Dexter voice continued.","\"At the beginning, yes. I did it because it was my responsibility, but now, I’m doing it because of another reason entirely.\"","Hos words were sincere and although Selene couldn’t see, her Takent could see every inch of his face. Every expression he made and she knew he was been serious.","Selene turned her head slightly towards him and let out an extremely beautiful smile.","\"You’re insane.\"","With that, she immediately left his room.","Dexter was stunned and he scratched his head. ’ What does she mean by that? Is it a good thigh or a bad thing.’","4","He smiled and shook his head, exhaling as he stretched his arms above his head.","His spine popped, his neck cracked twice and his shoulders groaned. He hadn’t moved for about 5 hours.","Because a beautiful woman had been sleeping on him and he had been too stubborn and too respectful to disturb her.","He stood up, stretched again, then he looked at the clock.","5:03 AM.","He had a lot to do today.","He stood at the kitchen counter, sleeves rolled to his elbows, and began prepping. He used only ordinary ingredients like yesterday.","His Arcane Nutrition Insight passive ability made the process remarkably efficient.","’Carrots. High in beta-carotene. When combined with ginger, produces a mild stamina recovery effect lasting ninety minutes.’","’Grade One beast meat. Moderate protein density. Low mana content. When seared and paired with soy sauce, enhances physical recovery rate by six percent for two hours.’","’Onions. Trace sulfur compounds. When caramelized, improves absorption of accompanying nutrients by eight percent.’","He didn’t need to think about what would work and what wouldn’t. The knowledge simply existed, guiding his hands as he chopped, seasoned, and stirred with practiced efficiency.","He used the large ordinary pot, without heavenly flame. Just heat, oil, and technique deliberately dialed back to produce food that was good without being extraordinary.","By 6:30 AM, the first batch was done."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181 | Kissing...","paragraphs":["Dexter was halfway through the second batch when he felt a presence behind him.","He turned around and suddenly saw Lyra was standing at the kitchen door.","Her dark eyes were fixed on the gas cooker with thirst.","The food smelled amazing.","She looked at Dexter as she formed a pout of such devastating proportions that it could have ended wars.","Dexter scratched the back of his head.","\"Sorry, Lyra. I haven’t made your food yet. I’m still cooking for the customers. Just give me about thirty minutes and I’ll be done.\"","Lyra’s pout deepened and her eyes grew wider as she looked so cute and pitiful.","Her shoulders dropped as she turned around saddened and began walking back to the living room.","Dexter watched her go and couldn’t help but sigh.","Suddenly, he flipped his hand and two bags of Sminley Chips materialized in his palm.","Then three Celestial Pastries also appeared beside it making everything smell like a bakery in heaven.","Lyra had already turned the corner when the smell traveled directly into her nose.","She immediately froze mid-step as her nose flared and she unconsciously inhaled deeply.","She suddenly turned her as her body rotated like a compass needle finding north and she was back in the kitchen doorway in less than two seconds.","Her eyes locked onto the chips and pastries in Dexter’s hand and the pout vanished as her lips curled up into an expectatant smile.","\"Whoosh!\"","She flash stepped across the kitchen with a speed that stunned even Dexter himself.","That speed actually rival Flame Burst step!","Her hands shot out and snatched the entire haul from Dexter’s palm like a pickpocket who had been doing this since birth.","She clutched the chips and pastries against her chest. Her arms wrapped around them protectively as her dark eyes looked up at him.","And she smiled.","It was, without exaggeration, the most brilliant smile Dexter had ever seen on Lyra’s face.","Then, before Dexter could react, she leaned forward.","She was almost his height so she didn’t need to tiptoe as she tilted her head to the side and suddenly, pressed her lips against his cheek.","A warm soft sensation touched against Dexter’s cheeks. If lasted for half a second as she then pulled back.","Her eyes widened.","The smile froze on her face as the realization of what she had just done crashed into her consciousness with the force of a freight train.","Her face instantly went red, climbing for her neck, consuming her cheeks, her ears, her forehead, and the back of her head.","She spun around, clutching her chips and pastries against her chest like a dragon guarding its hoard, and fled the kitchen.","Her bare feet slapped against the hallway floor. Her bedroom door slammed shut a moment later.","Dexter stood alone in the kitchen, a spatula in one hand, his other hand still extended in the air where the snacks had been.","He stared at the empty doorway.","His cheek tingled where her lips had touched.","The faint irritation he had been carrying since the diary incident, the lingering frustration from Lyra’s cold behavior the previous afternoon, the confusion about the voice that was almost hers but not quite.","All of it vanished.","Melted like snow in sunlight.","Something warm bloomed in his chest. Not the heat of his Flame Demon Bloodline. Not the mana warmth of his Abyssal Flame. Something quieter. Softer. Something that spread through his ribs like warm honey and settled there with a gentle, persistent glow.","The tips of his ears turned red.","His eyes blinked rapidly. Twice. Three times.","He inhaled sharply through his nose and held the breath for a long moment.","Then he exhaled slowly.","And smiled.","\"These women,\" he muttered to himself, shaking his head as he turned back to the stove. \"All of them. Every single one. They’re going to be the death of me.\"","He continued cooking.","---","By 7:15 AM, the fifty portions were done.","He had actually made fifty-five. Five extra, just in case. Each container was packed, sealed, and stacked neatly in his spatial storage. Fifty-five portions of Grade One Enchanted Meal. Comfort Chicken Rice with vegetables. Nothing fancy. Nothing that would attract heavenly tribulations. Just good, affordable food that would give ordinary people a genuine boost in their daily lives.","Then he turned his attention to the girls’ breakfast.","This was different. This was not for customers. This was for his wives.","He pulled out the good ingredients. Diamond Rice. Fresh vegetables. Premium chicken breast. A thin slice of Millennium Blood Ginseng. A single drop of Star Essence Serum.","His Arcane Nutrition Insight worked overtime, mapping combinations and calculating effects as he moved through the kitchen with the focused intensity of a man performing surgery.","The Type-II Spirit Cooking Pot came out. The heavenly flame ignited. His Great Grandmaster Foodsmith techniques activated fully, every movement precise and deliberate, every ingredient placed with the care of a master painter applying brushstrokes to canvas.","The kitchen filled with an aroma so rich and complex that even the walls seemed to lean closer.","[Ding! Congratulations! You have successfully created Celestial Dawn Nectar Bowl (Grade 5)]","’’[Effect: Permanently strengthens physical constitution. Accelerates meridian repair by 35%. Boosts mana regeneration for 6 hours. Induces deep cellular healing. Removes accumulated fatigue toxins.]’’","Grade Five.","Dexter stared at the notification. He hadn’t intentionally aimed for Grade Five. It had simply happened. The combination of premium ingredients, his upgraded cooking skills, and the Arcane Nutrition Insight had pushed the meal a grade higher than he thought would come out.","Also, there was no dark clouds gathered outside nor was there any heavenly thunder rumbling in the skies.","The meal’s energy was dense but was contained within the food rather than radiating outward.","The Grade Five threshold for atmospheric disturbance was higher than Grade Four, and this dish sat comfortably below it.","He plated four bowls. Each one glowed faintly with a warm, golden luminescence. Thin wisps of steam rose in lazy spirals, carrying a scent that was simultaneously savory, sweet, and deeply comforting.","He carried them to the dining table."]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182 | Taming The Dragon","paragraphs":["After he was done with the meal, Dexter went to get Mira.","He walked to the bedroom and found her in her wheelchair with her eyes closed, cultivating.","\"Mira. Bath time.\"","She opened one eye. Looked at him. Closed it.","\"Give me a moment.\"","\"Nop.\"","He ignored her glare as he wheeled her to the bathroom, carefully undressed her, and carried her to the shower.","He turned on the warm water, adjusted the temperature, and placed her on the shower bench.","Then he began bathing her, starting with her shoulders, using the same routine.","He usually kept his mind occupied with Cultivation techniques, recipe combinations, dungeon strategies and breathing patterns. Anything that could fill his thoughts and keep his mind detached from what he was currently doing.","Today, it didn’t work.","The mental firewall he had rebuilt overnight had been damaged by Selene’s touch and Lyra’s kiss that morning, and the residual cracks were letting things through.","He was washing Mira when he noticed her skin.","He had always noticed it, of course. You couldn’t bathe another human being daily without being aware of their physical form. But there was a difference between awareness and noticing things that made your heart pound and your breathing trembling.","Mira’s skin was pale, not pale like Selene’s skin but pale with tiny cute barely seen freckles on her skin.","As he touched her skin, he realized it was incredibly soft beneath his fingers as the soft sponge moved across her shoulders, softer than anything he had ever touched.","He noticed the way the warm water traced paths down her back. The way it followed the subtle curves of her spine, pooling briefly in the hollow above her hip before continuing downward.","He noticed her wet crimson hair as it darkened to the color of blood, clinging to her neck and shoulders. The color was so vivid and red that it didn’t look real. It looked like something painted by an artist who had been given access to colors that didn’t exist in nature.","He started to take notice of even the tiniest things.","The tiny mole just above her upper lip, no larger than the head of a pin. It made her beauty stand out to perfection.","The faint barely visible dusting of freckles across the bridge of her nose.","Her slender and graceful hands. The neat and unpolished nails, her long collarbones that had faint blue traces of veins beneath the surface.","Her full lips which was strangely red as it parted as she breathed. The lower lip was slightly fuller than the upper, giving her mouth a natural pout that she probably wasn’t aware of.","Everything about her was extraordinary.","And he couldn’t stop noticing.","’Dammit! What am I thinking? Think about literally anything other than the cute freckles on her nose, the mole above her lip and the way her hair looks when it’s wet.’","Shocker, it didn’t work.","The observations kept coming, unbidden, relentless, each one more detailed than the last.","Mira seemed entirely oblivious to his internal crisis. She passively closed her eyes, her expression holding its usual mask of calm indifference. If she noticed that his hands were moving faster than normal, or that his breathing was slightly more controlled than usual.","Dexter finished washing her as quickly as he could without being obvious about the haste.","He dried her, dressed her, pulled a fresh blouse over her head and began buttoning it.","His fingers fumbled and in his rush, he missed a button.","The second buttonhole went into the third button. The third into the fourth. The entire alignment was off by one, creating a subtle but noticeable asymmetry in the blouse’s fit.","Dexter didn’t notice.","He placed Mira in her wheelchair, wheeled her to the dining room, parked her at the table, and left.","Lyra and Selene were already there but Dexter did not put food on anyone’s plate.","He immediately left the dining room and walked directly to his bedroom, closed the door behind him, and stood in the center of the room with his hands pressed against his face.","’Calm...’","He activated his breathing technique and tried to calm himself. Then burning heat inside of him seemed to reduce slightly.","Then he walked to the bathroom, turned the cold water tap on full blast, and splashed his face about six times before the rising dragon was successfully tamed.","He looked at his reflection. ’Pervert,’","He sighed, dried his face, straightened his shirt, and walked back to the dining room.","The three girls were seated at the table. All three were looking at him with variations of the same expression.","Mira’s brow was furrowed. She had already noticed the missed button and her Spectral Arms were already correcting it.","Selene’s head was tilted slightly, her pale eyes aimed in his direction. Through her Echolocation, she had likely detected the elevated heart rate, the irregular breathing, and the hurried movements that were so unlike his usual calm demeanor.","Lyra blinked her eyes as she stared wide eyes at Dexter while eating her chips at the same time.","Dexter let out an awkward smile.","\"Sorry about that, something urgent came up.\"","He didn’t explain further as he walked to the kitchen, ladled the Celestial Dawn Nectar Bowl into four serving bowls, and placed them on the table.","The moment the bowls touched the table, the aroma filled the room.","All three girls looked down at their bowls.","Mira’s Spectral Arms paused mid-button-correction. Her nostrils flared as her crimson eyes widened by a fraction.","Selene tilted her head further, her pale lips parting slightly as the scent reached her.","Lyra set down her chips.","For Lyra to voluntarily set down chips in the presence of food was, by itself, a miracle of biblical proportions.","Everyday that Dexter cooked for them, he always seems to stun them with his astonishing cooking skill.","Day by day, his skill kept on increasing rapidly as though he had no limit and right now, today’s food seemed to be even better than yesterday’s food.","Even in their homes, while they ate Arcane meals everyday, Dexter food beats everything they had tsted back at their family homes."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183 | You’re Important To me","paragraphs":["’Sorry I ran off because I couldn’t stop thinking about you girls?’","Nop, that sentence would never leave his mouth under any circumstances short of torture.","He was trying his best not to lie to his wives. He had learned, through bitter experience and the slow, painful process of building trust with three traumatized women, that secrets were the termites that ate through the foundation of any relationship.","But, some things were better left unsaid.","They ate in silence as the girls enjoyed their meal.","Mira kept glancing at him and she was subtle about it.","But Dexter noticed every single one and he said nothing.","He kept his attention on his food. He had gotten very good at pretending he didn’t notice things over the past few weeks.","Lyra was buried in her food. She wasn’t even trying to savor the taste. She was simply inhaling the food like a vacuum.","Selene closed her eyes as she ate quietly.","Halfway through the meal, Dexter remembered something.","\"Oh,\" he said, setting down his spoon. \"While I go deliver the meals to Tessa’s father’s bakery, I also have a few errands to run.\"","The girls glaced at him but continued eating.","\"One involves getting a new place,\" Dexter continued. \"And the other involves the monster outbreak I participated in recently.\"","\"Whoosh!\"","All three of them stopped eating immediately and simultaneously. As though someone had pressed a pause button on the entire room.","Lyra’s spoon froze mid-scoop. Selene’s hand stopped halfway to her mouth. Mira’s Spectral Arms went rigid.","Three heads immediately lifted as the pairs of eyes locked onto Dexter with the intensity of mothers hearing the word \"hospital\" in a phone call about their child.","Dexter quickly raised his hand and clarified.","\"Don’t worry,\" he said, letting out a small, reassuring smile. \"While it is regarding the monster outbreak, it has nothing to do with participating in another one. I just want to meet with the comrades I fought alongside. Discuss a few things with them. That’s all.\"","Lyra and Selene held his gaze for a moment longer. Then, slowly, they put their heads back down and resumed eating.","Mira did not.","She continued looking at him, her crimson eyes searching his face as though not entirely satisfied with the explanation but had decided not to press the issue.","Dexter met her gaze for a beat, then returned to his food.","---","Lyra finished first.","She stood up, carried her bowl to the sink and walked to the living room couch where the Primordial Beast Egg was there.","Selene finished second. She placed her spoon neatly beside her bowl, stood up, and drifted toward the backyard.","Then it was just Mira and Dexter.","Dexter had finished his own food several minutes ago. He was sitting at the table, waiting for Mira to finish so he could collect the plates and head out. His schedule was tight. Delivery to the bakery. Housing agent at ten. Squad meeting at twelve. Every minute he spent sitting here was a minute he didn’t have.","But he waited for his wives to finish eating first.","Mira’s Spectral Arms continued feeding her. The movements were becoming smoother each day, the mana limbs responding to her mental commands with increasing precision.","Then suddenly, the spoon stopped.","The Spectral Arm holding it lowered the utensil to the bowl as the spoon clattered softly against the ceramic.","Mira looked directly at Dexter.","Dexter blinked.","\"Are you not going to continue eating?\" he asked, raising an eyebrow.","Mira didn’t answer immediately as she held his gaze. Her crimson eyes studied his face as thd silence stretched.","Five seconds, ten seconds, fifteen.","Dexter began to feel slightly uncomfortable under the weight of her stare. He opened his mouth to say something but Mira spoke first.","\"What is happening with you?\"","Dexter blinked. \"What do you mean?\"","Mira raised an eyebrow as she gave him a look.","\"You’ve been acting a bit weird with me. So tell me. What is happening with you?\"","Her brows suddenly furrowed as she spoke. \"Are you finally tired? Am I being too much of a burden?\"","The last question landed in the quiet kitchen like a stone dropped into still water.","Dexter’s expression changed slightly and his gaze turned serious as he shook his head.","\"I have never seen you as a burden,\" he coldly and seriously. \"And I need you to stop calling yourself that.\"","Mira’s lips parted slightly. She hadn’t expected that tone.","\"Any man who got married to you and called you a burden would be the stupidest person alive.\"","He held her gaze and his eyes were steady, his voice was firm.","\"So stop calling yourself that.\"","He paused.","\"You are important to me. You, Lyra, and Selene. You three are the most important people in my life right now. And that is not going to change.\"","The kitchen was very quiet.","Mira stared at him.","She had expected him to respond, had expected reassurance and had expected him to say something kind and move on. A quick \"of course not\" and a change of subject.","She had not expected this.","She had not expected him to look at her with that expression, speak with that conviction and say the words with the kind of absolute, unshakable certainty that left no room for doubt.","The words had stunned her.","She couldn’t say anything as her throat tightened and her crimson eyes, which could cut steel on a normal day, had gone slightly wide.","Her lips suddenly curled upward.","Then she immediately turned her head away, refusing to meet his gaze. Her ears had turned pink. Her Spectral Arms had retracted behind her back, disappearing completely.","Dexter chuckled softly.","He stood up, reached across the table, and picked up her bowl.","As he turned toward the kitchen.","But before he could take more than a few steps, he felt something grip his wrist.","Dexter smiled and looked down","But then, his entire body went rigid as his face changed drastically with wide-eyed shock. His jaw tightened, his eyes widened and his pupils contracted.","The grip on his wrist was warm, small, soft and strong.","Dexter looked down and his body trembled."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184 | Are You Sure?","paragraphs":["Stargate City — Main Hero Association Headquarters","Stargate City.","The heart of the world’s hero industry.","At the center of the city stood the Main Hero Association Headquarters, a massive structure that dwarfed nearly every branch headquarters scattered across the various regions.","This was not a branch.","It was the central headquarters of the Hero Association, the place where major decisions were made and where countless departments worked around the clock to keep the organization running.","Inside one of the administrative departments, the atmosphere was busy.","Dozens of people in suits sat at their desks, typing on computers, writing reports, submitting forms, and conducting the thousands of small, unglamorous tasks that kept the Hero Association functioning. The sound of keyboards clicking filled the room like mechanical rain. Occasional murmurs. The rustle of paper. The soft ping of arriving emails.","In one corner of the office, a young woman sat at her desk.","She was not typing.","While every other person around her was engaged in the steady, productive rhythm of morning work, she was staring at a document.","The document lay flat on her desk. A single sheet of official Hero Association letterhead, filled out in neat handwriting and signed at the bottom in blue ink.","Her eyes were fixed on the title printed at the top.","REQUEST FOR TRANSFER","Below the title, in the same neat handwriting:","Requesting transfer from Main Hero Association Headquarters to Branch Office, Lower District.","She stared at the words.","She had been staring at them for fifteen minutes.","She was twenty-three years old, slim, dark-haired and pretty, in the kind of way that drew attention without trying to.","She wore a standard Hero Association administrative uniform. A fitted grey blazer over a white blouse and a pencil skirt. Her employee badge hung around her neck, the photograph showing a younger version of herself with a slightly forced smile.","She had worked at the Main Headquarters for eight months. She had fought for the position. Made calls. Pulled favors. Endured three rounds of interviews and a background check before finally being offered a junior administrative role in the Personnel Division.","It was not a glamorous job. It involved processing hero registration forms, filing mission reports, and maintaining the personnel database. But it was a position at the Main Headquarters. The center of everything. The place where careers were built and futures were shaped.","Her name was Jasmine Constance.","And now she was leaving.","She picked up the letter. Stood up. Her chair rolled backward slightly.","She took a breath. Held the letter against her chest. And walked toward the department manager’s office at the far end of the floor.","She had taken three steps when a figure stepped directly into her path.","Darren.","He was tall. Well-built. Clean-shaven. The kind of man who looked like he belonged on a recruitment poster rather than behind a desk. He wore his blazer with the casual confidence of someone who knew he looked good in it. His dark hair was styled with expensive product. His cologne was subtle but present.","He was also, as Jasmine had learned over the past four months, persistent to the point of obstruction.","His brow furrowed as he looked down at her.","\"Jasmine. Are you sure you want to do this?\"","His voice was low. Intended to be private. But in an open-plan office where every worker within ten meters had enhanced hearing or simply well-trained ears, low voices didn’t stay private for long.","Jasmine stopped. She looked at him.","\"Yes,\" she said. \"I’ve made my choice.\"","Darren’s frown deepened. He glanced around the office, noting the subtly tilted heads and the suddenly very interested typists who were absolutely, definitely, one hundred percent focused on their screens and not on this conversation.","\"You struggled to get here,\" Darren said, his voice dropping further. \"You made calls. You pulled strings. You were lucky to get a position at the Main Headquarters. And now you want to transfer to a branch office? In the lower district?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Just yes?\"","\"Just yes.\"","Darren’s jaw tightened. He reached out and grabbed her wrist.","The grip was not aggressive. It was the grip of a man who was accustomed to getting his way and was genuinely confused when things didn’t go according to his plan. It was also a grip that Jasmine did not appreciate.","\"What about me?\" he said.","Jasmine looked down at his hand on her wrist. Then up at his face.","\"What about you?\"","Darren’s eyes flashed. \"What about what we have?\"","Jasmine stared at him.","Then she shook her head slowly.","\"You have quite the imagination,\" she said. Her voice was flat and tired. The kind of tired that came from having the same conversation multiple times. \"There is nothing between us. There has never been anything between us.\"","She held his gaze.","\"Please get your hand off me. Unless you want to embarrass yourself in front of the entire office.\"","Darren’s face went red.","He looked left. He looked right. The nearby typists had suddenly become very interested in their screens, their typing speeds increasing dramatically as they pretended to be deeply absorbed in quarterly personnel reports.","But their ears were perked. Every single one of them was listening.","Darren released her wrist.","He opened his mouth to say something. Then closed it. Then opened it again. Then closed it again.","Jasmine didn’t wait for whatever was going to come out of his mouth.","She turned and walked away.","Her heels clicked against the grey carpet with a steady, unhurried rhythm. She passed rows of cubicles where her colleagues suddenly developed intense fascination with their monitors. She walked the length of the office floor without looking back.","She reached the department manager’s door, knocked once, and entered.","The door closed behind her.","Darren stood alone in the middle of the office floor, his hand still hovering in the air where her wrist had been, his face the color of a ripe tomato.","Nobody looked at him.","Everyone was typing."]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185 | I Owe You More Than I can Repay","paragraphs":["Back at the bungalow.","Mira stared at her own hand.","Her right hand, her actual, physical, flesh-and-blood right hand that had been paralyzed for three years.","The one that no doctor, no healer, no geneticist had been able to restore was wrapped around Dexter’s wrist.","She hadn’t meant to do it. She had reached out instinctively, intending to grab him with her Spectral Arm as she had done dozens of times before. But something different had happened.","Her Spectral Arm had materialized above, hovering in the air as intended.","But her real arm had moved too.","Her real, physical arm had reached out from the her lap, fingers had extended and her hand had closed around Dexter’s wrist","A tear fell from her left eye and dripped off her jaw onto the fabric of her blouse.","She didn’t wipe it away. She couldn’t. Her left arm was still paralyzed.","But her right arm.","Her right arm was holding her husband’s wrist.","She flexed her fingers. Slowly. Deliberately.","They moved.","Her index finger curled inward. Then her middle finger. Then her ring finger. Then her pinky. Each one responding to her mental command with a lag of perhaps half a second, the movements trembling slightly from three years of muscular atrophy.","But they moved.","They moved.","\"Dexter,\" she whispered. Her voice cracked on his name. \"I can...\"","She couldn’t finish.","Dexter set the bowl down on the counter. Slowly. Carefully. As though any sudden movement might shatter whatever miracle was happening in front of him.","He knelt in front of her wheelchair.","He looked up at her. His eyes were bright. His expression was gentle. His voice, when he spoke, carried a quiet certainty that he didn’t fully feel but knew she needed to hear.","\"You did it.\"","Mira looked at him. Her crimson eyes, usually so sharp and guarded, were wide and glistening. Tears streamed down her face in silent rivers.","She shook her head. \"I don’t... I can’t...\"","\"Yes,\" Dexter said firmly. \"You did.\"","Mira’s trembling right hand released his wrist. She raised it slowly, inch by inch, the muscles straining visibly beneath her pale skin. She held it in front of her face.","Her own hand was actually moving at her command.","It looked as though it was an illusion, but they were hers.","She suddenly looked at Dexter.","\"Thank you.\"","The words were barely audible. Spoken through tears, through a throat tightened by emotion, through lips that trembled with the weight of three years of despair finally cracking open.","It was the most emotional thank you she had ever spoken in her life.","Dexter shook his head. \"There’s no need to thank me. I didn’t do much apart from the massages and taking care of you. This was all you. Your body, your will, your strength.\"","Mira shook her head firmly. The tears continued to fall, but her expression had hardened.","\"No,\" she said. Her voice was stronger now. Still cracking, but anchored by conviction. \"I don’t know what you did. I don’t know how you did it. But I know one thing for certain.\"","She looked directly into his eyes.","\"This was because of you.\"","Dexter opened his mouth to protest.","\"Don’t,\" Mira said, cutting him off. \"Don’t deny it. Don’t minimize it. Don’t stand there and pretend you had nothing to do with this.\"","Her right hand reached out again. This time, it touched his face. Her fingers, trembling and weak, brushed against his cheek. The touch was feather-light. Barely there. But it was real.","\"I thought my life was over,\" she whispered. \"I thought everything was gone. My talent. My future. My worth. Everything that made me Mira Calloway. I thought death was better than being paralyzed. I thought... I thought I was nothing.\"","Her voice broke. She swallowed hard. Continued.","\"But you changed that. You tried your best and even though I would rather die than admit it, you gradually changed my thoughts and tried your best to heal me.’","She pulled her hand back. Held it in front of her face again, staring at it as though it were the most precious thing in the world.","\"My family couldn’t do this,\" she said. \"The Calloway family. With all their wealth. All their resources. All their connections. They couldn’t do what you did.\"","She looked at him.","\"I owe you,\" she said. \"I owe you more than I can ever repay. And I don’t say things I don’t mean.\"","Dexter stared at her. He had expected an emotional reaction. He had not expected this.","\"Whatever request you want,\" Mira continued. \"No matter how despicable. No matter how evil. No matter how villainous. I will honor it. Just give me the command, and I will do as you say.\"","Dexter’s eyes widened. \"Mira, there is no need...\"","Mira raised her right hand.","The movement was deliberate. Not the instinctive grab from before. A conscious, willed motion of a hand she had only just regained control of.","She raised it high.","\"This promise,\" she said. Her voice was steady. Clear. Carrying the weight of absolute conviction. \"I swear by the Death God in the night. I swear with my soul.\"","The words left her lips in a cadence that was not conversational. It was ritualistic. Ancient. Each syllable weighted with power that predated modern cultivation systems.","Dexter’s face changed.","The air in the kitchen shifted. The temperature dropped. Not from cold, but from presence.","Something chilling that existed between the living and the dead had been summoned by the invocation of a power older than the Hero Association itself.","A shadow emerged from the ground.","It rose directly behind Mira’s wheelchair. A phantom shape, roughly humanoid, composed of darkness so dense it seemed to absorb the light around it. It had no features. No face. No expression. It simply existed, towering behind the wheelchair like a silent witness.","Mira bit her right hand.","Her teeth broke the skin of her thumb. A drop of blood, dark red and vivid, welled up from the wound.","She extended her hand downward.","The phantom image descended. It reached toward the falling drop of blood with an almost reverent slowness. Its shadowy hand caught the blood midair, cradling it as though it were a gem.","Then it sank back into the ground.","The shadow vanished. The temperature normalized. The oppressive presence disappeared as suddenly as it had arrived.","The entire event had lasted perhaps three seconds.","Dexter stared at the floor where the phantom had disappeared.","’ She just swore a Death God oath. She bound her soul to this promise.’","That meant she was dead serious!","A Death God oath was the most binding commitment a person could make. Breaking it would tear the swearer’s soul from their body. The same principle that governed the marriage contract.","Mira had just put her soul on the line for a promise to him.","Dexter looked at her solemnly.","\"Okay,\" he said quietly. He didn’t argue, nor did he protest. You didn’t argue with someone who had just sworn a Death God oath. You accept and honor it, making sure it was never abused.","Mira nodded her head as the contract was signed."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186 | Going Out","paragraphs":["Totally ignoring the fact that deh just sighed a death god contract, the wonder returned to her face as she flexed her fingers again.","Each movement was accompanied by a look of pure, childlike amazement that was so unlike her usual composed expression that.","\"Try to move the rest of your body,\" Dexter said. \"See if anything else responds.\"","Mira’s eyes lit up. But then she shook her head and spoke. \"I can feel that vitamins my right arm. My left arm and my legs are still paralyzed.\"","She paused.","\"However, I can feel the healing accelerating and my nerves are starting to reconnect.\"","She looked at Dexter with a smile.","\"By the end of this year, I should be able to move my second arm and maybe even walk.\"","Dexter smiled. \"Hopefully even before that.\"","Mira glanced at him. The smugness returned to her expression, but it was lighter now. Playful rather than defensive.","\"Don’t push it,\" she said. But she was still smiling. Still staring at her hand.","---","Dexter left her in the dining room, still mesmerized by her own hand.","He went to the kitchen, dealt with the dishes as he thought about Mira.","The 108 Body Massage Sutra, the Glove, the Grade-4 Spiritual Massage Oil, the diamond rice, the Star-Shaped Leaf tea, the Grand Cosmos Scripture, and various other things he had given herc it’s no wonder she could finally move in just a month.","It hadn’t been wasted at all. The only thing left was the bloodline. It hadn’t surfaced yet but Dexter had a feeling it needed some sort of trigger.","He shook his head. ’Will find a way to trigger the bloodline for them’","When he returned to the dining room, Mira was still there, staring at her hand and flexing her fingers.","He reached for the handles of her wheelchair to move her to the living room when she spoke.","\"I want to go out.\"","Dexter paused. \"What?\"","\"I want to go out with you,\" Mira said. \"Today. On your errands.\"","Dexter blinked and he looked down at her. She was still looking at her hand, but it eas clear she eas the one who had just spoken.","\"You want to go outside?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"With me?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Now?\"","Mira finally removed her gaze from her hand. She looked up at him with her crimson eyes.","\"I want to see the outside world with you.\"","Dexter was stunned.","Mira wanted to go outside. Mira, who hadn’t left the house since the day she arrived. Mira, who sat by the window every day and stared at nothing. Mira, who had spent a couple weeks treating the outside world as though it didn’t exist.","She wanted to go out, to see the city.","Dexter stared at her suspiciously.","\"I hope this is not you completing a request of mine. Because I didn’t ask for this.\"","Mira glared at him. \"Do you think I am that devious?\"","Dexter’s expression didn’t change. He continued to look at her with the flat, unblinking skepticism of a man who had been on the receiving end of Mira’s manipulations enough times to recognize the pattern.","Mira snorted. \"Okay. I might be that devious. But not this time. This is me wanting to go outside.\"","Dexter exhaled a breath of relief.","Then Mira raised an eyebrow. Her crimson eyes narrowed with sharp suspicion.","\"What exactly do you have planned?\" she asked. \"What request are you going to make?\"","Dexter smirked.","\"Don’t worry,\" he said. \"You’ll find out later.\"","Mira glared at him. Her face flushed. Her ears turned pink.","\"Pervert,\" she muttered.","Dexter laughed. He had no idea what she was imagining, but the fact that her mind had immediately gone somewhere inappropriate said more about her than it did about him.","\"Alright.\"","Dexter agreed to her request. But even as he agreed, a new problem presented itself.","If he took Mira out today, he was showing favoritism.","Taking one wife out while leaving the other two at home. Lyra and Selene would notice. They would feel excluded. They might not say anything, because neither of them was the type to complain openly, but the silence would be worse.","Which meant he would either have to explain himself to them, or take all three of them out. And taking all three of them out today, while running between the bakery delivery, the housing agent, and the squad meeting, was simply not practical.","Dexter was conflicted.","Mira noticed.","Her brow furrowed and the excitement in her eyes began to dim.","\"It’s fine if you don’t want to take me out,\" she said quietly.","Dexter saw her eyes.","The excitement and hope that had been building there and the anticipation of finally leaving this house flickered and faded like a candle in the wind.","And he knew exactly what she was thinking.","She thought he was embarrassed.","She thought he didn’t want to be seen in public with a cripple. A woman in a wheelchair who couldn’t walk. A broken wife who would draw stares and whispers and pity from strangers on the street.","She thought he was ashamed of her.","Dexter’s chest tightened.","\"No,\" he said quickly. \"You don’t understand. That’s not it at all.\"","Mira looked at him. The doubt in her crimson eyes was painful to see.","\"If I take you out,\" Dexter said, \"it means I’m being favorable to only you. And I would have to take all three of you out. At the same time. Otherwise it wouldn’t be fair.\"","He paused, rubbing the back of his neck.","\"But what I’m doing today involves delivering meals to the bakery, meeting with the heroes I fought alongside during the outbreak, and visiting a housing company. I’ll be moving between locations. I won’t have the time to properly look after the three of you while I’m running around. And I can’t just leave you somewhere while I handle business.\"","Mira’s eyes changed as the doubt and slight guarded hurt faded as she understood. Her eyes finally brightening.","She was about to speak when Dexter held up a hand."]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187 | The Promise","paragraphs":["\"How about this instead,\" he said. \"There’s a festival this weekend. Two days from now. Tessa mentioned it. The entire neighborhood is participating. It’s a picnic, held at Roland Stone Garden, which is close by.\"","He looked at her.","\"How about all three of you attend the festival with me? What do you think?\"","Mira blinked.","\"A festival,\" she repeated.","Dexter nodded.","Mira’s brow furrowed slightly. A festival meant crowds. Noise, and lots of people.","She didn’t know if she was ready for that.","Dexter saw the hesitation on her face and smiled gently. \"It’s fine if you don’t want to go.\"","Mira shook her head slowly. \"No. At some point I would have to go out. One way or another. It might as well be during the festival.\"","She paused as her eyes drifted to space.","\"Since everyone is attending, no one would be focused on us. It wouldn’t be bad to see the neighbors either.\"","Dexter smiled. \"Okay. I’ll tell Selene and Lyra.\"","He wheeled her to the living room and positioned her by the window. She was still staring at her right hand.","He turned toward the couch.","Lyra was there, but something was different.","She was not holding the Primordial Beast Egg.","Dexter raised an eyebrow. In the weeks since he had brought the egg home, Lyra had practically fused with it.","She carried it everywhere. On the couch. In the kitchen. To the bathroom. She cultivated with it, slept with it.","Seeing her without it was slightly odd.","’ Maybe they are taking turns?’","Dexter smiled to Lyra and spoke.","\"Lyra. Would you like to attend a festival in two days? It’s a neighborhood gathering. A picnic. Not far from here. The entire neighborhood will be there.\"","Lyra’s eyes remained closed for a moment. Then they opened.","She blinked.","Then her voice appeared in his mind.","\"Will there be food?\"","Dexter chuckled.","\"Yes. There will be food.\"","Lyra’s face lit up like a sunrise.","\"Yes. I would love to go.\"","Dexter shook his head with a quiet smile.","He walked to the backyard.","Selene was on the swing, eyes closed, cultivating.","The Primordial Beast Egg rested in her lap.","The swing moved gently in the breeze, giving her the appearance of a ghost drifting in the wind. A pale, silver-haired spirit suspended between earth and sky.","He walked directly beside her and waited.","He knew better than to speak. Selene’s Echolocation talent detected his presence through the vibrations of his footsteps and the displacement of air around his body. She knew he was there. She would acknowledge him when she was ready.","Five seconds passed.","Selene’s eyes opened.","She looked at him. And smiled.","Dexter smiled back.","And then, without warning, the memory of last night hit him.","Her head on his chest. Her arm around his torso. Her leg draped across his knee. The warmth of her body pressed against his side.","The quiet, content sound she had made in her sleep.","Heat rose within him.","Not Abyssal Flame heat. Not mana circulation heat. The other kind. The kind that had nearly destroyed his composure that morning in the bathroom and was now threatening to do it again in the backyard.","He inhaled deeply through his nose, held it and immediately exhaled slowly through his mouth.","’ Calm down, Calm down, Calm down. She is a person, not an object. She might be your wife but they might not see you as their husband. Moreover, you are still a very busy man with responsibilities but here you are thinking about crazy things... what the hell did I take?’","The rising heat subsided but not by much. However, it was manageable.","He spoke.","\"Selene. Would you like to go out for a festival in two days? It’s a picnic, not far from here. The entire neighborhood will be participating.\"","Selene blinked her pale, sightless eyes.","Then she slowly nodded.","Dexter was stunned. He had expected resistance and hesitation.","Of the three women, Selene had been the most withdrawn and then most guarded. The most reluctant to engage with the world beyond the walls of the bungalow.","But she had said yes.","Without argument or hesitation not did she even think much about it.","She had simply nodded.","Then she smiled.","\"Good luck,\" she said.","Dexter blinked and he understood. She was wishing him well for his errands. The bakery delivery, the housing agent and the squad meeting.","\"Thank you,\" he said. \"And bye.\"","\"Bye.\"","He turned and walked back inside.","---","He reached the front door and opened it. Before stepping out, he turned back toward the living room.","\"Bye, everyone. I’m leaving.\"","Lyra’s voice echoed in his mind. \"Bye.\"","Mira didn’t respond verbally. She was still staring at her right hand, flexing her fingers with the absorbed concentration of a scientist studying a new species.","Dexter leaned back inside.","\"Mira. Don’t open the door for anyone.\"","A laugh rang out from the living room.","An actual laugh from Mira sounded out.","He was quite stunned by this as it sounded genuine as though she found his joke funny.","Dexter paused, then he realized why she was laughing.","For three weeks, he had been telling Mira not to open the door for anyone. It had been a running gag between them, born from the fact that Mira was paralyzed from the neck down and physically incapable of opening any door.","It was a playful tease. A small, joke to annoy Mira whenever he was leaving the house.","And it had always worked. But now, she could actually move her right arm!","Which meant that she could open a door!","The joke that had been harmless for three weeks had suddenly become real, and the irony of it had struck Mira with enough force to make her chuckle unexpectedly.","Dexter shook his head at his own expense.","\"Right,\" he muttered. \"Note to self. Update the jokes.\"","He stepped outside, closed the door behind him, and walked to the SUV parked in front of the house."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188 | The Appointment","paragraphs":["The drive to the bakery took five minutes.","Dexter parked behind a small sedan in the lot beside the bakery, killed the engine, and checked the time on his phone.","9:15 AM.","Not late but not particularly early either. The bakery opened at seven, and by eight to nine, the morning rush was in full swing.","He climbed out of the SUV, retrieved two large bags from the back seat, and walked inside. Each bag contained twenty-five sealed containers of Grade One Arcane Meals.","When he entered, he saw that the bakery was crowded.","Every table was occupied and then line at the counter almost stretched to the door.","Parents in work clothes waited with tired expressions while children tugged at their sleeves and pointed at the pastry display.","Two teenage girls in school uniforms were sharing a croissant and giggling over something on one of their phones.","The smell in the bakery was incredible. Fresh bread, roasted coffee, butter and sugar, it was really nice.","Tessa appeared to possess some kind of sixth sense for Dexter as the moment he stepped through the door, her head popped up from behind the counter as her green eyes found him immediately across the crowded room.","She waved, turned to the staff member beside her, said something brief, and then wove through the customers toward him.","\"Good morning,\" she said, arriving at his side with a bright smile. She looked him up and down. \"You clean up quite good.\"","Dexter was slightly startled by the comment.","He immediately chose to ignore her.","\"Where should I drop these?\" he asked, lifting the two bags slightly.","Tessa’s eyes widened at the size of the bags. \"Come. Back here.\"","She led him through the narrow hallway behind the counter, into the small storage room at the back of the bakery. Steel shelves lined the walls, filled with ingredient containers, baking supplies, and spare equipment.","\"Place them here,\" Tessa said, pointing to an empty section of shelf. \"I’ll display about ten out front. When those sell out, I’ll restock from back here. If everything goes like yesterday, we won’t need to restock more than twice.\"","Dexter set the bags down and began stacking the containers neatly on the shelves. White boxes with tight-sealing lids, each one containing a portion of Comfort Chicken Rice. The smell of seasoned chicken and ginger seeped through the seals, mingling with the bakery’s existing aroma of bread and butter.","Tessa watched him stack them with a particular gleam again in her eyes.","\"These will probably sell out before 5 PM today,\" she said.","Dexter straightened up and looked at her. \"I hope so.\"","Then he saw the gleam.","His eyes narrowed.","\"You’re not increasing your commission again, are you? Because I can’t go higher than the twenty-five percent you already stole from me.\"","Tessa smirked. \"Stolen? I worked hard for that twenty-five percent. I sold the food. I handled the customers. I answered questions. I—\"","\"Fine! Fine! You did everything. You worked hard for it.\"","Dexter rolled his eyes.","\"Alright. I’m leaving. Have a good one.\"","\"Bye, Boss Chef!\"","Tessa waved him off with a cheerful grin and dollar signs in her eyes.","---","Dexter climbed back into the SUV and pulled up the address for Harvest Homes on his phone.","The navigation system calculated a thirty-minute drive from the bakery to the mid-district. He merged onto the main highway and settled in for the drive.","The city scrolled past his windows. Billboards advertised everything from. Hero gear to Dungeon insurance to Mana supplements to even Guild recruitment drives.","Twenty-eight minutes later, Dexter pulled into the parking garage beneath the Harvest Homes building.","He stepped out of the SUV, looked up, stopped, and was really stunned.","The building was really extraordinary.","It wasn’t very tall but was something else entirely. The Harvest Homes building was a work of art.","The structure more than 70 floors, but its height was not what made it remarkable, it was the design.","It looked like someone had brought a massive mountain cliff into the city.","Water fell from the top of the buiding, rushing straight to the ground. Living plants grew from integrated balconies on every floor, cascading downward in rivers of green.","It was difficult to describe.","Dexter stared at the building for a long moment.","He had seen impressive architecture before. The Ashford estate had been grandiose, the Hero Association headquarters was imposing and the Grand Meridian hotel had been luxurious.","But this was different.","He shook his head. In an age of heroes, where people possessed abilities that could mold stone, shape metal, and grow plants at will, extraordinary construction was simply the natural result of extraordinary talents applied to ordinary problems.","He walked through the archway and into the lobby.","The interior matched the exterior. It was really a thing of beauty.","A reception desk sat in the center of the lobby. Several receptionists were stationed behind it.","Dexter walked to the nearest available desk.","The receptionist was a beautiful young woman with blonde buzz-cut hair and sharp, angular features.","If not for two rather bumps on her chest, pushing against her fitted blazer, Dexter might have assumed she was a very handsome young man.","She looked up as he approached and smiled.","\"Good morning. Welcome to Harvest Homes. How may I help you?\"","\"Good morning. I’m Dexter Ashford. I have a ten o’clock appointment with Jennifer.\"","The receptionist’s fingers moved across her keyboard, then studied her screen for a moment, as she smiled.","\"Ah, yes. Dexter Ashford, ten o’clock with Jennifer. We’ve been expecting you.\" She gestured toward the elevator on the far wall.","\"Please head to the twenty-fourth floor. You’ll be met by someone there.\"","Dexter thanked her and walked toward the elevators.","A soft chime sounded and the door in front of him slid open silently, revealing a couple was already inside.","The man wore a tailored grey suit and the woman wore a designer dress and heels that added several inches to her height."]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189 | Choosing A Home","paragraphs":["They were standing close together, the woman’s hand resting on the man’s arm.","As the door began to close, the man noticed Dexter approaching. He reached out and pressed the open button. The door reversed, sliding back open.","Dexter stepped inside. \"Thank you.\"","The man nodded and smiled politely.","The woman glanced at Dexter. Her eyes moved from his face to his clothes to his shoes.","Then her brow furrowed slightly as she looked at her boyfriend then she let out a soft snort.","Dexter remained expressionless.","He pressed the button for the 24th floor.","The elevator began to rise and it felt like floating upward on a cloud of air, the floor numbers ticking past on the display panel beside the door in soft, glowing digits.","At the 20th floor, the elevator stopped and the doors opened as the couple stepped out.","As they exited, the man glanced back at Dexter. His expression carried a trace of apology.","The woman didn’t look back as the doors closed and the elevator continued upward.","Dexter stood alone as he chuckled. \"Women...\"","\"Ding!\"","The doors opened and Dexter stepped out into the hallway.","He had expected Jennifer to meet him, the woman he had spoken to on the phone but was instead met with a middle-aged man.","The middle-aged man came striding toward him from the far end of the corridor.","The man was... uhm... Fat.","Not fat, exactly, but heavy.","But his stomach was in the bigger side, stretching his dark blue suit very wide.","His face was round and ruddy, with thick lips and small eyes that crinkled into a smile when he saw Dexter.","\"Dexter Ashford!\" his voice booming through the hallway.","He immediately crossed the distance in a flash and grabbed Dexter’s hand before Dexter could offer it and shook his hands enthusiastically!","\"Welcome, welcome! You’re very much welcome! Come, come, come. Let’s go to my office.\"","Dexter frowned slightly. He glanced past the man, looking for Jennifer but the hallway was currently empty.","\"I was supposed to meet Jennifer,\" Dexter forcefully removed his hand and spoke..","The man waved a dismissive hand. \"Yes, yes. Jennifer is one of our junior staff. She handles the initial phone inquiries and is very good at what she does. But for property consultations of this nature, the company felt it best that someone with more experience handle your case personally.\"","He smiled broadly. \"And that someone is me. Marcus Webb, Senior Property Consultant.\"","He extended his hand again. Dexter didn’t shake it and simply glanced at him.","’ He’s looking quite sketchy...’","\"Please, here, come with me to my office.\"","Dexter filed the observation away and followed Marcus down the corridor.","The office was at the far end and marcus opened the door with a flourish and gestured Dexter inside.","The office was tidy. A large iron desk dominated the center of the room and its surface was clean except for a tablet, a stylus, and a small potted plant.","But it was the wall behind the desk that caught Dexter’s attention.","Weapons.","Three swords hung on the wall, mounted on individual display shelf.","Type One, Type Two, Type Three weapons!","Dexter’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Relic weapons and three of them at the moment.","Displayed openly on an office wall like hunting trophies.","Marcus noticed him looking and smiled proudly. \"Collectibles. A hobby of mine. The Type Three was a gift from a client who was very happy with the property I found him.\"","Dexter said nothing. Real estate agents in this city earned well. That was no secret. The most successful ones dealt with properties worth tens of millions of credits. A Type Three relic on the wall was the equivalent of a luxury car gift to someone people.","Marcus sat behind his desk with a grunt and gestured toward the leather chair opposite. \"Please, sit, sit.\"","Dexter sat.","Marcus leaned forward, his small eyes bright with enthusiasm. \"Now. I understand you are searching for a property. A home. Somewhere to live.\"","Dexter nodded. \"Yes. I’m looking for a simple house. At least four bedrooms. In a decent neighborhood.\"","Marcus clapped his hands together. \"Perfect. That is exactly the kind of request I love to hear.\"","He tapped his tablet and a holographic display materialized above the desk, projecting a three-dimensional map of Stargate City.","The city was rendered in miniature, with districts color-coded by zoning type and property value.","Small icons marked available properties, each one pulsing gently.","\"Now,\" Marcus said, manipulating the display with practiced gestures. \"As you may know, the rate of gate openings and monster outbreaks has increased across the city in recent months. This has driven up demand for residential properties in stable districts. Various families have been investing heavily in new developments, particularly in the outer rings where land is cheaper and security formations can be installed from scratch.\"","He zoomed the map outward, showing the ring of new developments along the city’s perimeter.","\"Several new estates have been completed in the last month.\"","The holographic display shifted, showing a series of newly developed neighborhoods, houses, townhouses, small estates.","Each one rendered in three-dimensional detail with specifications, pricing, and availability floating beside them.","Dexter studied the display.","Marcus swiped through several options. A townhouse in the western district. A duplex near the commercial ring. A mid-size family home in the northern sector.","Dexter’s eyes moved across the properties without interest. None of them felt right.","Then Marcus swiped to the next property, and Dexter’s hand shot out.","\"Wait.\"","Marcus paused as he swiped back.","Dexter looked at the image.","It was a two-story house with white exterior and dark roof.","It also has its front porch covered with a wooden railing wnd a small garden in the front with a path leading from the gate to the door. Behind the house, a backyard with enough space for a garden, a patio, and maybe a training area.","It was in a standard suburban neighborhood that looked and felt quite to Dexter.","But the most important detail was the location!","The house was at the eastern edge of Stargate City, at the far edge and the boundary where the city’s developed territory met the wilderness buffer zone that separated urban civilization from the untamed regions beyond.","It was far from the central district and far from the political heart of the city where the Nine Families schemed and maneuvered.","Far from the Ashfords, the Calloways, the Vances and far from the Frosts.","Moreover, it was isolated and completely anonymous.","Dexter felt something settle in his chest like he’d seen what scarily he wanted.","\"This one,\" he said. \"This is perfect.\"","Marcus beamed. \"Excellent eye! Excellent eye indeed.\" He tapped the property icon, and a detailed specification sheet expanded beside the house.","Property: Harvest Crest Residence, Plot 47","Type: Two-Story Single Family Home","Bedrooms: 5","Bathrooms: 3","Floor Area: 320 square meters","Lot Area: 450 square meters","Features: Integrated defense formation (Tier 2), climate-controlled interior, mana-infused foundation, private backyard, covered garage, storage basement","Year Built: Current Year (3 weeks prior)","Status: Unoccupied","Neighborhood Status: Newly developed. Low population density. 12 of 30 plots occupied.","\"The entire estate was completed just three weeks ago,\" Marcus smiled","Dexter nodded slowly and interrupted him. \"How much?\"","Marcus’s smile widened. \"This particular property is priced at nine million credits.\"","Dexter’s expression didn’t change.","But inside his mind, he chuckled bitterly.","Nine million credits."]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190 | Purchase","paragraphs":["\"How much?\"","Marcus’s smile widened. \"This particular property is priced at nine million Dollars.\"","Dexter’s expression didn’t change.","But inside his mind, he chuckled bitterly.","Nine million Dollars.","His bank account held 1.2 million.","He had walked into this building thinking his 1.2 million might be enough to purchase a decent home outright but he eas dead wrong.","If was even less than twenty percent of the asking price and wasn’t even close.","He kept his face neutral as he spoke.","\"Alright, I’ll come back later when I have the funds.\"","He placed both hands on the armrests, preparing to stand.","Marcus’s smile faltered for a second before he quickly spoke and raised his hands.","\"No, no, no. Wait, please sit. There’s no need to leave just yet.\"","Dexter paused as he glanced at Marcus for a while before he lowered himself back into the chair.","\"We have options,\" Marcus continued, his smile returning. \"For clients who have not yet gathered the full purchase price, we offer flexible installment plans.\"","He tapped the tablet and a new display appeared, showing three payment plan options.","\"We have a three-month plan, a six-month plan, and a twelve-month plan. Each one allows you to move into the property immediately upon payment of the first installment.\"","Dexter blinked. \"Move in immediately?\"","\"Immediately,\" Marcus confirmed. \"The first payment secures the property. You receive the keys and the provisional deed. The property is yours to live in, to use, to make your home. Subsequent payments are made monthly until the full amount is settled, at which point the final deed is transferred to your name.\"","Dexter listened attentively. \"What are the terms?\"","Marcus leaned forward. \"Let’s take the twelve-month plan, for example. The total purchase price under the twelve-month plan is twelve million Dollars.\"","He tapped the display.","\"Monthly payment: one million Dollars per month for twelve months.\"","Dexter frowned. \"One million per month.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"That’s twelve million total. Three million more than the asking price! Dexter was quite stunned at the greed of this company.","Marcus spread his hands. \"That’s the interest and it’s a standard rate too. Every property developer in the city charges the same rate and some even charge more.\"","Dexter frowned as he sat back in his chair.","One million per month while he currently had 1.2 million. That would cover the first payment and leave him with roughly 220,000 Dollars.","But he needed to make one million Dollars every month for twelve months which places burden on him by quite a lot.","The bakery business was generating approximately 90,000 dollars per day in gross sales.","After Tessa’s 25 percent commission, his net was about 67,500 Dollars per day. If he sold fifty portions daily, that was roughly 2 million dollars per month.","But that was just the gross price. He needed to subtract ingredient costs, which ran about 20,000 dollars per day for fifty portions.","That left roughly 1.4 million net per month from the bakery alone.","Add dungeon raiding income, and the math worked.","But it was tight. But then, the house was truly perfect.","Five bedrooms. One for each wife. One for himself and a real house in a real neighborhood where no one knew their names.","He thought more about it.","\"Okay,\" Dexter said. \"I’ll take the twelve-month plan.\"","Marcus’s face lit up like a sunrise. \"Excellent decision! Very good decision! I promise you, you will not regret this.\"","He practically lunged for his desk drawer, pulling out a stack of documents with the speed of a man who had closed this particular deal a hundred times and had the paperwork memorized.","\"Sign here. And here. And here. And one more here.\"","He placed four documents in front of Dexter, each one marked with a highlighted signature line. Dexter read each one carefully, his eyes scanning the legal language for hidden clauses, unfavorable terms, or the kind of small print that the Ashford family had used to trap three families into marrying their daughters to a bastard.","The documents were clean. Standard purchase agreement. Installment terms. Property transfer schedule. Default clause that returned the property to Harvest Homes if payments were missed for three consecutive months.","He signed all four.","Marcus produced an account number. \"Please transfer the first payment to this account. Once the transfer is confirmed, the process begins.\"","Dexter pulled out his phone, opened his banking app, and initiated the transfer. One million Dollars.","[Transfer sent: 1,000,000 Dollars]","The confirmation appeared on Marcus’s tablet within seconds. The man’s smile became almost blindingly bright.","\"Wonderful! Wonderful! The transfer is confirmed.\" He reached into his drawer again and pulled out a leather folder. Inside was a document embossed with the Harvest Homes seal.","\"This is your provisional housing deed,\" Marcus said, presenting it with both hands as though it were a royal decree. \"It confirms your ownership of the property pending completion of all installment payments. Once the final payment is made, this will be replaced with the permanent deed.\"","He then placed a small envelope on the desk.","\"And these are your keys.\"","Dexter took the envelope. Inside were two keys and a small electronic fob.","A thought struck him.","The system had given him the actual deed to his current bungalow, revealing that the Ashford family’s original documents had been fake. He was the true, legal owner of the bungalow.","Which meant he could sell it.","The bungalow, despite its run-down condition, sat on a plot of land in a developed neighborhood.","Even in poor condition, the land alone was worth something, enough to pad his remaining balance.","He would look into it later.","Marcus stood up, his round belly shifting as he rose. He extended his hand.","\"Let me be the first to congratulate you, Mr. Ashford. You are now the proud owner of a Harvest Crest residence.\"","Dexter stood and shook his hand. \"Thank you.\"","Marcus grabbed a tablet and pulled up a map. \"The property is located in Edge District 3, about forty minutes from the city center. I can have someone accompany you to the property for a walkthrough if you’d like.\"","Dexter shook his head. \"No need. I’ll go alone.\"","Marcus blinked. \"Alone? Are you sure? I could send an agent to show you around the neighborhood, introduce you to the local amenities, explain the defense formation system...\"","\"No,\" Dexter said firmly. \"I’ll go alone.\"","There was something about Marcus that Dexter didn’t quite trust. It wasn’t anything specific. The man was professional. The documents were clean. The transaction had been straightforward.","But he still felt something was wrong.","Dexter pocketed the keys, placed the deed in his spatial storage, and headed for the door."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191 | The House","paragraphs":["\"Thank you for your assistance, Marcus.\"","\"My pleasure! Absolutely my pleasure! And if you have any questions, don’t hesitate to call.\"","Dexter nodded once and stepped into the hallway.","The elevator ride down was smooth and silent. He stepped out into the lobby, walked through the marble archway, and emerged into the morning sunlight.","He stood on the plaza for a moment, looking up at the extraordinary building with its cascading plants and prismatic glass.","He had a house now.","He pulled out his phone and checked the time.","9:47 AM.","Plasmatic Man’s meeting was at twelve. He had two hours.","Two hours to drive to his new house, see it for the first time, and decide if it was truly as perfect as the holographic image had suggested.","Dexter walked to his SUV, climbed in, and entered the address into the navigation system.","Destination: Harvest Crest Residence, Plot 47, Edge District 3.","Estimated drive time: 38 minutes.","He started the engine and pulled out of the parking garage.","He needed to see the house first, Needed to verify that the holographic images and the enthusiastic sales pitch matched reality.","---","The drive took 42 minutes.","He drove through the city and then the city ended.","Instead, the urban landscape simply... ran out. The last row of houses faced an open expanse of cleared land, beyond which the wilderness buffer zone began.","There were trees, grasses and distant silhouette of mountains on the horizon.","Dexter turned into the development.","He drove slowly, studying the neighborhood through the windshield.","Marcus had described it as a newly built estate, and the description was accurate.","The houses were fresh with the streets smooth, newly paved asphalt without a single crack or pothole and also standing street lamp.","Of the thirty plots in the development, perhaps twelve showed signs of occupancy with cars in driveways.","Furniture visible through windows and even a child’s bicycle foils be seen leaning against a fence. The rest were unoccupied as of yet.","The entire place was silence not too silent but was a comfortable kind of sileve.","Dexter found Plot 47 at the end of a cul-de-sac.","He parked on the street and got out.","The house looked exactly as it had in the holographic display with white exterior, dark roof and front porch with a steel railing. A small garden space in the front too.","He walked to the front gate and pushed it.","He could feel it was a grade one steel and could withstand significant force.","Wild monsters could break through it eventually, but it would hold long enough for the neighborhood’s defense formation to activate and for residents to take shelter.","He walked up the path to the front door and used his new key to open it.","Dexter stepped inside.","The house was just as he expected, clean and fresh.","The living room was spacious, larger than the entire ground floor of the bungalow.","There was room for multiple sofas, a coffee table, a television unit, and still enough open space for someone to move around comfortably, or for a wheelchair to navigate without bumping into anything.","He walked through the living room into the dining area and it was large enough for a table that could seat six or even eight, if you pushed it.","The kitchen was twice the size of his kitchen at the bungalow, it was enormous, running along two full walls with an island in the center.","The stove was a commercial-grade unit with six burners and a built-in oven and the sink was deep and wide and looked quite flashy.","Cabinet space lined every wall, floor to ceiling and enough storage to hold ingredients, equipment, and supplies for a small-scale Foodsmith operation.","There was even a separate pantry room off to the side. A dedicated space for dry goods, spices, and bulk ingredients.","Dexter ran his hand along the counter with slight smile on his face.","’This kitchen could feed an army.’","He moved on to the bedroom and it was large also, large enough for a queen bed, a wardrobe, and a desk.","This would be perfect for Mira as it was ground floor access and didn’t need stairs to navigate and was also close to the bathroom, which was right next door.","The bathroom was fully equipped with walk-in shower, deep bathtub and dual sinks.","Everything looked brand new, which meant it was ever used.","He went upstairs.","Three bedrooms. Each one larger than the bedrooms at the bungalow. Each one with its own window, its own closet space, and access to a second bathroom that was identical in design to the one downstairs.","Dexter stood in the largest of the upstairs bedrooms and looked out the window. The backyard stretched out below him with enough space for a garden, a patio and maybe a small training area, if he sectioned off a corner and installed some equipment.","Beyond the backyard, the iron fence marked the property boundary.","It was quiet, private and I solated.","Dexter nodded slowly.","The girls would like this.","Mira would have her ground-floor bedroom, giving her independence and dignity without the humiliation of being carried up stairs.","Selene would have a quiet room where she could cultivate in peace, far from the noise and chaos of the old neighborhood. Lyra would have space for her egg, her chips, and whatever else she wanted to accumulate.","And he would have a kitchen that could actually handle the volume of cooking he needed to do for both the household and the bakery business.","He smiled.","’ This is quite perfect!’","He locked up, returned to the SUV, and checked his phone.","A message from Cole Stanley.","[Hey Dexter. We’re meeting at Janice’s Cuisine, 24 Thourist Plaza, Central District. Booth 24. We’ll be there by noon. See you there!]","Dexter raised an eyebrow. The restaurant was quite popular, he didn’t expect them to go to ont if the most expensive restaurants in the city.","He entered the address into the GPS, the Central District which was twenty-five minutes from his current location.","He started the engine and was about to move when a large man stood in front of his car.","\"Who are you and what are you doing coming out from my building?\"","---"]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192 | What Are You Doing In My Home?","paragraphs":["Dexter opened the car door, sat down and then started the engine.","However, a figure suddenly appeared in front of the vehicle.","Dexter’s foot paused over the accelerator.","A muscular man stood directly in his path and his face was set in an aggressive scowl as he glared at Dexter through the glass.","\"Who are you?\" the man demanded with a loud voice. \"What were you doing inside my building?\"","Dexter was stunned.","He turned off the engine, opened the door, and stepped out.","\"Your building?\"","The man’s scowl deepened.","He moved from the front of the SUV to the passenger side, closing the distance between himself and Dexter like he Wa about to fight.","\"So you’re one of those people,\" the man sneered. \"One of those people who break into houses and squat there for free once they see it’s empty.\"","He pulled out his phone.","\"I’m calling the cops on you right now.\"","Dexter’s stomach dropped.","But it wasn’t from fear but sinking else entirely as realization began to hit him.","’ No .’","He raised both hands calmly. \"Hold on. There’s a misunderstanding.\"","He turned back to the SUV, reached into the center console where he had placed the documents, and pulled out the leather folder Marcus had given him and then opened it as he held it out toward the man.","\"Look. I have documents. From Harvest Homes. I signed a purchase agreement. I have a deed. I have keys.\"","The man looked at the documents. His eyes scanned the Harvest Homes letterhead and a few things.","Slowly, his scowl faltered as he frowned in confusion, shich caused him to Lowe his phone and cut off the call he was making.","\"Harvest Homes doesn’t deal with properties in this neighborhood,\" the man said slowly. \"This estate is managed by Crestline Properties. They’re the exclusive sales agent for this development. Harvest Homes has no authority to sell anything here.\"","Dexter’s face changed and the feeling in the pit of his stomach grew even more.","\"What about the key?\" Dexter said, his voice tight. \"The key opened the door. The key you gave me opened the door.\"","He was talking to himself now as much as to the man.","’ The key worked and the door opened which meant that the property exists and the sale was real. Right?’","But deep down, he knew he had been scammed.","One million dollars,transferred less than an hour ago.","The man was looking at Dexter with an expression that had shifted from suspicion to pity.","He had clearly seen the name. Dexter Ashford and knew who he was, the one the news had been talking about. The one married to three crippled women.","\"Look,\" the man said, his voice softer now. \"I don’t know why you have my key. I just bought this house last month. I’m still moving in. Can I have the key back? I feel uncomfortable with someone else having a key to my home.\"","Dexter stared at the man. His mind was racing rapidly.","’Harvest Homes is a real company. A registered business. They can’t just disappear. Their office is in the mid-district. Their building exists. Their employees exist. Marcus Webb exists.’","’Even if the sale was fake, the scammer is still there. Still reachable. Still findable.’","\"And as for Harvest Homes,\" the man continued, his voice hardening, \"I’ll be reporting them to the appropriate authorities. If they have keys to my house, they might have keys to other people’s houses in this neighborhood too. This won’t stand.\"","Dexter nodded numbly.","\"Let me make a call,\" he said.","He pulled out his phone. Found Marcus’s number in the documents and pressed dial.","The phone rang and then the call connected.","\"Hello, yes, you’re speaking to Marcus.\"","The familiar, cheerful voice. The same warm tone the man had used while shaking Dexter’s hand and sliding documents across his desk.","\"Marcus,\" Dexter said. \"This is Dexter. Dexter Ashford. The man you just sold a house to in Edge District 3.\"","A pause on the line.","\"I’m having a problem,\" Dexter continued, keeping his voice level. \"There’s another man standing in front of me right now. He claims to be the owner of the house. He says he bought it last month from a different agency.\"","Silence on the line.","Then Marcus laughed.","It was not the professional, warm laugh Dexter had heard in the office. This was different. It was cold and sinister. The laugh of a man who had been waiting for this moment and found it amusing.","\"Oh!\" Marcus said, his voice bright with genuine delight. \"You actually met the owner! That’s quite fortunate. I was thinking of stringing you along for two or three months. Collecting a few more payments. Maybe two or three million more before you realized.\"","Dexter’s blood went cold.","\"What do you mean by that?\"","Marcus’s tone shifted. The warmth vanished entirely. What replaced it was the casual, unconcerned voice of a man who had done this before and knew there would be no consequences.","\"What can I say? It has nothing to do with me. It has everything to do with your family.\"","He paused.","\"Courtesy of the Ashford family.\"","The words landed like a hammer blow.","\"No home agency in their right mind would ever sell you a home,\" Marcus continued, his voice carrying the smug confidence of someone who knew they were untouchable. \"Everybody knows the Ashford family controls this city. And they’ve spoken. If you need a home, we can simply take your money and sell you a fake one.\"","Dexter’s grip on the phone tightened. His knuckles went white.","\"Aren’t you scared of the authorities?\" Dexter asked. His voice was quiet. Controlled. But something beneath it was beginning to fracture.","Marcus laughed again. Longer this time. More genuine.","\"The authorities? Are you truly that ignorant? The Ashford family controls over half the authorities in this city. The only thing they don’t control is the Hero Association. And the Hero Association will never involve itself in personal matters. Especially family feuds.\"","His voice dropped, becoming almost conversational.","\"So there is nothing you can do.\""]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193 | Choose One...","paragraphs":["\"There’s nothing you can do!\"","There was a beat of silence before he spoke again.","\"If that is all, I’m pretty sure the Ashford family will be very impressed with what I’ve done. I’ll gain a few favors from them. So I’ve got to say...\"","He paused.","\"Thank you very much for this.\"","He suddenly chuckled which grew into a mocking laughter as he need the call.","\"Ding!\" \"Ding!\" \"Ding!\"","Dexter stood in the street, phone pressed against his ear, listening to the dead tone of a disconnected call.","The man, the real owner, stood a few meters away. He had heard everything. His face changed sligrhtk as he looked at Dexter with uncomfortable pity.","He looked at Dexter the way people look at stray dogs in the rain.","Dexter lowered the phone.","He looked at the key in his hand expressionlessly.","One million Dollars.","His hard-earned money, money he had earned through sweat and labor and the systematic suppression of his own abilities. Money that was supposed to buy his family a home was now gone and stolen.","By a man who had done it on the Ashford family’s orders.","Dexter’s face was scarily blank.","He turned to the man and held out the key.","\"I’m sorry for the inconvenience,\" he said in a mechanical tone.","The man took the key but didn’t say anything.","Dexter ignored the man and climbed into the SUV, started the engine and pulled away from the curb.","---","The Harvest Homes building looked the same as it had two hours ago. The cascading plants. The prismatic glass. The marble archway. The water features with their lazy koi.","Dexter didn’t see any of it.","He parked the SUV in the garage, killed the engine, and walked toward the building.","He entered the lobby.","The blonde receptionist looked up as he passed.","\"Sir! Sir, who would you like to meet?\"","Dexter ignored her.","He walked straight past the reception desk, past the waiting area, past the art displays and the living walls, and pressed the elevator call button.","\"Sir, you can’t just go up without an appointment!\"","The elevator doors opened. Dexter stepped inside. Pressed 24. The doors closed.","The elevator rose.","The doors opened.","Two men stood in the hallway.","They were large. Both taller than Dexter by several inches. Both wider. Both carrying the unmistakable physical density of peak Superhuman Realm cultivators. They wore dark suits that had been tailored to accommodate bodies built like refrigerators.","Their arms were folded across their chests. Their expressions were professionally neutral.","Marcus had called ahead. Of course he had. He knew Dexter would come back. One million Dollars was not a small sum, especially not to a man who had nothing. Marcus had expected this. Had prepared for it.","The first bodyguard spoke in a very deep tone.","\"Mr. Dexter. Please turn around and leave. You have no business here. Go home before you embarrass yourself.\"","Dexter looked at them.","Then he smiled.","It was not a warm smile. It was not a friendly smile. It was the smile of a man who had spent the last hour compressing an overwhelming amount of rage into a space approximately the size of a fist, and was now feeling the quiet, focused clarity that came on the other side of that compression.","\"Okay,\" Dexter said.","Then he activated Flame Burst Step.","The air ignited beneath his feet. A concussive bang echoed through the hallway as his speed multiplied fivefold. The world blurred as the marble floor cracked beneath the force of his launch.","He appeared in front of the first bodyguard before the man’s brain had finished processing the word \"okay.\"","His open palm struck the bodyguard’s chest.","\"BOOM!\"","The impact was devastating. A shockwave exploded outward from the point of contact, shattering the overhead light fixtures and sending cracks spider-webbing across the marble floor. The bodyguard’s feet left the ground entirely. His massive frame became a projectile, hurtling backward through the hallway until he collided with the wall.","CRACK!","A human-shaped dent appeared in the reinforced concrete. The bodyguard slid downward, groaning, his suit torn, his chest caved inward by a palm strike that carried the full force of a Tenth Stage Superhuman with an Ancient Grade Flame Demon Bloodline.","The second bodyguard reacted faster.","His eyes widened and his body shifted into a combat stance as he threw a punch aimed directly at Dexter’s jaw, his fist cutting through the air with the insane speed and poer.","However, Dexter didn’t dodge and simply smirked coldly as he punched back.","Fist met fist.","\"BOOM!\"","The shockwave was enormous as the entire hallway walls shuddered, the ceiling panels rattled and a decorative vase on a nearby table shattered.","Even the air itself seemed to compress and rebound, sending a visible ripple of force radiating outward in all directions.","Neither combatant moved a single inch. The bodyguard’s eyes went wide, clearly stunned.","He was a peak Superhuman and had trained for years, fought monsters, criminals, and villains. He had never, in his entire career, met someone at a lower cultivation realm who could match his raw physical strength.","But this man had just stopped his full-power punch with an equal punch of his own eithout even changing expression.","The bodyguard was strong but Dexter’s body wasn’t made of foam either. One might even say he was stronger than him.","Before the bodyguard could recover from his shock, Dexter activated Flame Burst Step again.","He vanished.","The bodyguard roared as he activated his Talent.","His entire body turned silver, his muscles densified and his bones reinforced as he became a living statue of refined metal.","Dexter reappeared behind him. His fist drove into the bodyguard’s back.","\"BANG!\"","It was like punching a steel wall. The silver technique absorbed the kinetic energy, dispersing it across the bodyguard’s entire frame. The man barely staggered.","But Dexter wasn’t finished.","He smirked.","Blue lightning exploded from his knuckles.","The Thunder Manipulation talent, extracted from the dead assassin on the highway, activated at maximum output.","Crackling arcs of electricity poured from Dexter’s hand into the bodyguard’s body, bypassing the metallic defense entirely. Electricity didn’t care about physical hardness. It cared about conductivity. And the bodyguard’s silver-coated body was essentially one giant conductor.","The bodyguard screamed.","His entire body seized, his muscles locked as the silver talent covering his entire body flickered as his skin turned brown and then silver and eventually, it died as the electrical current overwhelmed his nervous system.","His eyes instantly rolled back and his jaw clenched unconsciously so hard that blood appeared at the corner of his lips as he collapsed to the ground.","\"Thud!\"","His bidy twitched involuntarily as residual electricity arced across his skin.","Dexter didn’t care and simply stepped over him.","He walked to Marcus’s office door, grabbed the handle and turned it."]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194 | Anger (1)","paragraphs":["The door swung open and Marcus could be seen seated in his seat, right behind the desk.","There were lots of documents on his desk as he wrote something down with a self-satisfied smile on his round, ruddy face.","As the door opened, Marcus didn’t bother to look up.","\"Is it done?\" he asked casually, his pen still moving. \"Have you chased the bastard away?\"","There was a bit of silence and then a voice spoke.","\"Yes. It is done.\"","Marcus still didn’t look up as he chuckled and continued writing.","\"Good. If that is all, just keep guarding. The bastard might come back again.\"","There was another silence throughout out the entire room.","Just when Marcus was feeling something was wrong, a fist came down on the iron desk..","\"CRACK!\"","The metal and glass desk instablt shattered as though made of wood as the entire surface exploded into pieces, splitting apart Instantly.","A massive shockwave of pure physical force ripped through the air as documents were sent flying.","Marcus’s was stunned and he raised his head. At that exact moment, his heart skipped a beat as the Marcus’s his face vanished like an illusion.","Dexter stood on the other side of what used to be a desk. His fist was still pressed into the wreckage and his eyes were cold.","Marcus’s face went pale and the ruddy complexion drained to a sickly grey in approximately one second. His mouth opened. No sound came out.","Dexter reached across the wreckage of the desk, grabbed Marcus by the throat, and lifted him out of his chair.","Marcus weighed over a hundred kilograms. Dexter lifted him with one hand as though he were a bag of feathers.","The man’s feet dangled in the air. His hands clawed at Dexter’s grip. His face turned from grey to red to purple as the pressure on his throat cut off blood flow and air simultaneously.","Dexter held him there. At eye level. Close enough that Marcus could see every detail of Dexter’s face. Close enough to see that there was no bluff in his eyes. No negotiation. No room for talk.","Dexter smiled.","\"Either you give me my money,\" he said, his voice light, almost pleasant, \"or you die. Choose one.\"","Marcus’s eyes bulged. Sweat poured down his forehead, running into his eyes and mixing with the tears that had begun to leak from the corners. His lips moved, producing choked, wheezing sounds that couldn’t quite form words.","\"Wait,\" he managed, the word barely audible through his crushed throat. \"Wait, wait, wait. I’ll send you your money. I’ll send it right now. Don’t do anything rash. Don’t do anything rash.\"","He gasped, his face contorting with desperate urgency.","\"But the money is with the company. It’s not with me. I’m just a messenger. I’m just a messenger for the higher-ups. I had nothing to do with the decision. I’m just a messenger. I just did what I was told.\"","Dexter’s smile didn’t waver.","\"Didn’t you say you wanted to curry favor with the Ashford family?\" he asked, tilting his head slightly. \"You wanted to impress them. Gain a few favors. And you’ve got Type One, Type Two, and Type Three relic weapons hanging on your wall.\"","He glanced at the three swords on their display plaques, still rattling from the shockwave that had destroyed the desk.","\"So I’m sure you can afford one million credits. Transfer my money. Right now. This instant.\"","Marcus’s face turned even paler. The blue tint receded slightly as Dexter loosened his grip just enough to allow speech, but the terror in the man’s eyes only deepened.","He gritted his teeth. A flash of defiance, born from desperation rather than courage, crossed his features.","\"You have no idea who you’re dealing with,\" he hissed.","Dexter smiled wider.","\"You also have no idea who you’re dealing with.\"","His grip tightened.","Marcus’s face went from blue to a mottled red. Then green. Then a horrifying combination of both as the pressure on his throat increased. His eyes began to bulge. The veins on his forehead stood out like cables as his kicking became weaker, frantic and pathetic.","Dexter stared into his eyes.","And Marcus saw something there.","It was killing intent.","Pure, cold, absolute killing intent.","Marcus saw it, and he understood that the next five seconds would determine whether he lived or died.","\"Pl-ease!\" \"Waaaait!\"","He began to plead. Frantic, garbled sounds spilled from his lips.","But Dexter wasn’t listening anymore.","His eyes had flashed violet and then crimson as killkmgbjnegent began to rise.","Demonic essence surged through his DNA, flooding his muscles, his bones, his nervous system with power that was not entirely human.","The Asura Physique also stirred, wanting souls.","The two combined want enough to fully influence Dexter but it was enough for them to give him an idea which grew rapidly.","’Kill him.’","’Kill him and forget about the money. He insulted you, he stole from you and he deserves death. Take it.’","Dexter’s violet eyes narrowed and his grip on Marcus’s throat shifted, no longer a restraining hold but was tightening.","Marcus eyes went wide with terror and he opened his mouth to scream but he could not.","Dexter’s other hand began to rise, crimson flames flickering around his knuckles.","\"You can only blame me for what is about tot happen.\"","Dexter grinned as he tightened his hand and was ready for the kill when his Enhanced Hearing Talent suddenly heard something behind him.","The thing was fast to an almost impossible level as it closed in on him with speed that rivaled sound.","Dexter’s eyes snapped back to their natural color for a fraction of a second and his conscious mind, the part that was still Dexter Ashford and not the Flame Demon ascending through his bloodline, processed the information speed.","But as Dexter’s brain processed all this, he didn’t dodge in the slightest.","It wasn’t that he didn’t have time to dodge, it was that he chose especially at that moment not to dodge!"]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195 | Anger (2)","paragraphs":["Dexter didn’t dodge. Instead, he left his back vulnerable as the attack swooshed towards him.","At that moment, the black stud earring suddenly exploded outward from Dexter’s body, expanding to cover both him and Marcus in a transparent, dome-shaped barrier.","At that split second, a silver arc of sword energy collided with the barrier with a cataclysmic force.","\"DING!\"","A massive shockwave exploded out in an astonishing burst.","The entire office shook violently as glass shattered and every window in the room exploded!","Even the walls cracked and the ceiling panels also shattered to smithereens!","\"Crack!\"","The barrier had mutiple cracks on it but it actually didn’t explode.","Dexter slowly turned around.","Marcus still dangled from his left hand, choking and gasping and crying, barely able to speak but Dexter barely noticed as his entire attention was focused on the figure standing in the doorway of the office.","The person was a middle-aged who looked his fifties it maybe even older.","It was difficult to tell because his face carried the particular agelessness of a high-level her.","His hair was pure white, cropped short and swept back from a forehead. There was also a matching white beard covered his jaw which was trimmed neatly.","The man wore an expensive blue suit that proved he had money but the most astonishing part was that in his left hand was a long silver sword.","The man’s brow was furrowed slightly as his eyes stared at Dexter.","Dexter’s face turned serious as his gaze landed on him.","’Ultra Realm.’","He immediately knew the cultivation level of the man. The attack he had launched had been reduced to Peak Superhuman levels, thinking it was enough to deal with Dexter which was why he used the strength of a peak realm Super Human.","However, he had been very wrong. Nit only had Dexter survived, he had survived with indifference!","Dexter turned around and stared at the man with an expressionless gaze and then suddenly smirked.","\"You truly want him to die, don’t you?\"","The middle-aged man didn’t say anything as he moved his gaze from Dexter to Marcus, ehi was still dangling and choking from Dexter’s grip.","After a while, he suddenly spoke.","\"You do know, i possess the power to make you stay here forever if I wish.\"","His said in a casual tone as thought he wasn’t bothered that his employee was on the verge of death.","\"Even if I give you the one million back or even 100 million, I can make sure you never leave this building.\"","Dexter blinked at the man’s voice but then suddenly, he chuckled drily.","\"You can try,\"","Then he tilted his head, his violet-tinged eyes meeting the old man’s dark gaze.","\"But what do you think killing an Ashford son would do to your company? Most especially you...\"","Dexter’s grin widened as he said this.","Dexter Ashford was, by legal definition, the firstborn son of the Ashford family. Disowned or not, cast out or not.","He still bore the Ashford name.","Killing him would would definitely benefit the Ashford family but the Ashford family would definitely not let it down especially not in public.","The company would definitely die and so would he, like literally!","If it became known that a real estate company had murdered an Ashford son, even a disowned one, the political fallout would be significant.","The delicate web of business relationships that Harvest Homes depended on would be damaged.","The old man stared at Dexter for a long time.","Silence filled the ruined office.","\"What do you want?\" the old man asked.","Dexter chuckled.","\"I want my two million credits back.\" He paused. \"With interest.\"","He raised Marcus slightly, adjusting his grip.","Marcus’s eyes went wide. He tried to speak to explain that it wasn’t two million credits personally. But Dexter’s grip tightened, crushing the words back down his throat before they could form.","The old man glanced at Marcus. Then at Dexter.","Then he chuckled.","\"Even if I give you the two million,\" the old man said, \"do you think you would leave here intact?\"","He paused, letting the question settle.","\"Although I might not be able to kill you, the Ashford family won’t blame me if I cripple you. Disownment works both ways, boy. They discarded you. That means you have no protection.\"","His dark eyes narrowed.","\"Crippled and useless wives, crippled husband. Isn’t that fitting?\"","He smiled. It was not a kind smile.","\"A few people were quite jealous that you managed to snag three beauties. However, they are crippled and they are stupid. And now you will be crippled and useless along with them.\"","He tilted his head.","\"I know what the headlines will say tomorrow.\"","Dexter was silent.","His face turned blank and expressionless.","’Useless.’","’Crippled.’","’Stupid.’","’My wives.’","\"Bang!\"","Something broke inside him.","Something even Dexter didn’t understand.","The old man had insulted him. That was fine. Dexter had been insulted his entire life, a bastard and even a slave with an f rank talent.","He had heard every variation, every iteration, every creative combination of contempt that the human vocabulary could produce and he was alredy quite used to it.","But the old man had not stopped at insulting him, he had insulted his wives.","Mira who had sworn a Death God oath to honor any request Dexter made, Selene who had fallen asleep on his chest because she needed heat and Lyra who had kissed his cheek because he gave her chips.","’Useless.’","’Crippled.’","’Mute.’","’Blind.’","The words echoed in his mind, bouncing off the walls of his consciousness, growing louder and louder as time passed.","Dexter’s eyes changed drastically.","One moment they were their natural dark brown. The next moment, they were violet.","A strange pressure began to radiate from his body as the temperature in the office rose rapidly","Even the air shimmered as the dust motes suspended in the air began to glow faintly by the heat that was pouring from Dexter’s skin.","The old man’s expression changed.","\"What are you...\"","Dexter’s lips curled into a cold smile.","\"Flame Demon Transformation!\""]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196 | Enough!","paragraphs":["\"Flame Demon Transformation.\"","\"BOOM!!!\"","An enormous pillar of crimson flame erupted from Dexter’s body.","The flames surged upward, punching through the ceiling of the office, up into the office above.","Then the flames collapsed inward.","They wrapped around Dexter’s body, compressing, molding themselves to his form.","His hair lifted, floating upward as though suspended in zero gravity as they literally lit up with white, gold and violet flames.","The flames compressed in Dexter’s body as it formed demonic tattoos on his skin!","The visual manifestation of a bloodline that was older and more powerful than anything the old man had ever encountered.","His eyes burned with violent flames as the entire office trembled and shook from the raw power and sheer heat that Dexter was radiating T that moment.","The old man’s expression changed as he became serious.","He hadn’t expected this trouble maker who everyone knew has been useless to possess this sort of strength.","\"So you’ve been hiding your strength,\" he murmured.","Dexter didn’t answer but released his grip on Marcus.","The man dropped to the floor like a sack of wet sand.","\"K-off!\" \"Koff!!\"","He gasped, coughed, and tried to crawl away on his hands and knees.","Dexter didn’t look at him.","His burning gaze remained fixed on the old man.","Dexter lifted his leg up and stepped forward but as his feet landed on the ground—","\"BOOM!\"","The floor beneath his foot exploded. A spiderweb of fractures spread outward from the point of impact, reaching the walls in every direction.","The old man’s pupils contracted.","’That physical strength...’","Dexter smiled wider. The violet flames in his eyes flickered.","\"You said something interesting earlier,\" Dexter voice was thick and different. It sounded as though two of him was talking at the same time and not just one.","He took another step.","\"BOOM!\"","\"You said crippling me would be fitting.\"","Another step.","\"BOOM!\"","\"You also said my wives are useless.\"","The demonic patterns on his skin pulsed with light, darkening and spreading as the bloodline’s influence deepened.","\"You called them crippled.\"","The old man’s expression hardened. He raised his sword, the blade humming with gathered mana.","\"Don’t think that transformation is enough to...\"","\"WHOOSH!\"","Dexter vanished.","The air where he had been standing exploded outward in a shockwave of displaced atmosphere and superheated air.","The old man’s eyes widened.","’Fast!’","He swung his sword on pure instinct. A full-speed horizontal slash that drew a silver arc through the air with the speed of a lightning bolt.","\"CLANG!!!\"","Dexter’s fist collided with the edge of the blade.","As the shockwave tore through the office. What remained of the furniture was destroyed as the office cracked even more.","The old man’s arm trembled and he actually slid three meters backward as his feet carved trenches on the ground before he finally stopped.","His arm was trembled as the. The impact traveled from his sword to his entire body.","But Dexter hadn’t moved a single inche backward.","The old man’s expression changed.","’Impossible.’","’He’s not at the Ultra Realm. His cultivation is Superhuman. Tenth Stage at most. But his physical strength...’","’His physical strength is matching mine.’","’No. Exceeding mine.’","Dexter slowly raised his head. His violet eyes locked onto the old man’s dark gaze.","\"One thing you said was correct.\"","The heat around him intensified and the temperature in the room climbed past the point where ordinary materials could survive. The carpet smoldered. The remaining furniture began to char and even the air itself seemed to ignite.","\"My wives are crippled.\"","The old man’s lip curled. He opened his mouth to speak.","Dexter’s voice cut through the air like a blade.","\"But they are still my wives.\"","The violet light in his eyes flared.","\"And anyone who dares insult them...\"","His fist slowly clenched. The flames around it compressed, densified, concentrated into a point of light so intense it was painful to look at.","\"...will pay the price.\"","\"BOOM!!!\"","Dexter vanished again.","A crater appeared in the ground, surrounded by a ring of superheated debris that was already melting from the residual thermal energy.","The old man reacted on pure instinct. He raised his sword, channeled every ounce of his Ultra-Rank mana into the blade, and braced.","\"BANG!!!\"","Dexter’s fist smashed against the blade.","A massive shockwave exploded through the entire room.","The collision unleashed a shockwave not like a wave but a solid, visible wall of compressed air and mana. This sphere-shaped wall expanded outward, simultaneously hitting every surface in the office.","Windows shattered throughout this office and every other one on the floor. The hallway walls cracked and ceiling panels across the entire twenty-fourth floor disintegrated. Everything not bolted down – desks chairs computers filing cabinets – became projectiles.","The old man’s was blasted backwards as he slammed against the office wall!","His sword arm screamed with pain and the blade in his hand developed a visible fracture line.","He was barely able to land on his feet as he stared at Dexter with wide eyes.","Shock.","He looked at the man standing in front of him and he realized something.","The Ashford family was wrong. There was no way a useless person could climb realms to battle!","They were clearly lying to everyone again!","He had barely thoug he this when another fist flashed through the air.","He immediately tried to block it but he was too late.","\"Bang!\"","The fist struck the side of his mouth and he was sent flying with a black mark on his face.","He collided again with the wall, creating a dent in the wall as gravity let him down.","The old man touched his lips and saw blood on his palm.","His face changed as he looked down at his trembling sword arm.","Then he looked up at Dexter as his gaze turned cold.","\"Enough,\" he said.","As he said this, his body exploded instantly exploded with energy as he activated his own talent.","His body began to change as he also transformed.","The custom-fitted suit that had cost more than most people’s monthly rent ripped like tissue paper as his body expanded.","The white dress shirt beneath it followed. Then the undershirt. Then the skin itself seemed to shift, stretching, thickening, densifying."]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197 | Attack!","paragraphs":["The middle aged man’s body expanded outward in every direction simultaneously.","His shoulders broadened until they were wider than the doorway behind him. His chest deepened until it was deeper than Dexter’s entire torso. His arms thickened, the muscles swelling to proportions that no human skeleton should have been able to support, each one larger than Dexter’s waist.","Four meters.","The old man had been slightly under two meters tall. Now he was four. His head nearly touched the cracked ceiling of the ruined office.","His face had changed too. The aristocratic features, the neat white beard, all of it was gone","His jaw had extended, his brow had thickened and his teeth, visible behind lips that no longer closed properly, had become pronounced.","He looked down at Dexter.","Licked his lips.","His dark eyes burned with a violent, predatory hunger.","He chuckled.","\"Do you think you’re the only one hiding your strength?\"","Dexter’s violet eyes narrowed.","The transformed man’s power had exploded upward. Stage Two Ultra Realm had been his baseline. The transformation had pushed him past Stage Three. Past Stage Three’s peak. All the way to Stage Four Ultra Realm.","Stage Four Ultra Realm meant an additional two hundred attribute points across every stat compared to a Stage Two. Strength. Agility. Physique. Mana. All of them had surged far beyond anything Dexter’s Tenth Stage Superhuman cultivation could match through raw numbers alone.","Dexter’s gaze turned serious.","But he didn’t care.","He activated Flame Burst Step.","The air ignited.m as he vanished. A crater appeared in the floor where he had been standing, the marble vaporized by the force of his launch.","He materialized directly beside the transformed man.","He punched out once more.","Amplified by Scorching Fury, powered by every ounce of physical strength his Ancient Flame Demon Bloodline and Extreme Slaughtering Demon Body could produce.","The man reacted as he also punched out with his massive trunk-sized fist that moved with a speed that should have been impossible for something that large.","\"BOOM!\"","Their fists collided.","The shockwave was unlike anything the building had experienced so far. It didn’t just shatter windows or crack walls. It tore through the office like a bomb detonating.","The floor between them disintegrated. The ceiling above them collapsed inward, raining concrete and rebar. The entire corner of the twenty-fourth floor opened to the sky.","The transformed man turned his head slowly toward the point of impact to Dexter.","His massive lips curled.","\"As expected,\" he rumbled. \"You’re quite weak now, aren’t you?\"","Dexter said nothing but his arm trembled slightly.","But Dexter didn’t retreat.","He flipped his right hand.","The Void Star Saber materialized in his grip. The blade was dark.","The transformed man’s eyes tracked the weapon.","Then he vanished.","Dexter’s Enhanced Hearing screamed.","’Above!’","He swung upward. A desperate, full-power vertical slash that channeled every passive effect the Void Star Saber possessed.","DING!","The collision was sharp. Piercing. The sound of two relic-grade weapons meeting at maximum speed. A point of light appeared at the contact point, so bright it burned afterimages into the retina.","The transformed man had appeared directly above Dexter. Descending. His massive body casting a shadow that blocked the sunlight streaming through the destroyed ceiling. His sword, the same silver blade he had been carrying before the transformation but now enlarged to match his four-meter frame, was aimed straight down. A killing strike. Intended to split Dexter from crown to groin.","The Void Star Saber caught it.","The force of the impact drove Dexter downward. His feet punched through the marble floor. Then through the concrete beneath. He sank to his ankles, his knees absorbing the impact, his entire body compressing under the weight of a four-meter Ultra-Rank combatant bearing down from above.","The ground beneath him exploded. Cracked. Shattered. A crater formed, spreading outward, the floor giving way under the combined pressure of two fighters who had long since exceeded the structural capacity of the building.","Dexter didn’t care.","He countered.","His blade twisted, deflecting the massive sword to the side. He stepped forward, out of the crater, and slashed. A horizontal cut aimed at the transformed man’s midsection.","DING!","The man’s sword came down, blocking.","Dexter reversed the blade and slashed again.","DING!","It was once again blocked m.","Another slash!","DING!","Dexter pressed forward. His blade became a blur. Slash after slash after slash, each one flowing into the next without pause, without hesitation, without the briefest fraction of a second’s recovery between strikes.","The Void Star Saber’s Star Velocity passive increased his attack speed by thirty percent.","The Void Edge doubled his attack power. Armor Break ignored twenty percent of the man’s physical defense.","DING! DING! DING! DING! DING!","The collisions came so fast they merged into a continuous scream of metal against metal.","Sparks flew in every direction as white-hot fragments of displaced mana ignited the air, creating brief, violent flares of light that strobed across the ruined office like lightning.","The transformed man matched his every strik, deflecting each of Dexter’s strikes with accuracy.","The office was being destroyed around them.","The room was being dismantled. The walls were gone. The ceiling was gone. The floor was a landscape of craters and cracks. What had once been a corner office on the twenty-fourth floor of a luxury building was now an open-air platform, exposed to the sky and the wind and the distant sounds of the city below.","Marcus had been crawling toward the corner when the first shockwave hit.","He was no longer crawling on the ground but was flattened, pressed down against the floor by the combined atmospheric pressure of two fighters exchanging blows at a rate that turned the air itself into a weapon.","Marcus pressed his face against the floor, covered his head with his hands, and prayed to every deity he had ever heard of.","He was not a fighter and was just a businessman. He had never even been in a real fight in his life."]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198 | Ultimate Attacks","paragraphs":["\"BANG!\"","Shockwave exploded out as the two fighters separated, each launching backward to opposite ends of what remained of the office.","Dexter’s feet dug trenches in the cracked marble as he slid to a stop near the destroyed doorway.","The transformed middle-aged man landed on the far side, his massive four-meter frame cracking the floor beneath his weight","The office was mostly gone. The walls destroyed, revealing the entire office to the outside world.","The ground had several holes in them too","The middle aged man’s expression was grim as he stared down at Dexter.","\"I must admit,\" His voice rumbling like distant thunder. \"You are quite strong.\"","\"But I’ve been fighting way before your mother was even born,\" the man continued. His dark eyes narrowed. His grip on his enlarged silver sword shifted, the blade angling upward. \"Now, let me show you the power of a true Ultra Realm expert.\"","The moment he raised his sword the air immediately changed drastically.","The turbulent mana surging like a violent river from their battle suddenly inverted and began to spiral toward the raised blade like vacuum.","In that split second, darkness descended like nightfall.","The darkness swallowed every single light in ten surrounding as everything seem to vanish.","Dexter’s eyes narrowed as he watched the strange darkness consume the office.","\"Crimson Moon Slash.\"","As his voice landed, the darkness pulsed as something illuminated directly behind him!","The light surged and formed a crescent moon directly behind the man.","The crescent moon was large, about three meters tall as it cascaded crimson blood like rays of light to the enter office.","Suddenly, the man smirked as he slashed directly at Dexter.","In that split second, the crimson moon obeyed.","It suddenly moved as it slashed down at Dexter, spinning rapidly as it flew.","\"Whoosh!\"","The air screamed in its wake as a massive pressure surged directly at Dexter.","Dexter’s face turned grim.","The power behind this attack was on a completely different level from anything the man had demonstrated before.","Dexter raised his saber.","\"Don’t think you’re the only one with a technique,\" he muttered through gritted teeth.","He activated the first form of the Thunder God Saber Art.","God Slayer Flash.","Thunder crackled around Dexter’s body. Blue-white arcs of electricity exploded from his skin, dancing along his arms, his shoulders, his neck.","His hair lifted, standing on end, each strand crackling with electrical charge.","But that wasn’t all.","Dexter simultaneously activated his bloodline skill. Flame Slash.","Violet flames erupted from his blade, merging with the blue lightning.","Fire and lightning. Two of the most volatile, incompatible elemental forces in existence, brought together on the edge of a single weapon.","Previously, this combination wouldn’t have been possible. Thunder and flame repelled each other and attempting to merge them would have resulted in a violent reaction.","Before his flame evolved to become an heavenly flame!","The Void Star Saber erupted with a blinding cascade of crimson and blue. Fire and lightning wrapped around each other in a double helix of destructive energy, climbing the blade in spiraling tendrils that reached upward and outward, painting the darkness with streaks of violent color.","Dexter took a single step forward as he slashed out.","The two attacks collided and everywhere went silent for a moment.","\"KA-BOOOOOOOOM!!!\"","What happened was an event. A moment where the fabric of reality bent, warped, and briefly tore. The collision point between the crimson moon and the flame-thunder slash became a singularity of compressed energy so dense that the air around it turned to plasma.","Then it released.","BOOOOOOM!!!","A mushroom cloud of mixed energy exploded upward. Crimson and blue and white and black, all swirling together in a towering column that punched through the remains of the ceiling, through the floors above, through the roof of the building, and into the sky. The column rose hundreds of meters, visible from across the city like a beacon.","The shockwave that followed was total.","The next, every molecule of air in a fifty-meter radius was moving outward at supersonic speed.","The remaining walls of the office disintegrated. The concrete and steel and glass reduced to powder in an instant, the particles carried outward by the shockwave like sand in a hurricane.","The floor beneath them gave way entirely, replaced by a jagged hole that extended downward through multiple floors.","Marcus was hit.","The shockwave caught him as he lay flattened against the floor, already barely conscious, already broken from the earlier impacts.","The wall of compressed air struck his body with the force of a freight train. His mouth opened. Blood erupted from his lips in a thick, dark spray. His chest compressed. His ribs cracked. His internal organs shifted violently against each other.","He was a Superhuman Realm cultivator. His body was enhanced. Toughened. Reinforced by years of cultivation. An ordinary human would have been vaporized.","Marcus was merely almost killed.","Blood poured from his ears. His nose. His mouth. His eyes rolled upward, showing white. His body went limp, his mind shutting down to escape the pain. He lost consciousness immediately, his broken body slumping against the debris-covered floor like a discarded puppet.","Dexter was blasted backward.","The shockwave caught him and threw him like a leaf in a hurricane as he tumbled through the air, spinning, crashing through the remains of the office doorway, through the hallway wall, and into the corridor beyond.","He stood there and with The Void Star Saber still gripped in his right hand, its blade dimmed, the flame-thunder combination exhausted. His Flame Demon Possession had faded during the collision.","But he was alive.","The transformed man was instead blasted out of the building.","His massive four-meter frame was launched through the exterior wall, which no longer existed to stop him, and into the open air beyond. He tumbled through the sky, his enormous body rotating end over end, trailing debris and dust.","He fell twenty-four floors.","Glass, concrete fragments, steel rebar, office furniture, and pulverized drywall rained down around him, a cascade of debris that peppered the street below like hail.","He hit the ground.","CRACK!"]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199 | The Meeting","paragraphs":["The asphalt cratered beneath his impact. A shockwave rippled outward from the landing point, shattering the windows of parked cars and sending pedestrians staggering.","The man’s massive frame was driven into the street surface, his body creating a crater roughly two meters deep and five meters across.","He lay there. In the crater. In his four-meter form. His silver sword buried in the rubble beside him.","Then he moved.","He pushed himself up. His massive arms trembled. His transformed body, which had seemed so invincible moments ago, was battered. Bruised. Cracked in places where the shockwave had exceeded even his enhanced durability.","He stood and then Looked up.","At the twenty-fourth floor of the ruined building.","At Dexter.","Who was standing at the edge of the destroyed floor, looking down at him.","---","People were gathering.","Dozens of them. Pedestrians who had felt the shockwave, heard the explosions, seen the pillar of light, and come running. They stood at the edge of the crater, their phones raised, recording everything. Some were screaming. Some were crying. Most were simply staring with the wide-eyed, uncomprehending shock of ordinary people who had just witnessed something far beyond their understanding.","The transformed man’s massive form was impossible to miss. A four-meter tall, impossibly muscled, white-haired figure standing in a crater in the middle of the street. People immediately recognized him as they saw the power he was Radiating.","And he was looking up at a young man standing in the ruins of the twenty-fourth floor.","Dexter stared down at the old man.","His violet eyes had faded back to their natural brown.","Dexter wanted to go down there, tocontinue the fight. Wanted to finish what the old man had started. Wanted to make him bleed. To make him pay for every word.","But now was not the time.","The street was full of people, cameras were recording and the Hero Association would be responding within minutes.","The police were probably already on their way. Fighting an Ultra Realm expert in front of a crowd of civilians, in the middle of the central district, during broad daylight, would attract exactly the kind of attention he could not afford.","Not today.","Dexter turned away from the edge.","He walked back into the ruins of the office. His eyes scanned the debris. The desk was gone. The bookshelves were gone. The decorative items were shattered beyond recovery.","But Marcus was still there.","The man lay unconscious in a corner of what remained of the office. Blood had pooled beneath him and his breathing was shallow.","Dexter felt no sympathy for him in the slightest.","He walked over to Marcus’s unconscious body and knelt beside it and started to remove the man’s watch. A luxury timepiece. Mana-powered. Probably worth 100,000 dollars.","He removed the gold ring on Marcus’s right hand which seemed to Worth at least a hundred thousand.","He removed the bracelet on Marcus’s left wrist and was about to move when he noticed something in Marcus’s mouth.","A gold tooth.","Dexter reached down, pried Marcus’s jaw open with his thumb, and yanked.","The tooth came free with a faint resistance and a wet sound.","He held it up.","\"Gold! Nice!\"","Dexter pocketed it anyway.","Then he stood up and walked to the far wall, where the three sword plaques had fallen. The display mounts were broken, but the swords themselves were intact. Type One. Type Two. Type Three. Three relic weapons, undamaged by the battle.","He collected all three.","Seller’s remorse, Marcus?","He placed everything into his spatial storage.","He looked around the ruined office one last time. Scanned for anything else of value. Found nothing that had survived the destruction.","He nodded to himself. Satisfied.","Then he turned and walked out.","---","The elevator was still functional. Miraculously.","Dexter rode it down to the lobby. The doors opened. He stepped out.","The lobby was full of people. Receptionists behind the desk, security guards near the entrance, visitors who had been evacuated from the upper floors, all of them crowded into the ground floor space, staring upward through the skylights at the smoke and debris rising from the twenty-fourth floor.","Several bodyguards stood near the elevator bank. They were armed. Armored. Their postures were aggressive. Their faces were set with the determination of men who had been ordered to stop someone.","They saw Dexter step out of the elevator.","None of them moved.","They had seen what happened. Or heard about it. The security feeds, the frantic radio communications, the bodyguards who had been stationed on the twenty-fourth floor and had been found unconscious in the hallway. The four-meter transformation of their boss. The pillar of light that had blown through the roof.","And they had seen the old man. Their employer. Their leader. An Ultra Realm expert. Lying in a crater in the middle of the street.","Looking up at a young man who was now walking calmly through the lobby.","None of them were Ultra Realm. Most were Peak Superhuman at best. And they had just witnessed their Ultra Realm boss get thrown out of a building by the casually dressed young man now walking toward them.","They stepped aside.","Dexter walked through the lobby without looking at any of them. His pace was unhurried and his expression was neutral.","He pushed through the glass doors and stepped out into the sunlight.","The pillar of energy had dissipated, leaving only a thin trail of smoke rising from the damaged building.","A crowd had gathered behind police barricades that had been erected as Emergency vehicles were arriving.","And in the center of the crater, the transformed man had reverted to his human form. He was surrounded by emergency responders who were wisely keeping their distance.","He was staring at Dexter.","Their eyes met across the chaos of the street.","The old man’s expression was unreadable.","He was reassessing.","Dexter held his gaze for one second.","Then he turned away, walked to his SUV, opened the door, climbed in, and started the engine.","He pulled out of the parking garage. Merged onto the main road and then instantly drove out.","---","He was driving when his phone rang.","Dexter glanced at the screen. Cole.","’ Damn! I almost forgot.’","He answered.","\"Hey, Dexter. I don’t mean to disturb, but I just wanted to make sure you haven’t forgotten about the meeting we set up.\"","Dexter checked the time on his dashboard display.","12:30 PM.","He was thirty minutes late.","\"I apologize. I got held up by something but I’m on my way.\""]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200 | You Don’t Have To Carry It Alone","paragraphs":["Three years before the present.","The rooftop of the old Ashford servants’ quarters was a flat, tar-papered surface cluttered with ventilation ducts, rusted water tanks, and exposed pipes.","Nobody came up here and the door to the roof was supposed to be locked, but the lock had been broken for years, and nobody had bothered to fix it because nobody cared enough except for Dexter.","He had found this place when he was 12 and it had always been hiding spot.","The one place he could sit and not be seen by the servants and the family members who looked down on him.","He had also always celebrated his birthday here, alone since no one had remembered his birthday.","If wasn’t that he had expected them to anyways.","If he was remembered, he got extra chores instead, had to scrub floors until his knees arched, washed laundry and plates and even eaten leftovers in the corner of the servants’ hall, alone, while the other servants chatted and laughed around him.","He was used to it.","But this particular sunset was quite nice.","The sky above Stargate City was in shades of amber and rose and deep, burning gold. The towers of the central district caught the light and threw it back in blinding flashes.","Dexter sat on the concrete wall, his legs dangling over the edge.","He also wore a faded grey t-shirt that was slightly too large for his body. At this particular day, he was 16. But right now, he didn’t feel 16, but quite tired.","The rooftop door creaked and immediately, Dexter’s head turned.","A girl stepped through.","She was a slim, dark haired beautiful girl who looked 18 to 17.","Her hair was pulled back in a simple ponytail, and she wore a plain white blouse tucked in her dark skirt and carried a small cloth bundle in both hands,","That young woman was Jasmine Constance, the only person in the entire Ashford estate who had ever looked at Dexter and actually smart enough ot lucky enough tot have lived.","Others have died but Jasmine’s hero talent had rendered her invisible, so she couldn’t be seen with Dexter.","It wasn’t that there wasn’t people that cared for Dexter, it was that they hadn’t lived long enough.. they had all died mysteriously!","Dexter suspected it was his father and most likely Step mother Seraphina.","He had met Jasmine a year ago. Dexter had been carrying a stack of clean linens through the east corridor when he had rounded a corner and collided with Jasmine, who had been carrying a stack of documents in the opposite direction.","They had both knelt on the floor, gathering the scattered mess, apologizing simultaneously, and in the process of disentangling their respective stacks, Jasmine had looked up at him and said, \"You have really nice eyes.\"","The comment had so thoroughly short-circuited his brain that he had simply stared at her, stunned for ten full seconds before stammering \"thank you\" and fleeing down the corridor.","After that, they had kept running into each other. In the corridors. In the kitchen, in the garden. Each encounter was brief, giving each other a smile, greetings, comment about the weather or the food or the latest news from the Hero Association. Small moments that accumulated like snowflakes until they formed something solid between them.","Jasmine found the rooftop three weeks ago. Dexter hadn’t shown it to her. She had followed him.","She hadn’t asked why he hid not asked why he was alon, she had simply sat down beside him on the wall, dangled her legs over the edge, and watched the sunset in comfortable silence.","They had been coming here together ever since.","Jasmine walked the rooftop. She reached the wall, climbed up beside him, and sat.","She didn’t say anything immediately.","She just sat there, shoulder to shoulder with him as they both watched the sunset.","Then she held out the cloth bundle.","\"Happy birthday,\" she said.","Dexter stared at the bundle.","Then at her.","\"How did you know?\"","Jasmine shrugged with a smile on her lips.\"That’s for me to know.\"","She wiggled the bundle slightly. \"Open it.\"","Dexter took the bundle from her hands and he unfolded the cloth carefully.","Inside was a sweater, a clearly secondhand cloth that was worn but clean. The color was warm blue and the stitching was slightly uneven in places, suggesting it had been repaired by hand.","But it was warm, thick and soft against his fingers.","It was the nicest piece of clothing Dexter had ever owned.","His throat tightened.","\"You didn’t have to,\" he said quietly.","\"I know,\" Jasmine replied. \"That’s the point.\"","She bumped her shoulder against his. \"Try it on. I want to see if it fits.\"","Dexter pulled the sweater over his head. The fabric settled onto his shoulders with a soft, warm weight that immediately began to insulate his body heat. It fit. Not perfectly. The sleeves were slightly long, covering his hands to the first knuckle. But the shoulders were right, and the torso was snug without being tight.","He looked down at himself. At the blue fabric covering his arms and chest. At something that was his. Something that had been given to him not because it was owed, not because it was required, but because someone had wanted to.","\"It’s perfect,\" he said.","His voice cracked on the second word.","He looked away quickly, blinking hard, his jaw clenched against the pressure building behind his eyes.","Jasmine didn’t comment on the crack in his voice. She didn’t look at his face. She simply sat beside him, her shoulder pressed against his, and watched the sunset as though nothing had happened.","After a moment, she spoke.","\"Do you know what I thought the first time I saw you?\"","Dexter shook his head. His eyes were still fixed on the horizon, his jaw still tight.","\"I thought, ’That boy looks like he’s carrying the weight of the entire world on his shoulders,’\" Jasmine said. \"And then I thought, ’He’s carrying it alone.’\"","She paused.","\"You don’t have to carry it alone, Dexter.\"","The sunset painted her profile in shades of gold and rose."]}]);
